t/epic-fix-02.test.ts:431:    // m2 joins the cascade — its call summary clears and re-queues.\npackages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts:435:    expect(deleted.value.cleared.map(formKey)).toContain(\"message/m2/tool_call_summary\");\npackages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts:436:    expect(deleted.value.queued.map((q) => q.workItemId)).toContain(\"w-m2-tool_call_summary-v3\");\npackages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts:439:    // pair — its outcome reverts to unknown.\npackages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts:442:      (f) => f.subjectId === \"m2\" && f.form === \"tool_call_summary\",\npackages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts:445:    expect(callV3?.metadata?.outcome).toBe(\"unknown\");\npackages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts:452:describe(\"FIX-3.3: a claimed summary for a deleted message discards on completion\", () => {\npackages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts:465:    // Hold m2's tool_call_summary in flight: the drain claims it, the handler\npackages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts:467:    double.delayKind(\"tool_call_summary\", 400);\npackages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts:472:      \"m2's tool_call_summary to be claimed and in-handler\",\npackages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts:475:    // Delete m2 (the tool_call) while its summary item is claimed. Its own form\npackages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts:480:    expect(deleted.value.dropped.map(formKey)).toContain(\"message/m2/tool_call_summary\");\npackages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts:487:    const m2Item = drained.value.ran.find((r) => r.workItemId === \"w-m2-tool_call_summary-v1\");\npackages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts:490:    // Tombstone intact: m2 is gone from the live read and its summary form was\npackages/lhc/src/cli/render.ts:9:// Adapter-level failures (unknown command, missing command) happen before any\npackages/lhc/src/cli/render.ts:12:export type CliErrorCode = \"unknown_command\" | \"missing_flag\" | \"unknown_flag\";\npackages/lhc/src/cli/render.ts:14:export function renderResult(result: OpResult<unknown>): CliResult {\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:13:Epics 01 and 02 built the thread record and its derivation pipeline. Events stream in and project to messages and turns; derivation work runs in the background and lands summarized forms: smoothed prompts, tool-call and tool-result summaries, composed turn renderings, lower-band projections, and chunk summaries in two fidelities. All of that is material. None of it is what a model sees.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:17:Two cost realities shape everything here. First, the pull sits on the hot path between a user's action and a model call, so it must be reads and deterministic assembly only — derivation already happened, in Epic 02, off this path. Second, harnesses cache the prompt prefix; every byte that changes above the newest content costs real money. The MVP's per-turn tool-result truncation churned the cache every turn. This design changes the prompt only in planned, batched steps: a compact (rare, explicit), or a tool-result visibility advance (only under budget pressure).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:105:- **TC-1.2** (AC-1.7, AC-1.1): Pull twice with nothing between → byte-identical results; assert no work rows created, no provider double calls recorded (provider fake observes zero calls).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:106:- **TC-1.3** (AC-1.4): Compact, pull, then edit a message whose chunk summary landed in a band; pull again → band bytes unchanged; drain; pull again → still unchanged (rebuilt summary lands in record only).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:120:- **AC-2.3**: Invalid configuration (band percentages not summing to 100, unknown profile, non-positive bound) is rejected with a caller error naming the violation; thread state is unchanged.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:131:- **TC-2.1** (AC-2.2, AC-2.3, AC-2.7): Compact with a built-in profile → succeeds with that profile's bound and mix recorded in the receipt; compact with percentages summing to 105 → caller error naming the sum; unknown profile → caller error naming it; thread unchanged after both rejections.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:132:- **TC-2.2** (AC-2.4, AC-2.9): On a thread with full derivation coverage, compact → view targets the bound (receipt's actual counts within whole-entry tolerance of band shares, deviations attributable to whole-entry inclusion rules), provider fake observes zero calls during the compact; read the record after → identical to before.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:133:- **TC-2.3** (AC-2.5, AC-2.7): On a thread with one failed chunk summary and one pending turn rendering, compact → completes; degraded entries render fallbacks and are marked; receipt lists both with reasons and reports per-band counts; no span silently absent (every turn/chunk in the compacted range accounted for in some form).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:159:- **TC-3.1** (AC-3.1, AC-3.2, AC-3.3): Seed a thread with ready, pending, transiently-failed, non-transiently-failed, and blocked forms (fixture-manufactured states); sweep → returns immediately; transient failure requeued (work row exists, form pending), non-transient and blocked untouched and reported, pending untouched; provider fake observes zero calls from the sweep itself.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:168:The rule set, complete: tool results at-or-behind the boundary render short (Epic 02's summary when usable, deterministic truncation otherwise); tool results ahead of it render full; nothing else is ever affected — prompts, assistant text, and thinking always render full. After an intake batch commits, the advance check runs as a thread-view maintenance step, triggered through the SDK's post-commit seam (Epic 02's onCommit pattern) — automatic, never a host-remembered call, and outside the intake transaction, so intake's outcome never depends on it. One indexed sum measures the full-zone tool tokens; if it exceeds the max budget, the boundary advances oldest-first until the zone is at-or-under the target budget; otherwise nothing happens. A failed advance leaves the boundary unchanged and the over-budget condition visible in the status read; the next batch's check re-evaluates the same condition, so the debt is bounded by one batch. The boundary never advances into the protected floor — the most recent stretch of tool output stays full even mid-monster-turn — and never moves backward: a flipped result stays flipped. A compact resets the boundary to the compact point, because the old tail just became bands.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:187:- **TC-4.2** (AC-4.1, AC-4.2): With flipped results: one with a usable summary renders the summary; one with a failed summary renders deterministic truncation with the marker; an interleaved assistant message renders full.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:245:- **No inference in this epic:** pull, compact, sweep, materialize, boundary advance — no Epic 03 operation invokes a provider. Tests observe zero provider calls from these operations; test setups may drain Epic 02 work (which exercises the provider fake) to reach the states under test.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:253:2. Per-band degrade ladders: exact fallback order per band kind (e.g. brief entry falls back to detailed summary? smoothed turn falls back to raw-composed rendering?). The epic pins degrade-visibly-never-omit; the ladder is design.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:287:**Boundary / risk notes:** proves the hot path before any view machinery exists; the array shape pinned here is the contract Stories 2–5 render into.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:295:**Scope out:** the sweep (compact ships with the sweep step absent — Story 3 adds it; same pattern as Epic 01's Story 4→5 queue seam, stated so nobody reads the gap as a shim).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:311:**Boundary / risk notes:** the classification table (which Epic 02 reason codes count as transient) is tech-design output consumed here; TC-3.4's heal leg drains Epic 02 work via the provider fake — the one place a test setup exercises inference machinery.\npackages/lhc/test/cli-process-fix.test.ts:28:  it(\"NB-2: an unknown flag exits 1 and is named back to the caller\", () => {\npackages/lhc/test/cli-process-fix.test.ts:47:      expect(parsed.error.code).toBe(\"unknown_flag\");\npackages/lhc/src/cli/work.ts:61:// parity). Form names pass through as given; an unknown form is refused by\npackages/lhc/test/work-queue.test.ts:63:// proof of durability (anti-shim requirement).\npackages/lhc/test/work-queue.test.ts:112:      workItemId: \"w-m2-tool_result_summary-v1\",\npackages/lhc/test/work-queue.test.ts:114:      kind: \"tool_result_summary\",\npackages/lhc/test/work-queue.test.ts:130:        workItemId: \"w-m2-tool_result_summary-v1\",\npackages/lhc/test/work-queue.test.ts:132:        kind: \"tool_result_summary\",\npackages/lhc/test/work-queue.test.ts:146:  // the kind gate now also queues tool_call → tool_call_summary; the inert\npackages/lhc/test/work-queue.test.ts:297:    // 3 message items since Epic 02 Story 2: tool_call queues its summary\npackages/lhc/test/work-queue.test.ts:309:        .all() as unknown as Array<{ work_item_id: string; status: string }>;\npackages/lhc/test/work-queue.test.ts:312:        { work_item_id: \"w-m2-tool_call_summary-v1\", status: \"queued\" },\npackages/lhc/test/work-queue.test.ts:313:        { work_item_id: \"w-m3-tool_result_summary-v1\", status: \"queued\" },\npackages/l