 deterministic truncation rung — fixed 200-char\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:228:    // r2: usable summary ⇒ the summary verbatim.\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:385:    // The Story-0 facility's named post-commit point — not a mock of\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:418:      expect(m.forms?.find((f) => f.form === \"tool_result_summary\")?.state).toBe(\"ready\");\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/02-smart-compact.md:22:**Scope out:** the sweep — compact ships with the sweep step absent; the receipt's sweep section reports `absent`. Story 3 adds the embedded sweep and flips the receipt to `SweepReceipt | { skipped: true }`. Same pattern as Epic 01's Story 4→5 queue seam: the gap is a stated cross-story debt, not a shim — nothing fakes a sweep, nothing stubs one.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/02-smart-compact.md:31:- **AC-2.3**: Invalid configuration (band percentages not summing to 100, unknown profile, non-positive bound) is rejected with a caller error naming the violation; thread state is unchanged.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/02-smart-compact.md:32:  - **TC-2.1** (AC-2.2, AC-2.3, AC-2.7): Compact with a built-in profile → succeeds with that profile's bound and mix recorded in the receipt; compact with percentages summing to 105 → caller error naming the sum; unknown profile → caller error naming it; thread unchanged after both rejections.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/02-smart-compact.md:34:  - **TC-2.2** (AC-2.4, AC-2.9): On a thread with full derivation coverage, compact → view targets the bound (receipt's actual counts within whole-entry tolerance of band shares, deviations attributable to whole-entry inclusion rules), provider fake observes zero calls during the compact; read the record after → identical to before.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/02-smart-compact.md:36:  - **TC-2.3** (AC-2.5, AC-2.7): On a thread with one failed chunk summary and one pending turn rendering, compact → completes; degraded entries render fallbacks and are marked; receipt lists both with reasons and reports per-band counts; no span silently absent (every turn/chunk in the compacted range accounted for in some form).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/02-smart-compact.md:45:  - **TC-1.3** (AC-1.4): Compact, pull, then edit a message whose chunk summary landed in a band; pull again → band bytes unchanged; drain; pull again → still unchanged (rebuilt summary lands in record only).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/02-smart-compact.md:55:The view comes into existence here. Compact is the only writer of the snapshot (`thread_view` + `thread_view_band`, singleton, delete-then-insert in one transaction) and one of exactly two writers of the boundary (reset; the other writer is Story 4's advance). Pull — Story 1's code, unmodified in shape — starts serving snapshot + tail the moment a view row exists. The sweep step is **absent** this story: the receipt's `sweep` field reports a literal `absent` placeholder, and Story 3 replaces it with `SweepReceipt | { skipped: true }`.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/02-smart-compact.md:88:| TC-2.1 | `test/view-compact.test.ts` | profile compact: receipt config matches; 105% sum → named error; unknown profile → named error; thread unchanged after rejections (read-back equality) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/02-smart-compact.md:90:| TC-2.3 | `view-compact.test.ts` | failed chunk summary + pending rendering → ladder fallbacks marked degraded; receipt lists both with reasons + per-band counts; every subject represented |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/02-smart-compact.md:116:The sweep-absent receipt must be the honest literal (`sweep: \"absent\"` placeholder shape per Story 3's flip note) — not a fake empty `SweepReceipt`, which would make TC-3.4's Story 3 diff invisible. Goldens are immutable once committed: an implementation that disagrees with a golden is wrong until the *design rule* is shown wrong (deviation process, not golden edit). Degrade ladders must consume real fixture states — no test may flip a form's state by writing `derived_form` directly.\npackages/lhc/test/view-pull.test.ts:53:function sha256(value: unknown): string {\npackages/lhc/test/view-pull.test.ts:72:function stateSnapshot(filePath: string): Record<string, unknown> {\npackages/lhc/test/view-pull.test.ts:79:          .all() as unknown as Array<{ work_item_id: string; status: string; attempts: number | bigint }>\npackages/lhc/test/view-pull.test.ts:100:// the operation). No stubbed op remains on this surface.\npackages/lhc/test/view-pull.test.ts:259:  it(\"renders the ready summary behind the boundary and full content ahead of it\", async () => {\npackages/lhc/test/view-pull.test.ts:293:      (form) => form.form === \"tool_result_summary\" && form.state === \"ready\",\npackages/lhc/test/view-pull.test.ts:308:    // Behind: short form — the ready summary verbatim, abridged marker,\npackages/lhc/test/view-pull.test.ts:324:  it(\"falls to deterministic truncation when no summary is ready and the content is oversized\", async () => {\npackages/lhc/test/view-pull.test.ts:338:    // No drain: the summary stays pending, so the ladder's truncation rung\npackages/lhc/test/view-pull.test.ts:422:    // production terminal path (turn_rendering + lower_band_projection).\npackages/lhc/test/view-pull.test.ts:499:    // unchanged; the provider fake observed zero calls.\npackages/lhc/src/shared/derivation.ts:13:  | \"tool_call_summary\"\npackages/lhc/src/shared/derivation.ts:14:  | \"tool_result_summary\"\npackages/lhc/src/shared/derivation.ts:16:  | \"lower_band_projection\"\npackages/lhc/src/shared/derivati