rt-compact/stories/01-pull-and-status.md:15:- `thread-view` surface skeleton (structured-result stubs per tech design §Interface Definitions) with `pull` and `status` implemented\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/01-pull-and-status.md:27:  - **TC-1.2** (AC-1.1, AC-1.7): Pull twice with nothing between → byte-identical results; assert no work rows created, no provider double calls recorded (provider fake observes zero calls).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/01-pull-and-status.md:42:First story on the surface: `thread-view/index.ts` is born here with all five operations as structured-result stubs, two of which (`pull`, `status`) go real. The pull this story builds is the *tail-only* path — no view row exists yet, so `snapshot.ts` reads return absent and the whole record renders as tail from event 1. The array shape and tail mapping pinned here are load-bearing for every later story: Story 2 prepends band messages to this exact shape, Story 4 changes which results render short, Story 5 maps it to JSONL.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/01-pull-and-status.md:46:Types first (`shared/view.ts` landed in Story 0 — consume, don't redefine), then the surface skeleton with all five stubs (Red asserts each returns `{ ok: false, reason: \"not implemented: <op>\" }`), then Green: `render.ts` tail formatting kind-by-kind against the mapping table, then `pull` assembly, then `status`. The mapping table is seven rows — implement and test them as seven legs, not one blob assertion, so a single kind's drift fails one named test.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/01-pull-and-status.md:52:| `src/domains/thread-view/index.ts` | surface skeleton (5 ops, structured-result stubs); `pull` + `status` real |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/01-pull-and-status.md:53:| `src/domains/thread-view/internal/render.ts` | tail formatting: the 7-kind mapping table, short/full tool-result selection by boundary position, short-form ladder (summary → deterministic truncation) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/01-pull-and-status.md:62:| Surface signatures, stub contract | tech-design.md L342–352 |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/01-pull-and-status.md:74:| TC-1.2 | `view-pull.test.ts` | two pulls, nothing between: byte-identical; zero work rows; provider fake count unchanged |\npackages/lhc/src/shared/view.ts:19:// construction (FC-0.2's unknown-override violation).\npackages/lhc/src/shared/view.ts:75://   | tool_result (at-or-behind boundary)| user      | `[tool result · <name> · abridged]\\n<summary or deterministic truncation>` (short-form ladder) |\npackages/lhc/src/shared/view.ts:125:  // \"absent\" placeholder).\npackages/lhc/test/threads.test.ts:28:      .get() as unknown as MetadataRow;\npackages/lhc/test/threads.test.ts:41:      .all() as unknown as RegistryRow[];\npackages/lhc/test/threads.test.ts:110:  it(\"TC-1.3: resolve known id returns path and metadata; unknown id fails thread_not_found\", async () => {\npackages/lhc/test/threads.test.ts:131:    const unknown = await threads.resolve({\npackages/lhc/test/threads.test.ts:135:    expect(unknown.ok).toBe(false);\npackages/lhc/test/threads.test.ts:136:    if (unknown.ok) return;\npackages/lhc/test/threads.test.ts:137:    expect(unknown.error.code).toBe(\"thread_not_found\");\npackages/lhc/test/threads.test.ts:138:    expect(unknown.error.errorClass).toBe(\"caller_error\");\npackages/lhc/test/threads.test.ts:232:    const unknown = await threads.resolveThreadRef({\npackages/lhc/test/threads.test.ts:233:      threadId: \"th_unknown\",\npackages/lhc/test/threads.test.ts:236:    expect(unknown.ok).toBe(false);\npackages/lhc/test/threads.test.ts:237:    if (unknown.ok) return;\npackages/lhc/test/threads.test.ts:238:    expect(unknown.error.code).toBe(\"thread_not_found\");\npackages/lhc/test/threads.test.ts:299:  it(\"TC-1.3 (CLI): resolve known id round-trips; unknown id exits 1 with thread_not_found\", async () => {\npackages/lhc/test/threads.test.ts:327:    const unknown = await runCli([\npackages/lhc/test/threads.test.ts:335:    expect(unknown.exitCode).toBe(1);\npackages/lhc/test/threads.test.ts:336:    const unknownParsed = parseStdout<never>(unknown.stdout);\npackages/lhc/test/threads.test.ts:337:    expect(unknownParsed.ok).toBe(false);\npackages/lhc/test/threads.test.ts:338:    if (unknownParsed.ok) return;\npackages/lhc/test/threads.test.ts:339:    expect(unknownParsed.error.code).toBe(\"thread_not_found\");\npackages/lhc/test/threads.test.ts:367:    const emptyParsed = parseStdout<unknown[]>(empty.stdout);\npackages/lhc/src/shared/context.ts:71:// directly, and the single-background \"production path\" where a top-level\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/05-render-targets.md:20:**Scope out:** non-PI formats (`--format` accepts `pi-session` only; unknown → caller error); any view or state mutation from materialize or any CLI read path.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/05-render-targets.md:47:Format fixture first — capture a real PI session file, trim to structure, commit with provenance note — because TC-5.5 is unwritable without it and it may surface format surprises that reshape `materialize.ts`. Then materialize over pull output (pure mapping + file write), then `cli/view.ts` command-by-command, then the process suite. Red: `materialize` stub; CLI commands exit nonzero with structured not-implemented.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/05-render-targets.md:94:Deterministic `id`s: the header id derives from thread id + view createdAt; message entry ids from message ids; a never-compacted thread's header uses the thread's created-at (viewId null — `ViewMeta` carries both nullables). Byte-identical repeats are the test for any sneaky `Date.now()`/random — hash the whole file. CLI band-override flags merge field-wise over the profile *before* validation, so `--full 40` on a 30/30/20/20 profile fails the sum check with the named violation — that's correct behavior, not a bug to smooth over. The `--format` flag accepts only `pi-session`; unknown → `caller_error` naming accepted values.\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:2:// handlers (prompt smoothing, tool-call summary, tool-result summary) through\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:133:describe(\"TC-2.2 / AC-2.2: tool_call queues its summary additively; intake returns before any handler runs\", () => {\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:134:  it(\"the batch reports the queued item with the capture log still empty; the drained summary names tool and args\", async () => {\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:147:        workItemId: \"w-m1-tool_call_summary-v1\",\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:149:        kind: \"tool_call_summary\",\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:157:        workItemId: \"w-m1-tool_call_summary-v1\",\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:161:    const form = formOf(filePath, \"m1\", \"tool_call_summary\");\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:166:    // No paired result intaken: outcome stamped unknown, in metadata.\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:167:    expect(form?.metadata).toEqual({ outcome: \"unknown\" });\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:171:describe(\"TC-2.3 / AC-2.3: the result summary abbreviates; the full content stays byte-identical in the record\", () => {\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:172:  it(\"a 300KB result drains to a bounded summary and reads back whole through the Epic 01 surface\", async () => {\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:179:    const summary = formOf(filePath, \"m3\", \"tool_result_summary\");\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:180:    expect(summary?.state).toBe(\"ready\");\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:181:    expect(summary?.content?.startsWith(\"toolresult(\")).toBe(true);\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:183:    expect(summary?.content?.length ?? 0).toBeLessThan(100);\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:184:    expect(summary?.metadata).toEqual({ outcome: \"succeeded\" });\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:195:  it(\"three variants with identical provider text land succeeded / failed / unknown from metadata alone\", async () => {\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:218:      formOf(filePath, \"m2\", \"tool_call_summary\"),\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:232:      \"unknown\",\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:238:  it(\"the captured tool-call summary input is exactly the call plus its paired result\", async () => {\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:316:describe(\"TC-2.8 / AC-2.8 (architecture risk): a late result re-queues an unknown-outcome summary at intake\", () => {\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:317:  it(\"split batches: the result's intake re-queues the summary; the repair is a real queue round-trip\", async () => {\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:322:    // Batch 1: the call alone. Its summary derives with no pair in sight.\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:325:    const before = formOf(filePath, \"m1\", \"tool_call_summary\");\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:327:    expect(before?.metadata).toEqual({ outcome: \"unknown\" });\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:331:    // reports the re-queued summary — repair is intake-time and visible,\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:335:      workItemId: \"w-m2-tool_result_summary-v1\",\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:337:      kind: \"tool_result_summary\",\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:341:      workItemId: \"w-m1-tool_call_summary-v2\",\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:343:      kind: \"tool_call_summary\",\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:347:    const cleared = formOf(filePath, \"m1\", \"tool_call_summary\");\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:353:      [\"w-m2-tool_result_summary-v1\", \"done\"],\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:354:      [\"w-m1-tool_call_summary-v2\", \"done\"],\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:357:    // One summary form, outcome repaired, source version advanced — the\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:360:      (f) => f.form === \"tool_call_summary\",\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:372:  it(\"control: call and result in one batch never trigger the re-queue; the summary runs exactly once\", async () => {\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:382:    const summaryItems = batch.queuedWork.filter((item) => item.kind === \"tool_call_summary\");\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:383:    expect(summaryItems.map((item) => item.workItemId)).toEqual([\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:384:      \"w-m1-tool_call_summary-v1\",\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:388:    // The capture log proves the summary ran once — after both halves of its\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:391:    const form = formOf(filePath, \"m1\", \"tool_call_summary\");\npackages/lhc/src/shared/storage.ts:19:// tables, and the projection-level delete stamps. The whole epic's schema\npackages/lhc/src/shared/storage.ts:38:  // call id — never a block scan (anti-shim requirement).\npackages/lhc/src/shared/storage.ts:66:  // projection-level delete (the record keeps everything; reads filter)\npackages/lhc/src/shared/storage.ts:75:    SELECT 'message', json_extract(source_ref, '$.messageId'), 'tool_result_summary', 'pending', 1\npackages/lhc/src/shared/storage.ts:76:    FROM work_item WHERE status = 'queued' AND kind = 'tool_result_summary';`,\npackages/lhc/src/shared/storage.ts:81:    SELECT 'turn', json_extract(source_ref, '$.turnId'), 'lower_band_projection', 'pending', 1\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/03-readiness-sweep.md:22:**Dependencies:** Stories 0–2. **Hard gate, verify before story start (extended per design):** (1) Epic 02's requeue patch landed — live-work-only queue rows, no terminal-row collision; (2) the terminal-failure write path verified against landed code — exhausted forms persist a classifiable reason class (FC-0.4 proved the fixture side; this gate proves the production side). If the persisted reason is opaque, the named Epic 02 patch is: stamp the provider's `retryable` flag onto the failed form at exhaustion.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/03-readiness-sweep.md:30:  - **TC-3.1** (AC-3.1, AC-3.2, AC-3.3): Seed a thread with ready, pending, transiently-failed, non-transiently-failed, and blocked forms (fixture-manufactured states); sweep → returns immediately; transient failure requeued (work row exists, form pending), non-transient and blocked untouched and reported, pending untouched; provider fake observes zero calls from the sweep itself.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/03-readiness-sweep.md:37:  - **TC-3.4** (AC-3.6, AC-2.7): Compact with default options → receipt includes sweep section; compact with skip → receipt records the skip and no requeues occurred; drain after the default compact → requeued form heals; next compact's view includes the healed form. *(The drain leg exercises Epic 02 machinery through the provider fake — the one sanctioned test-setup use of inference machinery; no Epic 03 operation touches it.)*\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/03-readiness-sweep.md:44:The sweep is thread-view's only *writing* interaction with other domains, and it writes nothing itself — every mutation goes through `messages.requeue`/`turns.requeue`. It is the repair half of the degrade-don't-block posture: compact degrades around missing material; the sweep is why the same material isn't missing at the *next* compact. This story also completes the compact receipt: Story 2's `absent` placeholder becomes `SweepReceipt | { skipped: true }`.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/03-readiness-sweep.md:48:Gate first — both legs verified and recorded in the story log before any code (requeue patch landed; reason-class persistence verified against landed Epic 02 code, with FC-0.4 as the fixture-side proof). Then the classification table as data with its own unit legs, then the walk/bucket/receipt as a pure function over report outputs, then the requeue calls, then the compact embed + skip flag. Red: `sweep` stub + compact receipt still `absent`.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/03-readiness-sweep.md:82:Zero-provider assertion completes here across all five ops (the fake is in fixture scope all around the sweep — this assert is what keeps it out of the operation). Once-per-invocation dedupe is structural (owner noop) but asserted anyway — if Epic 02's requeue ever stops nooping, this is the test that notices.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/03-readiness-sweep.md:86:Buckets come from the *owners' report joins*, not raw form states: \"retrying\" is a report-level distinction (pending + queue detail), and the sweep must not re-derive it from `derived_form` reads. The receipt's `requeued` carries subject ids so TC-3.4 can follow specific forms through heal. The classification table starts minimal (the design's named classes); unknown codes landing in `permanentFailed` with their literal reason is the receipt's visibility mechanism — expanding the table is config-tier work later, not a redesign.\npackages/lhc/src/shared/errors.ts:17:  | \"unknown_work_kind\" // state_corruption — unregistered kind at dispatch\npackages/lhc/src/shared/errors.ts:21:  // Epic 03 (tech design §Interface Definitions): the surface-skeleton stub\npackages/lhc/src/shared/errors.ts:27:  | \"unknown_profile\" // caller_error — named profile not configured\npackages/lhc/src/shared/errors.ts:29:  // Epic 03 Story 5: materialize accepts pi-session only; an unknown format\npackages/lhc/src/shared/errors.ts:31:  | \"unknown_format\"; // caller_error — materialize format not supported\npackages/lhc/test/goldens/g2-edge-inclusion.json:8:    { \"band\": \"detailed\", \"subjectKind\": \"chunk\", \"subjectId\": \"c1\", \"formUsed\": \"chunk_summary_detailed\", \"degraded\": false },\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/00-foundation.md:31:- **FC-0.2**: Invalid profile configs are rejected at SDK construction with errors naming the violation (band sum ≠ 100, `max ≤ target`, `target < floor`, non-positive lower bound, unknown built-in override target).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/00-foundation.md:74:| FC-0.2 | `view-fixture.test.ts` | each invalid config rejected at construction with the named violation (sum≠100, max≤target, target<floor, bound≤0, unknown override) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/00-foundation.md:86:The fixture conversation shape is pinned in the design (~12 turns, 4 chunks, tool-heavy middle): the tool-heavy middle is what gives Story 4 a realistic over-max zone, and the 4 chunks give Story 2's coverage edge something to exclude. Scripted provider failures manufacture the failed states (retryable-fail-exhaust for transient; non-retryable for permanent); blocked comes from source damage on a sacrificial sibling fixture, not the main one. FC-0.4 is the Story 3 gate's fixture-side proof — if it can't pass because Epic 02's persisted reason is opaque, stop and surface it immediately; that's the named Epic 02 patch trigger, not something to work around.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/00-foundation.md:90:Fixture states must be reached through real `intake → drain` paths against the deterministic provider. Hand-writing `derived_form` rows to fake a state is the exact fiction FC-0.3 exists to prevent — a hand-written row can encode a state shape the production writer never produces, and every downstream test would then prove compatibility with fiction. The boundary-seed helper is the one sanctioned below-SDK write, and only because boundary *mechanics* are Story 4's to prove.\npackages/lhc/test/goldens/g4-turnless-straggler.json:8:    { \"band\": \"brief\", \"subjectKind\": \"chunk\", \"subjectId\": \"c1\", \"formUsed\": \"chunk_summary_brief\", \"degraded\": false },\npackages/lhc/test/goldens/g4-turnless-straggler.json:9:    { \"band\": \"detailed\", \"subjectKind\": \"chunk\", \"subjectId\": \"c2\", \"formUsed\": \"chunk_summary_detailed\", \"degraded\": false },\npackages/lhc/src/providers/deterministic.ts:30:  projectLowerBand: \"projection\",\npackages/lhc/src/providers/deterministic.ts:37:export function deterministicDigest(input: unknown): string {\npackages/lhc/src/providers/deterministic.ts:49:  input: unknown,\npackages/lhc/src/providers/deterministic.ts:55:function ok(op: DeterministicOpName, input: unknown, text: string): Promise<ProviderResult> {\npackages/lhc/src/providers/deterministic.ts:59:// The chunk-summary contract made visible in deterministic output (AC-3.8):\npackages/lhc/src/providers/deterministic.ts:60:// the detailed summary's artifact carries the members' tool-run receipts —\npackages/lhc/src/providers/deterministic.ts:61:// account and outcome — verbatim; the brief summary's carries outcomes\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:13:Two cost structures dominate the design, and they pull in the same direction: do nothing per-turn. The pull sits on the hot path between the user's action and the model call, so it must be reads and string assembly — every judgment (which chunk in which band, which tool result short) was made earlier by an explicit operation. And the harness caches its prompt prefix; every byte that changes above the newest content is money. The MVP's tool-result truncation re-decided every result's visibility on every message — the prefix churned every turn, which at Opus-class pricing is roughly $0.15 per turn, forever. The replacement design changes the prompt only at discrete, attributable events: a compact (explicit, rare), or a boundary advance (batched, budget-triggered). Between those events, identical pulls return identical bytes.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:15:The view is a snapshot, not a projection-on-read. A compact selects the band arrangement, renders each band's text from stored artifacts, and stores the rendered snapshot; pulls serve those bytes verbatim until the next compact. Record mutations and repairs land in the record immediately and become visible at the next compact — this was settled deliberately in the epic round (edit-then-recompact, no live view patching, no force-refresh) because curation is an occasional batch act, not a runtime channel. The one self-acting piece is the boundary: old tool results in the tail age to short form in batches when a budget breaks, because tool bloat accumulates without anyone deciding it.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:25:| Transient classification basis | AC-3.3, epic TD-Q9 | By **reason-code classification table** (per TD-Q9), owned by `sweep.ts`: rate-limit / timeout / provider-unavailable classes ⇒ transient; content-refusal / validation / `unknown_work_kind` ⇒ permanent; **unclassified codes ⇒ permanent** (reported in the receipt as unclassified, never requeued — the conservative default; the other way re-spends on a permanent failure at every compact). Attempt count distinguishes only retrying-vs-exhausted, never repairability. Dependency: exhausted forms must persist the final failure's reason class, not a bare retry-exhausted marker — the Story 0 fixture proves the two failed states carry distinguishable codes; if Epic 02's persisted reason is opaque, that is an Epic 02 patch named at the Story 3 gate. | Resolved — clarified |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:28:| Band context messages need a role | AC-5.1 | Rendered as `user`-role messages with band-marker headers. Provider APIs reject unknown roles; `system` placement is harness-owned; `user` is what the MVP's injection used and what PI session files accept anywhere. | Resolved — clarified |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:63:**Error contract** (inherited vocabulary, no new classes): `caller_error` (bad profile, bad budgets, unknown thread), `state_corruption` (canonical span unreadable at compact — AC-2.5), `system_error` (storage failures). All operations return `OpResult`; programmer errors at construction throw (Epic 02 rule).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:180:3. **Detailed band:** chunks entirely older than the smooth band's coverage, newest-first, same fill rule against `L × detailed%`, using `chunk_summary_detailed` counts.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:195:| Smooth (turn) | `turn_rendering` | `lower_band_projection` | deterministic excerpt of the turn's messages (truncated, marked) | `[turn t12 unavailable: <reason>]` |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:196:| Detailed (chunk) | `chunk_summary_detailed` | `chunk_summary_brief` | concatenated member projections (truncated, marked) | `[chunk c4 unavailable: <reason>]` |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:197:| Brief (chunk) | `chunk_summary_brief` | `chunk_summary_detailed`, truncated | — | `[chunk c4 unavailable: <reason>]` |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:198:| Tail tool result (short) | `tool_result_summary` | deterministic truncation (existing Epic 01 abbreviation rule) | — | n/a (raw content always exists) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:213:| `tool_result` (at-or-behind boundary) | `user` | `[tool result · <name> · abridged]\\n<summary or deterministic truncation>` (per the short-form ladder) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:289:**Wiring (DD — the advance seam, pinned).** Intake-stream imports the thread-view *surface* (sanctioned: domains call each other's surfaces in-process, never internals — the same rule that lets intake call `messages.createFromEvent`). At the end of batch projection it registers the advance on `ctx.onCommit`: advance first (synchronous, cheap), queue poke second (fires async drain); the advance call is wrapped so a throw is caught and diagnosed, never eats the poke, never reaches intake's caller (isolation half of epic TD-Q1). The advance runs at flush in **both host modes** — unlike the poke it is not mode-gated, because it is deterministic and cheap; this is what keeps CLI-driven threads from bloating. **Budgets resolve like the poke resolves** (epic-fix-001's instance seam): an SDK operation carries its instance's `SdkViewConfig.visibility` on the per-instance seam; below-SDK direct domain calls fall back to the defaults (32000/24000/8000). The CLI builds a real SDK (`cli/work.ts` pattern), so CLI intake gets config-or-defaults through the same path — no separate CLI budget channel, no silently different behavior. The advance's `SUM(token_estimate)` filters deleted messages — the sum must equal what pull would render.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:352:Stubs are structured-result: each returns `{ ok: false, errorClass: \"system_error\", reason: \"not implemented: <op>\" }` until Green (machine-readable contract; no throw stubs on this surface). Internal pure functions (`selectArrangement`, `advanceDecision`, `renderBand`) may throw `NotImplementedError` in skeleton.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:368:Inherited wholesale from Epic 02: real temp SQLite thread files everywhere (persistence is the product); the deterministic `DerivationProvider` fake is the only mock, and in this epic it appears *only in fixture setup* (draining Epic 02 work to manufacture form states) — no Epic 03 operation may touch it, and the architecture-risk suite asserts zero provider calls across pull/compact/sweep/status/materialize. CLI parity through the spawned-process suite (`LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1`). Verification tiers reuse the project's existing `verify` family unchanged.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:370:The Story-0 fixture is the load-bearing test asset: one recorded conversation (~12 turns, 4 chunks, tool-heavy middle) drained through real Epic 02 machinery into known form states — ready everywhere, plus manufactured failed-transient (provider fake scripted retryable-fail-exhaust on named subjects), failed-permanent (scripted non-retryable), blocked (source damage via the Epic 01 corruption pattern on a sacrificial sibling fixture), and a canonical-corruption variant. States reached through production paths, never hand-written rows; fixture invariant tests prove each state by read-back before any story consumes it.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:383:| 3 Sweep | Walk, classify, requeue, receipts, embed | AC-3.1–3.7 | **Gate (extended): Epic 02 requeue patch landed, AND the terminal-failure write path verified against landed code** — exhausted forms must persist a classifiable reason class (and `metadata.attempts`/`lastError` per the patch direction); if the persisted reason is opaque at the gate check, the named Epic 02 patch is: stamp the provider's `retryable` flag onto the failed form at exhaustion (Epic 02 knew it at failure time and currently discards it), which makes classification exact rather than inferred |\npackages/lhc/test/goldens/g2-edge-exclusion.json:8:    { \"band\": \"detailed\", \"subjectKind\": \"chunk\", \"subjectId\": \"c1\", \"formUsed\": \"chunk_summary_detailed\", \"degraded\": false },\npackages/lhc/test/goldens/g2-edge-exclusion.json:9:    { \"band\": \"detailed\", \"subjectKind\": \"chunk\", \"subjectId\": \"c2\", \"formUsed\": \"chunk_summary_detailed\", \"degraded\": false },\npackages/lhc/src/scheduler.ts:140:          sourceRef: item.sourceRef as unknown as Record<string, string>,\npackages/lhc/test/view-compact.test.ts:6:// degraded states are reached through production paths (scripted provider\npackages/lhc/test/view-compact.test.ts:63:function sha256(value: unknown): string {\npackages/lhc/test/view-compact.test.ts:143:  it(\"rejects percentages summing to 105 naming the sum, and an unknown profile naming it; thread unchanged\", async () => {\npackages/lhc/test/view-compact.test.ts:165:    const unknown = await fixture.sdk.threadView.compact(\npackages/lhc/test/view-compact.test.ts:169:    expect(unknown.ok).toBe(false);\npackages/lhc/test/view-compact.test.ts:170:    if (unknown.ok) return;\npackages/lhc/test/view-compact.test.ts:171:    expect(unknown.error.errorClass).toBe(\"caller_error\");\npackages/lhc/test/view-compact.test.ts:172:    expect(unknown.error.code).toBe(\"unknown_profile\");\npackages/lhc/test/view-compact.test.ts:173:    expect(unknown.error.reason).toContain('\"nonesuch\"');\npackages/lhc/test/view-compact.test.ts:198:    // the fixture's transiently-failed summary requeues HERE — every later\npackages/lhc/test/view-compact.test.ts:205:      (line) => line.owner === \"messages\" && line.kind === \"tool_result_summary\",\npackages/lhc/test/view-compact.test.ts:422:// through production paths: c1's