ges/lhc/test/mutations.test.ts:317:      \"w-c1-chunk_summary_detailed-v2\",\npackages/lhc/test/mutations.test.ts:348:      \"w-c1-chunk_summary_brief-v3\",\npackages/lhc/test/mutations.test.ts:349:      \"w-c1-chunk_summary_detailed-v3\",\npackages/lhc/test/mutations.test.ts:507:describe(\"background mode: edit-and-walk-away (production path)\", () => {\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/05-render-targets/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:41:**Scope out:** non-PI formats (`--format` accepts `pi-session` only; unknown → caller error); any view or state mutation from materialize or any CLI read path.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/05-render-targets/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:68:Format fixture first — capture a real PI session file, trim to structure, commit with provenance note — because TC-5.5 is unwritable without it and it may surface format surprises that reshape `materialize.ts`. Then materialize over pull output (pure mapping + file write), then `cli/view.ts` command-by-command, then the process suite. Red: `materialize` stub; CLI commands exit nonzero with structured not-implemented.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/05-render-targets/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:115:Deterministic `id`s: the header id derives from thread id + view createdAt; message entry ids from message ids; a never-compacted thread's header uses the thread's created-at (viewId null — `ViewMeta` carries both nullables). Byte-identical repeats are the test for any sneaky `Date.now()`/random — hash the whole file. CLI band-override flags merge field-wise over the profile *before* validation, so `--full 40` on a 30/30/20/20 profile fails the sum check with the named violation — that's correct behavior, not a bug to smooth over. The `--format` flag accepts only `pi-session`; unknown → `caller_error` naming accepted values.\npackages/lhc/docs/0