ed with outcome ready-for-verification and status ok.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/05-render-targets/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:270:    planSummary: \"Resolved verifier finding S5-001 only. In src/cli/view.ts, `view pull` now prints the message array itself as JSON on stdout on success (the AC-5.5/TC-5.4 contract: the array IS the product, not an OpResult envelope), and `view materialize` prints the written path itself on stdout. Both commands fall through to the existing renderResult on failure, so every failure case still exits nonzero with the structured OpResult error JSON (missing-thread and unknown-format legs unchanged and still passing). status, compact, and sweep are untouched and keep printing the SDK result JSON, preserving their parity coverage. The --help blurb names the two success-output exceptions. cli-process-view.test.ts now asserts the story contract directly: the pull parity leg and the CLI-advance leg parse stdout as a ViewMessage[] and compare it to the SDK pull's messages; the materialize leg asserts stdout.trim() equals the --out path before validating the file. Manifest hash re-recorded for the modified process test; both gates rerun green.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/05-render-targets/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:308:        - \"Failure-case output is deliberately asymmetric with success output for these two commands (structured OpResult JSON on exit 1) — this is the story's own requirement ('failure case exits nonzero with a structured error') and is covered by the missing-thread and unknown-format legs\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/05-render-targets/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:353:    planSummary: \"Format fixture first: trimmed a real PI session file (PI 0.79.1, session version 3) into test/fixtures/pi-session-structure.jsonl with a provenance note, and a conformance helper that derives required shapes from the fixture at runtime. Then materialize over pull output: refactored the pull assembly in thread-view/index.ts into one shared assembleView() that both pull and materialize consume (parity by construction — internal/materialize.ts never sees a DB handle), with entry ids/timestamps derived from message ids, event recorded_at, and view created-at (never write-time clocks; tail rows now carry recorded_at via an event join, and thread_metadata feeds the header — the sanctioned fix-pull's-output path). Added the unknown_format caller error. Then cli/view.ts with the full pinned grammar (five commands, band-override flags merged field-wise before validation, --no-sweep, --json, --out, --format), routed ahead of the shared flag parser so its flags don't widen other commands. Finally the process suite: TC-5.4, parity legs for all five commands on twin fixture threads, the profile-violation and missing-thread nonzero legs, TC-3.3's CLI receipt-shape leg via the shared schema, and the CLI-intake-advances-boundary leg (spawned intake over default max → spawned pull shows abridged flips, spawned status zone ≤ target). Two hash-locked tests amended under the established sanctioned-amendment pattern (Story 2/3 precedent) with the manifest re-recorded.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/05-render-targets/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:357:        reason: \"new unknown_format caller-error code for materialize's format check (story Scope: unknown format names accepted values)\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/05-render-targets/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:366:        reason: \"pull assembly extracted into shared assembleView(); materialize implemented over the same entry array (AC-5.3 parity structural), touch-suppressed, format-validated; stub and notImplemented helper removed\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-