ts:222:         AND json_extract(df.metadata, '$.outcome') = 'unknown'\npackages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/forms.ts:225:    .get(toolCallId) as unknown as\npackages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/chunks.ts:2:// policy, and the close→summary enqueues. Placement is pure arithmetic over\npackages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/chunks.ts:8:// turn (with any close's summary enqueues) or nothing.\npackages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/chunks.ts:39:    .get(chunkId) as unknown as { n: number | bigint };\npackages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/chunks.ts:63:// members and the incoming turn opens the next chunk; a single projection\npackages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/chunks.ts:74:    .get(turnId) as unknown as { chunk_id: string; member_idx: number | bigint } | undefined;\npackages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/chunks.ts:90:    .get() as unknown as OpenChunkRow | undefined;\npackages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/chunks.ts:118:    // Max rule (AC-3.7): the projection alone meets the maximum, so the\npackages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/chunks.ts:127:// Closing queues the two summary kinds as two work items with independent\npackages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/chunks.ts:134:  return ([\"chunk_summary_detailed\", \"chunk_summary_brief\"] as const).map((kind) =>\npackages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/chunks.ts:151:    .all() as unknown as Array<{\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:43:**Dependencies:** Stories 0–2. **Hard gate, verify before story start (extended per design):** (1) Epic 02's requeue patch landed — live-work-only queue rows, no terminal-row collision; (2) the terminal-failure write path verified against landed code — exhausted forms persist a classifiable reason class (FC-0.4 proved the fixture side; this gate proves the production side). If the persisted reason is opaque, the named Epic 02 patch is: stamp the provider's `retryable` flag onto the failed form at exhaustion.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:51:  - **TC-3.1** (AC-3.1, AC-3.2, AC-3.3): Seed a thread with ready, pending, transiently-failed, non-transiently-failed, and blocked forms (fixture-manufactured states); sweep → returns immediately; transient failure requeued (work row exists, form pending), non-transient and blocked untouched and reported, pending untouched; provider fake observes zero calls from the sweep itself.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:58:  - **TC-3.4** (AC-3.6, AC-2.7): Compact with default options → receipt includes sweep section; compact with skip → receipt records the skip and no requeues occurred; drain after the default compact → requeued form heals; next compact's view includes the healed form. *(The drain leg exercises Epic 02 machinery through the provider fake — the one sanctioned test-setup use of inference machinery; no Epic 03 operation touches it.)*\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:65:The sweep is thread-view's only *writing* interaction with other domains, and it writes nothing itself — every mutation goes through `messages.requeue`/`turns.requeue`. It is the repair half of the degrade-don't-block posture: compact degrades around missing material; the sweep is why the same material isn't missing at the *next* compact. This story also completes the compact receipt: Story 2's `absent` placeholder becomes `SweepReceipt | { skipped: true }`.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:69:Gate first — both legs verified and recorded in the story log before any code (requeue patch landed; reason-class persistence verified against landed Epic 02 code, with FC-0.4 as the fixture-side proof). Then the classification table as data with its own unit legs, then the walk/bucket/receipt as a pure function over report outputs, then the requeue calls, then the compact embed + skip flag. Red: `sweep` stub + compact receipt still `absent`.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:103:Zero-provider assertion completes here across all five ops (the fake is in fixture scope all around the sweep — this assert is what keeps it out of the operation). Once-per-invocation dedupe is structural (owner noop) but asserted anyway — if Epic 02's requeue ever stops nooping, this is the test that notices.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:107:Buckets come from the *owners' report joins*, not raw form states: \"retrying\" is a report-level distinction (pending + queue detail), and the sweep must not re-derive it from `derived_form` reads. The receipt's `requeued` carries subject ids so TC-3.4 can follow specific forms through heal. The classification table starts minimal (the design's named classes); unknown codes landing in `permanentFailed` with their literal reason is the receipt's visibility mechanism — expanding the table is config-tier work later, not a redesign.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:162:| TC-1.2 | 1.1, 1.7 | view-pull | two pulls with nothing between are byte-identical and create no work or provider calls | provider fake call-count assert |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:166:| TC-2.1 | 2.2, 2.3, 2.7 | view-compact | profile compact succeeds with config in receipt; 105% sum and unknown profile reject with named violations, thread unchanged | read-back equality after rejections |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:178:| TC-4.2 | 4.1, 4.2 | view-boundary | flipped: usable summary renders summary; failed renders truncation + marker; interleaved assistant text full | |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:197:| zero-provider sweep across all five ops | view-sweep | The provider fake is in scope for fixtures; nothing stops an internal \"helpful\" derivation call except this assert. The epic's no-inference rule needs teeth. |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:216:Per-chunk TDD tables follow Epic 02's pattern; estimates: Chunk 0 ≈ 6, 1 ≈ 9, 2 ≈ 16 (incl. goldens + restart), 3 ≈ 10, 4 ≈ 13, 5 ≈ 11 — ~65 total. Red exits on the project `red-verify` (no behavior tests); structured-result stubs make Red failures assertion-shaped on the surface ops. Green exits on `green-verify` with test immutability. The process suite runs at story completion (`verify-all`), not in Red/Green loops.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:228:- current_summary: story-verify completed with outcome revise and status ok.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:288:        title: \"Sweep production path is still the Story 2 placeholder\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:309:        title: \"Required Story 3 test coverage is absent and existing tests assert old placeholder behavior\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:310:        evidence: \"packages/lhc/test/view-sweep.test.ts does not exist. Existing coverage still expects the placeholder behavior: packages/lhc/test/view-pull.test.ts lines 98-108 asserts sweep returns ok:false not_implemented, and packages/lhc/test/view-compact.test.ts lines 196-198 asserts compact receipt sweep is \\\"absent\\\". The configured gates passed, but they did not exercise TC-3.1 through TC-3.4 or the shared SweepReceipt schema leg for TC-3.3.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:328:        title: \"Sweep production path is still the Story 2 placeholder\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:349:        title: \"Required Story 3 test coverage is absent and existing tests assert old placeholder behavior\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:350:        evidence: \"packages/lhc/test/view-sweep.test.ts does not exist. Existing coverage still expects the placeholder behavior: packages/lhc/test/view-pull.test.ts lines 98-108 asserts sweep returns ok:false not_implemented, and packages/lhc/test/view-compact.test.ts lines 196-198 asserts compact receipt sweep is \\\"absent\\\". The configured gates passed, but they did not exercise TC-3.1 through TC-3.4 or the shared SweepReceipt schema leg for TC-3.3.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:368:        - \"AC-3.1, AC-3.2, AC-3.3, TC-3.1: no sweep report walk, classification, owner requeue behavior, no-wait behavior, or zero-provider sweep assertion exists because sweep is a stub.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smar