pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:33:**Objective:** prove the hot path before any view machinery exists. The array shape pinned here is the contract Stories 2–5 render into.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:36:- `thread-view` surface skeleton (structured-result stubs per tech design §Interface Definitions) with `pull` and `status` implemented\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:48:  - **TC-1.2** (AC-1.1, AC-1.7): Pull twice with nothing between → byte-identical results; assert no work rows created, no provider double calls recorded (provider fake observes zero calls).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:63:First story on the surface: `thread-view/index.ts` is born here with all five operations as structured-result stubs, two of which (`pull`, `status`) go real. The pull this story builds is the *tail-only* path — no view row exists yet, so `snapshot.ts` reads return absent and the whole record renders as tail from event 1. The array shape and tail mapping pinned here are load-bearing for every later story: Story 2 prepends band messages to this exact shape, Story 4 changes which results render short, Story 5 maps it to JSONL.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:67:Types first (`shared/view.ts` landed in Story 0 — consume, don't redefine), then the surface skeleton with all five stubs (Red asserts each returns `{ ok: false, reason: \"not implemented: <op>\" }`), then Green: `render.ts` tail formatting kind-by-kind against the mapping table, then `pull` assembly, then `status`. The mapping table is seven rows — implement and test them as seven legs, not one blob assertion, so a single kind's drift fails one named test.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:73:| `src/domains/thread-view/index.ts` | surface skeleton (5 ops, structured-result stubs); `pull` + `status` real |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:74:| `src/domains/thread-view/internal/render.ts` | tail formatting: the 7-kind mapping table, short/full tool-result selection by boundary position, short-form ladder (summary → deterministic truncation) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:83:| Surface signatures, stub contract | tech-design.md L342–352 |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:95:| TC-1.2 | `view-pull.test.ts` | two pulls, nothing between: byte-identical; zero work rows; provider fake count unchanged |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:159:| TC-1.2 | 1.1, 1.7 | view-pull | two pulls with nothing between are byte-identical and create no work or provider calls | provider fake call-count assert |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:163:| TC-2.1 | 2.2, 2.3, 2.7 | view-compact | profile compact succeeds with config in receipt; 105% sum and unknown profile reject with named violations, thread unchanged | read-back equality after rejections |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:175:| TC-4.2 | 4.1, 4.2 | view-boundary | flipped: usable summary renders summary; failed renders truncation + marker; interleaved assistant text full | |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:194:| zero-provider sweep across all five ops | view-sweep | The provider fake is in scope for fixtures; nothing stops an internal \"helpful\" derivation call except this assert. The epic's no-inference rule needs teeth. |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:213:Per-chunk TDD tables follow Epic 02's pattern; estimates: Chunk 0 ≈ 6, 1 ≈ 9, 2 ≈ 16 (incl. goldens + restart), 3 ≈ 10, 4 ≈ 13, 5 ≈ 11 — ~65 total. Red exits on the project `red-verify` (no behavior tests); structured-result stubs make Red failures assertion-shaped on the surface ops. Green exits on `green-verify` with test immutability. The process suite runs at story completion (`verify-all`), not in Red/Green loops.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:225:- current_summary: story-continue completed with outcome ready-for-verification and status ok.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:258:    planSummary: \"Fixed SV-01-PULL-STATUS-001 at the seam layer: the verified side-effect path was openThreadDatabase → fireThreadTouch → scheduler.touch, which in a background SDK can hang a first-touch catch-up drain (queue claims, provider calls, writes) off a thread-view read. The fix is a reads-only operation scope in shared/context.ts — runWithThreadTouchSuppressed runs a function under the current instance seam with the touch announcement replaced by a no-op while preserving the poke target and view config (and delegating to the below-SDK defaults when no seam is in scope, minus the touch). thread-view pull and status wrap their entire bodies in this scope, which structurally covers not just their own openThreadDatabase calls but also the owners' report surfaces status consumes — no test-only bypass, no signature changes to the frozen messages/turns domains, and write paths are untouched so first-touch catch-up still works everywhere it should. A new background-mode test leg extends TC-1.2/TC-2.5: pending work is manufactured through a manual SDK, then a fresh background SDK pulls twice and reads status; it asserts work rows / form states / view rows / boundary unchanged (full below-SDK state snapshot), provider fake at zero calls, repeated pulls byte-identical via full-result hash, repeated status byte-identical, and pending work visible through the read itself — after settling the scheduler (timeout + drainSettled) so a wrongly-scheduled drain would surface. The regression test was proven live: with the suppression temporarily removed it fails (the catch-up drain fires), with the fix it passes.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:340:    planSummary: \"Landed the thread-view surface skeleton with pull and status real. pull is the tail-only hot path built as the production code path with snapshot-absent (band prepend + tail render share one path, no never-compacted branch): snapshot.ts reads the view header/bands (absent ⇒ null) plus the deleted-filtered tail messages, boundary.ts reads the seeded position and owns the parameterized deleted-filtered zone SUM Story 4's advance will consume, and render.ts implements the seven-kind tail mapping table as pure functions with the short-form ladder (ready tool_result_summary → Epic 01 deterministic truncation) selected by boundary position. status reads tail tokens vs threshold (compactRecommended = tailTokens > threshold, nothing smarter), derivation counts bucketed from the owners' report surfaces (must-not-own respected — no direct derived_form reads for counts), view health null pre-compact, and the live zone sum vs max. Config reaches the domain through the per-instance seam (InstanceSeam.view, Flow 4's pattern) with below-SDK calls falling back to resolveViewConfig() defaults. compact/sweep/materialize return structured not-implemented results under a new not_implemented ErrorCode. sdk.ts exposes the threadView namespace (five ops) scoped to the instance seam.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:344:        reason: \"Surface skeleton: pull and status implemented; compact/sweep/materialize structured-result stubs; Story 0 profile re-exports retained\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:350:        reason: \"New: read path — view header + bands (absent ⇒ tail-only signal), tail message/block reads, tail token sum, ready tool_result_summary reads\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:362:        reason: \"New ErrorCode not_implemented for the surface-skeleton stub contract (system_error class per tech design)\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:368:        reason: \"New: TC-1.1, TC-1.2, TC-1.4 (both ladder rungs), TC-2.5 pre-compact legs, seven named mapping legs, stub-contract test, zero-provider pull/status legs\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:384:        - \"test/view-pull.test.ts :: TC-1.4 ready summary behind / full ahead / non-tool full everywhere\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:408:        - \"The tech design's stub sketch ({ ok: false, errorClass, reason }) was realized through the codebase's binding OpResult contract as { ok: false, error: { errorClass, code: 'not_implemented', reason } } — a new ErrorCode was added rather than reusing storage_failure so the contract stays machine-readable.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:486:        evidence: \"AC-1.1 requires pull to do local reads and deterministic assembly only with no inference, network, queue interaction, or writes; AC-2.8 requires status to be reads-only with no side effects. `threadView.pull` and `status` call `openThreadDatabase` at `src/domains/thread-view/index.ts:81` and `src/domains/thread-view/index.ts:170`. `openThreadDatabase` always calls `fireThreadTouch` at `src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts:206-209`. In a background SDK, `createSdk` wires that touch to `scheduler.touch` at `src/sdk.ts:339-344`, and `scheduler.touch` schedules a drain when live work exists at `src/scheduler.ts:383-394`. Focused probes confirmed the production effect: after manual intake left 4 work rows, a background `threadView.pull` followed by `drainSettled` changed work rows 4→0 and the provider double captured 5 calls (`smoothPrompt`, `summarizeToolCall`, `summarizeToolResult`, `composeTurnRendering`, `projectLowerBand`). The same happened for background `threadView.status`. A boundary-seeded two-pull probe also returned `equal:false`: first pull rendered raw fallback text and the second rendered the provider-produced summary after the pull-triggered drain. Existing TC-1.2/TC-2.5 tests exercise manual SDK paths only (`test/view-pull.test.ts:34-39`; fixture SDK is manual at `test/fixtures/view-thread.ts:133-139`).\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:508:        evidence: \"AC-1.1 requires pull to do local reads and deterministic assembly only with no inference, network, queue interaction, or writes; AC-2.8 requires status to be reads-only with no side effects. `threadView.pull` and `status` call `openThreadDatabase` at `src/domains/thread-view/index.ts:81` and `src/domains/thread-view/index.ts:170`. `openThreadDatabase` always calls `fireThreadTouch` at `src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts:206-209`. In a background SDK, `createSdk` wires that touch to `scheduler.touch` at `src/sdk.ts:339-344`, and `scheduler.touch` schedules a drain when live work exists at `src/scheduler.ts:383-394`. Focused probes confirmed the production effect: after manual intake left 4 work rows, a background `threadView.pull` followed by `drainSettled` changed work rows 4→0 and the provider double captured 5 calls (`smoothPrompt`, `summarizeToolCall`, `summarizeToolResult`, `composeTurnRendering`, `projectLowerBand`). The same happened for background `threadView.status`. A boundary-seeded two-pull probe also returned `equal:false`: first pull rendered raw fallback text and the second rendered the provider-produced summary after the pull-triggered drain. Existing TC-1.2/TC-2.5 tests exercise manual SDK paths only (`test/view-pull.test.ts:34-39`; fixture SDK is manual at `test/fixtures/view-thread.ts:133-139`).\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:529:        - \"AC-1.5 / TC-1.4: story tests verify boundary short/full rendering, ready-summary fallback, truncation fallback, and non-tool content full rendering.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:533:        - \"AC-1.1 / TC-1.2: background SDK production path violates no-provider/no-queue/read-only behavior.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:560:      - \"No material fake adapter, shim, placeholder, or fallback branch was found in the thread-view production code path; the blocker is real side-effect behavior in the SDK read path.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:624:  summary: \"Verifier found one blocking Story 1 violation: background SDK pull/status can trigger scheduler drain work, provider calls, work-row mutations, and non-byte-identical pulls. Continue the existing implementor to fix SV-01-PULL-STATUS-001 and add production-path coverage for background SDK pull/status read-only behavior.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:652:  summary: \"Story orchestration run started after orienting from 1 existing artifact(s).\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:658:  summary: \"Fresh story-lead provider turn executed without planner session resume.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:670:  summary: \"Story-lead selected run-implement.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:680:  summary: \"Story-lead recorded a durable self-note for a future planner turn.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:691:  summary: \"story-implement completed with outcome ready-for-verification and status ok.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:703:  summary: \"Fresh story-lead provider turn executed without planner session resume.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:715:  summary: \"Story-lead selected run-verify.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:725:  summary: \"Story-lead recorded a durable self-note for a future planner turn.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:736:  summary: \"story-verify completed with outcome revise and status ok.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:748:  summary: \"Fresh story-lead provider turn executed without planner session resume.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:760:  summary: \"Story-lead selected run-continue.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:770:  summary: \"Story-lead recorded a durable self-note for a future planner turn.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:781:  summary: \"story-continue completed with outcome ready-for-verification and status ok.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:873:{\"action\":\"accept-story\",\"rationale\":\"...\",\"inputs\":{\"summary\":\"...\",\"acceptanceCheckRefs\":[\"...\"],\"acceptanceChecks\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":[\"...\"],\"reasoning\":\"...\"}],\"recommendedImplLeadAction\":\"accept\"},\"verification\":{\"finalVerifierOutcome\":\"pass\",\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"...\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":[\"...\"]}]}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:52:- **FC-0.2**: Invalid profile configs are rejected at SDK construction with errors naming the violation (band sum ≠ 100, `max ≤ target`, `target < floor`, non-positive lower bound, unknown built-in override target).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:95:| FC-0.2 | `view-fixture.test.ts` | each invalid config rejected at construction with the named violation (sum≠100, max≤target, target<floor, bound≤0, unknown override) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:107:The fixture conversation shape is pinned in the design (~12 turns, 4 chunks, tool-heavy middle): the tool-heavy middle is what gives Story 4 a realistic over-max zone, and the 4 chunks give Story 2's coverage edge something to exclude. Scripted provider failures manufacture the failed states (retryable-fail-exhaust for transient; non-retryable for permanent); blocked comes from source damage on a sacrificial sibling fixture, not the main one. FC-0.4 is the Story 3 gate's fixture-side proof — if it can't pass because Epic 02's persisted reason is opaque, stop and surface it immediately; that's the named Epic 02 patch trigger, not something to work around.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:111:Fixture states must be reached through real `intake → drain` paths against the deterministic provider. Hand-writing `derived_form` rows to fake a state is the exact fiction FC-0.3 exists to prevent — a hand-written row can encode a state shape the production writer never produces, and every downstream test would then prove compatibility with fiction. The boundary-seed helper is the one sanctioned below-SDK write, and only because boundary *mechanics* are Story 4's to prove.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:162:| TC-1.2 | 1.1, 1.7 | view-pull | two pulls with nothing between are byte-identical and create no work or provider calls | provider fake call-count assert |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:166:| TC-2.1 | 2.2, 2.3, 2.7 | view-compact | profile compact succeeds with config in receipt; 105% sum and unknown profile reject with named violations, thread unchanged | read-back equality after rejections |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:178:| TC-4.2 | 4.1, 4.2 | view-boundary | flipped: usable summary renders summary; failed renders truncation + marker; interleaved assistant text full | |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:197:| zero-provider sweep across all five ops | view-sweep | The provider fake is in scope for fixtures; nothing stops an internal \"helpful\" derivation call except this assert. The epic's no-inference rule needs teeth. |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:216:Per-chunk TDD tables follow Epic 02's pattern; estimates: Chunk 0 ≈ 6, 1 ≈ 9, 2 ≈ 16 (incl. goldens + restart), 3 ≈ 10, 4 ≈ 13, 5 ≈ 11 — ~65 total. Red exits on the project `red-verify` (no behavior tests); structured-result stubs make Red failures assertion-shaped on the surface ops. Green exits on `green-verify` with test immutability. The process suite runs at story completion (`verify-all`), not in Red/Green loops.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:228:- current_summary: Story orchestration started and durable state has been initialized.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:274:  summary: \"Orient from 1 existing story artifact(s).\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:299:  summary: \"Story orchestration run started after orienting from 1 existing artifact(s).\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:385:{\"action\":\"accept-story\",\"rationale\":\"...\",\"inputs\":{\"summary\":\"...\",\"acceptanceCheckRefs\":[\"...\"],\"acceptanceChecks\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":[\"...\"],\"reasoning\":\"...\"}],\"recommendedImplLeadAction\":\"accept\"},\"verification\":{\"finalVerifierOutcome\":\"pass\",\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"...\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":[\"...\"]}]}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/04-tool-result-visibility/story-lead/streams/001-story-lead.stdout.log:3:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"{\\\"action\\\":\\\"run-implement\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"No bounded child operation has run yet, and the durable record is ready for the first implementation pass. The story file and test plan provide sufficient story-local requirements for TC-4.1 through TC-4.6, seam isolation, both host modes, G1 golden, status consistency, and verify expectations.\\\",\\\"inputs\\\":{\\\"promptAddendum\\\":\\\"Implement Story 4: Tool-Result Visibility using only the story file and test plan as requirements. Focus on the full production path: boundary advance decision and executor, post-commit SDK seam wiring in intake-stream with advance first and poke second, throw isolation both directions, per-instance visibility budget resolution and validation, boundary-active short-form rendering in pulls, compact reset proof, TC-4.1 through TC-4.6, seam-isolation sibling leg, both host modes, status zone sum consistency, and Boundary G1 trajectory golden. Do not add a host-called advance surface. Keep changes scoped and run the configured story gate `pnpm run green-verify` before returning evidence.\\\"},\\\"selfNote\\\":\\\"After implementor returns, check for required evidence: TC-4.1-4.6, seam isolation both directions, both host modes, G1 golden, status sum consistency, and green-verify output before deciding verify or quick-fix.\\\"}\"}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/04-tool-result-visibility/story-lead/streams/001-story-lead.stdout.log:11:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"{\\\"action\\\":\\\"accept-story\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Latest verifier result is pass with no open findings, required Story 4 proof is present, and configured gates passed.\\\",\\\"inputs\\\":{\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Story 4 implementation is verified against TC-4.1 through TC-4.6, boundary rendering, deterministic advance, protected floor behavior, never-backward behavior, compact reset, budget validation, post-commit seam isolation, both in-process host modes, Boundary G1 golden, and status/advance deleted-filter consistency.\\\",\\\"acceptanceCheckRefs\\\":[\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/04-tool-result-visibility/003-implementor.json\\\",\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/04-tool-result-visibility/004-verify.json\\\"],\\\"acceptanceChecks\\\":[{\\\"name\\\":\\\"TC-4.1-4.6 coverage\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"pass\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"Verifier reports all Story 4 acceptance criteria and TC-4.1 through TC-4.6 verified in packages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts.\\\"],\\\"reasoning\\\":\\\"The verifier found no unverified requirements and no open findings.\\\"},{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Architecture-risk proof\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"pass\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"Verifier reports seam isolation both directions, manual/background in-process host-mode advance proof, Boundary G1 golden, and status-sum/delete-filter consistency verified.\\\"],\\\"reasoning\\\":\\\"These satisfy the story Definition of Done items present in the durable record.\\\"},{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Verification gates\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"pass\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"cd packages/lhc && pnpm run green-verify: pass\\\",\\\"cd packages/lhc && pnpm run verify-all: pass\\\"],\\\"reasoning\\\":\\\"The configured story and epic gates passed according to the verifier artifact.\\\"}],\\\"recommendedImplLeadAction\\\":\\\"accept\\\"},\\\"verification\\\":{\\\"finalVerifierOutcome\\\":\\\"pass\\\",\\\"findings\\\":[]}}\"}}\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/threads.ts:107:        .all() as unknown as Array<{\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/threads.ts:126:        .all() as unknown as Array<{\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/threads.ts:166:      .all() as unknown as RawFormRow[];\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/threads.ts:270:    { subjectKind: \"message\", subjectId: \"m4\", form: \"tool_result_summary\" },\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/threads.ts:292:      { subjectKind: \"message\", subjectId: \"m4\", form: \"tool_result_summary\", state: \"ready\" },\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/threads.ts:295:      { subjectKind: \"turn\", subjectId: \"t1\", form: \"lower_band_projection\", state: \"pending\" },\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/threads.ts:297:      { subjectKind: \"turn\", subjectId: \"t2\", form: \"lower_band_projection\", state: \"pending\" },\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:43:**Dependencies:** Stories 0–2. **Hard gate, verify before story start (extended per design):** (1) Epic 02's requeue patch landed — live-work-only queue rows, no terminal-row collision; (2) the terminal-failure write path verified against landed code — exhausted forms persist a classifiable reason class (FC-0.4 proved the fixture side; this gate proves the production side). If the persisted reason is opaque, the named Epic 02 patch is: stamp the provider's `retryable` flag onto the failed form at exhaustion.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:51:  - **TC-3.1** (AC-3.1, AC-3.2, AC-3.3): Seed a thread with ready, pending, transiently-failed, non-transiently-failed, and blocked forms (fixture-manufactured states); sweep → returns immediately; transient failure requeued (work row exists, form pending), non-transient and blocked untouched and reported, pending untouched; provider fake observes zero calls from the sweep itself.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:58:  - **TC-3.4** (AC-3.6, AC-2.7): Compact with default options → receipt includes sweep section; compact with skip → receipt records the skip and no requeues occurred; drain after the default compact → requeued form heals; next compact's view includes the healed form. *(The drain leg exercises Epic 02 machinery through the provider fake — the one sanctioned test-setup use of inference machinery; no Epic 03 operation touches it.)*\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:65:The sweep is thread-view's only *writing* interaction with other domains, and it writes nothing itself — every mutation goes through `messages.requeue`/`turns.requeue`. It is the repair half of the degrade-don't-block posture: compact degrades around missing material; the sweep is why the same material isn't missing at the *next* compact. This story also completes the compact receipt: Story 2's `absent` placeholder becomes `SweepReceipt | { skipped: true }`.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:69:Gate first — both legs verified and recorded in the story log before any code (requeue patch landed; reason-class persistence verified against landed Epic 02 code, with FC-0.4 as the fixture-side proof). Then the classification table as data with its own unit legs, then the walk/bucket/receipt as a pure function over report outputs, then the requeue calls, then the compact embed + skip flag. Red: `sweep` stub + compact receipt still `absent`.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:103:Zero-provider assertion completes here across all five ops (the fake is in fixture scope all around the sweep — this assert is what keeps it out of the operation). Once-per-invocation dedupe is structural (owner noop) but asserted anyway — if Epic 02's requeue ever stops nooping, this is the test that notices.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:107:Buckets come from the *owners' report joins*, not raw form states: \"retrying\" is a report-level distinction (pending + queue detail), and the sweep must not re-derive it from `derived_form` reads. The receipt's `requeued` carries subject ids so TC-3.4 can follow specific forms through heal. The classification table starts minimal (the design's named classes); unknown codes landing in `permanentFailed` with their literal reason is the receipt's visibility mechanism — expanding the table is config-tier work later, not a redesign.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:162:| TC-1.2 | 1.1, 1.7 | view-pull | two pulls with nothing between are byte-identical and create no work or provider calls | provider fake call-count assert |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:166:| TC-2.1 | 2.2, 2.3, 2.7 | view-compact | profile compact succeeds with config in receipt; 105% sum and unknown profile reject with named violations, thread unchanged | read-back equality after rejections |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:178:| TC-4.2 | 4.1, 4.2 | view-boundary | flipped: usable summary renders summary; failed renders truncation + marker; interleaved assistant text full | |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:197:| zero-provider sweep across all five ops | view-sweep | The provider fake is in scope for fixtures; nothing stops an internal \"helpful\" derivation call except this assert. The epic's no-inference rule needs teeth. |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:216:Per-chunk TDD tables follow Epic 02's pattern; estimates: Chunk 0 ≈ 6, 1 ≈ 9, 2 ≈ 16 (incl. goldens + restart), 3 ≈ 10, 4 ≈ 13, 5 ≈ 11 — ~65 total. Red exits on the project `red-verify` (no behavior tests); structured-result stubs make Red failures assertion-shaped on the surface ops. Green exits on `green-verify` with test immutability. The process suite runs at story completion (`verify-all`), not in Red/Green loops.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:228:- current_summary: Story orchestration resume requested and durable state has been reopened.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:288