ult_summary\", 3, {\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/view-thread.ts:167:      double.failKind(\"tool_result_summary\", 1, {\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/view-thread.ts:248:        `fixture invariant: expected exactly one transient-failed and one permanent-failed tool_result_summary on the named subjects`,\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:33:**Objective:** prove the hot path before any view machinery exists. The array shape pinned here is the contract Stories 2–5 render into.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:36:- `thread-view` surface skeleton (structured-result stubs per tech design §Interface Definitions) with `pull` and `status` implemented\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:48:  - **TC-1.2** (AC-1.1, AC-1.7): Pull twice with nothing between → byte-identical results; assert no work rows created, no provider double calls recorded (provider fake observes zero calls).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:63:First story on the surface: `thread-view/index.ts` is born here with all five operations as structured-result stubs, two of which (`pull`, `status`) go real. The pull this story builds is the *tail-only* path — no view row exists yet, so `snapshot.ts` reads return absent and the whole record renders as tail from event 1. The array shape and tail mapping pinned here are load-bearing for every later story: Story 2 prepends band messages to this exact shape, Story 4 changes which results render short, Story 5 maps it to JSONL.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:67:Types first (`shared/view.ts` landed in Story 0 — consume, don't redefine), then the surface skeleton with all five stubs (Red asserts each returns `{ ok: false, reason: \"not implemented: <op>\" }`), then Green: `render.ts` tail formatting kind-by-kind against the mapping table, then `pull` assembly, then `status`. The mapping table is seven rows — implement and test them as seven legs, not one blob assertion, so a single kind's drift fails one named test.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:73:| `src/domains/thread-view/index.ts` | surface skeleton (5 ops, structured-result stubs); `pull` + `status` real |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:74:| `src/domains/thread-view/internal/render.ts` | tail formatting: the 7-kind mapping table, short/full tool-result selection by boundary position, short-form ladder (summary → deterministic truncation) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:83:| Surface signatures, stub contract | tech-design.md L342–352 |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:95:| TC-1.2 | `view-pull.test.ts` | two pulls, nothing between: byte-identical; zero work rows; provider fake count unchanged |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:159:| TC-1.2 | 1.1, 1.7 | view-pull | two pulls with nothing between are byte-identical and create no work or provider calls | provider fake call-count assert |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:163:| TC-2.1 | 2.2, 2.3, 2.7 | view-compact | profile compact succeeds with config in receipt; 105% sum and unknown profile reject with named violations, thread unchanged | read-back equality after rejections |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:175:| TC-4.2 | 4.1, 4.2 | view-boundary | flipped: usable summary renders summary; failed renders truncation + marker; interleaved assistant text full | |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:194:| zero-provider sweep across all five ops | view-sweep | The provider fake is in scope for fixtures; nothing stops an internal \"helpful\" derivation call except this assert. The epic's no-inference rule needs teeth. |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:213:Per-chunk TDD tables follow Epic 02's pattern; estimates: Chunk 0 ≈ 6, 1 ≈ 9, 2 ≈ 16 (incl. goldens + restart), 3 ≈ 10, 4 ≈ 13, 5 ≈ 11 — ~65 total. Red exits on the project `red-verify` (no behavior tests); structured-result stubs make Red failures assertion-shaped on the surface ops. Green exits on `green-verify` with test immutability. The process suite runs at story completion (`verify-all`), not in Red/Green loops.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:225:- current_summary: Story orchestration started and durable state has been initialized.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:271:  summary: \"Orient from 1 existing story artifact(s).\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:296:  summary: \"Story orchestration run started after orienting from 1 existing artifact(s).\"\npacka