fest.json:11:    \"test/cli-process-projection.test.ts\": \"ef4770eacb01448c0414a4316ed0b1be17d45b42d2fa6dbead26f496f93b35e3\",\npackages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts:66:      version: 2, // Story 3: message projection\npackages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts:143:function errorDetail(cause: unknown): string {\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:33:**Objective:** prove the hot path before any view machinery exists. The array shape pinned here is the contract Stories 2–5 render into.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:36:- `thread-view` surface skeleton (structured-result stubs per tech design §Interface Definitions) with `pull` and `status` implemented\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:48:  - **TC-1.2** (AC-1.1, AC-1.7): Pull twice with nothing between → byte-identical results; assert no work rows created, no provider double calls recorded (provider fake observes zero calls).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:63:First story on the surface: `thread-view/index.ts` is born here with all five operations as structured-result stubs, two of which (`pull`, `status`) go real. The pull this story builds is the *tail-only* path — no view row exists yet, so `snapshot.ts` reads return absent and the whole record renders as tail from event 1. The array shape and tail mapping pinned here are load-bearing for every later story: Story 2 prepends band messages to this exact shape, Story 4 changes which results render short, Story 5 maps it to JSONL.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:67:Types first (`shared/view.ts` landed in Story 0 — consume, don't redefine), then the surface skeleton with all five stubs (Red asserts each returns `{ ok: false, reason: \"not implemented: <op>\" }`), then Green: `render.ts` tail formatting kind-by-kind against the mapping table, then `pull` assembly, then `status`. The mapping table is seven rows — implement and test them as seven legs, not one blob assertion, so a single kind's drift fails one named test.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:73:| `src/domains/thread-view/index.ts` | surface skeleton (5 ops, structured-result stubs); `pull` + `status` real |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:74:| `src/domains/thread-view/internal/render.ts` | tail formatting: the 7-kind mapping table, short/full tool-result selection by boundary position, short-form ladder (summary → deterministic truncation) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:83:| Surface signatures, stub contract | tech-design.md L342–352 |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:95:| TC-1.2 | `view-pull.test.ts` | two pulls, nothing between: byte-identical; zero work rows; provider fake count unchanged |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:159:| TC-1.2 | 1.1, 1.7 | view-pull | two pulls with nothing between are byte-identical and create no work or provider calls | provider fake call-count assert |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:163:| TC-2.1 | 2.2, 2.3, 2.7 | view-compact | profile compact succeeds with config in receipt; 105% sum and unknown profile reject with named violations, thread unchanged | read-back equality after rejections |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:175:| TC-4.2 | 4.1, 4.2 | view-boundary | flipped: usable summary renders summary; failed renders truncation + marker; interleaved assistant text full | |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:194:| zero-provider sweep across all five ops | view-sweep | The provider fake is in scope for fixtures; nothing stops an internal \"helpful\" derivation call except this assert. The epic's no-inference rule needs teeth. |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:213:Per-chunk TDD tables follow Epic 02's pattern; estimates: Chunk 0 ≈ 6, 1 ≈ 9, 2 ≈ 16 (incl. goldens + restart), 3 ≈ 10, 4 ≈ 13, 5 ≈ 11 — ~65 total. Red exits on the project `red-verify` (no behavior tests); structured-result stubs make Red failures assertion-shaped on the surface ops. Green exits on `green-verify` with test immutability. The process suite runs at story completion (`verify-all`), not in Red/Green loops.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:225:- current_summary: story-verify completed with outcome pass and status ok.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:282:        - \"AC-1.5 / TC-1.4: existing tests verify boundary short/full rendering, ready-summary fallback, truncation fallback, and non-tool content full rendering.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:285:        - \"Definition of Done: structured stubs, zero-provider assertions, full-result hashing, array shape comments, and required gates are present and green.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:306:      - \"No fake adapter, placeholder branch, or non-real runtime path was found in the fix. The suppression scope is production code used by the SDK thread-view read path, and the regression test goes through `createSdk().threadView.pull/status` against real temp thread files.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:346:    planSummary: \"Landed the thread-view surface skeleton with pull and status real. pull is the tail-only hot path built as the production code path with snapshot-absent (band prepend + tail render share one path, no never-compacted branch): snapshot.ts reads the view header/bands (absent ⇒ null) plus the deleted-filtered tail messages, boundary.ts reads the seeded position and owns the parameterized deleted-filtered zone SUM Story 4's advance will consume, and render.ts implements the seven-kind tail mapping table as pure functions with the short-form ladder (ready tool_result_summary → Epic 01 deterministic truncation) selected by boundary position. status reads tail tokens vs threshold (compactRecommended = tailTokens > threshold, nothing smarter), derivation counts bucketed from the owners' report surfaces (must-not-own respected — no direct derived_form reads for counts), view health null pre-compact, and the live zone sum vs max. Config reaches the domain through the per-instance seam (InstanceSeam.view, Flow 4's pattern) with below-SDK calls falling back to resolveViewConfig() defaults. compact/sweep/materialize return structured not-implemented results under a new not_implemented ErrorCode. sdk.ts exposes the threadView namespace (five ops) scoped to the instance seam.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:350:        reason: \"Surface skeleton: pull and status implemented; compact/sweep/materialize structured-result stubs; Story 0 profile re-exports retained\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:356:        reason: \"New: read path — view header + bands (absent ⇒ tail-only signal), tail message/block reads, tail token sum, ready tool_result_summary reads\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:368:        reason: \"New ErrorCode not_implemented for the surface-skeleton stub contract (system_error class per tech design)\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:374:        reason: \"New: TC-1.1, TC-1.2, TC-1.4 (both ladder rungs), TC-2.5 pre-compact legs, seven named mapping legs, stub-contract test, zero-provider pull/status legs\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:390:        - \"test/view-pull.test.ts :: TC-1.4 ready summary behind / full ahead / non-tool full everywhere\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:414:        - \"The tech design's stub sketch ({ ok: false, errorClass, reason }) was realized through the codebase's binding OpResult contract as { ok: false, error: { errorClass, code: 'not_implemented', reason } } — a new ErrorCode was added rather than reusing storage_failure so the contract stays machine-readable.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:492:        evidence: \"AC-1.1 requires pull to do local reads and deterministic assembly only with no inference, network, queue interaction, or writes; AC-2.8 requires status to be reads-only with no side effects. `threadView.pull` and `status` call `openThreadDatabase` at `src/domains/thread-view/index.ts:81` and `src/domains/thread-view/index.ts:170`. `openThreadDatabase` always calls `fireThreadTouch` at `src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts:206-209`. In a background SDK, `createSdk` wires that touch to `scheduler.touch` at `src/sdk.ts:339-344`, and `scheduler.touch` schedules a drain when live work exists at `src/scheduler.ts:383-394`. Focused probes confirmed the production effect: after manual intake left 4 work rows, a background `threadView.pull` followed by `drainSettled` changed work rows 4→0 and the provider double captured 5 calls (`smoothPrompt`, `summarizeToolCall`, `summarizeToolResult`, `composeTurnRendering`, `projectLowerBand`). The same happened for background `threadView.status`. A boundary-seeded two-pull probe also returned `equal:false`: first pull rendered raw fallback text and the second rendered the provider-produced summary after the pull-triggered drain. Existing TC-1.2/TC-2.5 tests exercise manual SDK paths only (`test/view-pull.test.ts:34-39`; fixture SDK is manual at `test/fixtures/view-thread.ts:133-139`).\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:514:        evidence: \"AC-1.1 requires pull to do local reads and deterministic assembly only with no inference, network, queue interaction, or writes; AC-2.8 requires status to be reads-only with no side effects. `threadView.pull` and `status` call `openThreadDatabase` at `src/domains/thread-view/index.ts:81` and `src/domains/thread-view/index.ts:170`. `openThreadDatabase` always calls `fireThreadTouch` at `src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts:206-209`. In a background SDK, `createSdk` wires that touch to `scheduler.touch` at `src/sdk.ts:339-344`, and `scheduler.touch` schedules a drain when live work exists at `src/scheduler.ts:383-394`. Focused probes confirmed the production effect: after manual intake left 4 work rows, a background `threadView.pull` followed by `drainSettled` changed work rows 4→0 and the provider double captured 5 calls (`smoothPrompt`, `summarizeToolCall`, `summarizeToolResult`, `composeTurnRendering`, `projectLowerBand`). The same happened for background `threadView.status`. A boundary-seeded two-pull probe also returned `equal:false`: first pull rendered raw fallback text and the second rendered the provider-produced summary after the pull-triggered drain. Existing TC-1.2/TC-2.5 tests exercise manual SDK paths only (`test/view-pull.test.ts:34-39`; fixture SDK is manual at `test/fixtures/view-thread.ts:133-139`).\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:535:        - \"AC-1.5 / TC-1.4: story tests verify boundary short/full rendering, ready-summary fallback, truncation fallback, and non-tool content full rendering.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:539:        - \"AC-1.1 / TC-1.2: background SDK production path violates no-provider/no-queue/read-only behavior.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:566:      - \"No material fake adapter, shim, placeholder, or fallback branch was found in the thread-view production code path; the blocker is real side-effect behavior in the SDK read path.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:604:    planSummary: \"Fixed SV-01-PULL-STATUS-001 at the seam layer: the verified side-effect path was openThreadDatabase → fireThreadTouch → scheduler.touch, which in a background SDK can hang a first-touch catch-up drain (queue claims, provider calls, writes) off a thread-view read. The fix is a reads-only operation scope in shared/context.ts — runWithThreadTouchSuppressed runs a function under the current instance seam with the touch announcement replaced by a no-op while preserving the poke target and view config (and delegating to the below-SDK defaults when no seam is in scope, minus the touch). thread-view pull and status wrap their entire bodies in this scope, which structurally covers not just their own openThreadDatabase calls but also the owners' report surfaces status consumes — no test-only bypass, no signature changes to the frozen messages/turns domains, and write paths are untouched so first-touch catch-up still works everywhere it should. A new background-mode test leg extends TC-1.2/TC-2.5: pending work is manufactured through a manual SDK, then a fresh background SDK pulls twice and reads status; it asserts work rows / form states / view rows / boundary unchanged (full below-SDK state snapshot), provider fake at zero calls, repeated pulls byte-identical via full-result hash, repeated status byte-identical, and pending work visible through the read itself — after settling the scheduler (timeout + drainSettled) so a wrongly-scheduled drain would surface. The regression test was proven live: with the suppression temporarily removed it fails (the catch-up drain fires), with the fix it passes.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:714:  summary: \"Latest implementor result reports SV-01-PULL-STATUS-001 fixed and ready for verification; acceptance requires a fresh verifier pass with no open findings.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:743:  summary: \"Story orchestration run started after orienting from 1 existing artifact(s).\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:749:  summary: \"Fresh story-lead provider turn executed without planner session resume.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:761:  summary: \"Story-lead selected run-implement.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:771:  summary: \"Story-lead recorded a durable self-note for a future planner turn.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:782:  summary: \"story-implement completed with outcome ready-for-verification and status ok.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:794:  summary: \"Fresh story-lead provider turn executed without planner session resume.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:806:  summary: \"Story-lead selected run-verify.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:816:  summary: \"Story-lead recorded a durable self-note for a future planner turn.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:827:  summary: \"story-verify completed with outcome revise and status ok.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:839:  summary: \"Fresh story-lead provider turn executed without planner session resume.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:851:  summary: \"Story-lead selected run-continue.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:861:  summary: \"Story-lead recorded a durable self-note for a future planner turn.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:872:  summary: \"story-continue completed with outcome ready-for-verification and status ok.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:884:  summary: \"Fresh story-lead provider turn executed without planner session resume.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:896:  summary: \"Story-lead selected run-verify.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:906:  summary: \"Story-lead recorded a durable self-note for a future planner turn.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:917:  summary: \"story-verify completed with outcome pass and status ok.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:1009:{\"action\":\"accept-story\",\"rationale\":\"...\",\"inputs\":{\"summary\":\"...\",\"acceptanceCheckRefs\":[\"...\"],\"acceptanceChecks\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":[\"...\"],\"reasoning\":\"...\"}],\"recommendedImplLeadAction\":\"accept\"},\"verification\":{\"finalVerifierOutcome\":\"pass\",\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"...\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":[\"...\"]}]}}\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:4:// Stories 3–5 extend the same per-event walk with projection, turn\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:30:// mocked transaction object.\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:48:function detail(cause: unknown): string {\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:70:    const placeholders = chunk.map(() => \"?\").join(\", \");\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:72:      .prepare(`SELECT idempotency_key FROM event WHERE idempotency_key IN (${placeholders})`)\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:73:      .all(...chunk) as unknown as Array<{ idempotency_key: string }>;\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:220:        // Turn transition before projection — the order is load-bearing: a\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:229:        // it can never drift from its source; a projection failure throws\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:323:      .all() as unknown as RawEventRow[];\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:331:          payload: JSON.parse(row.payload) as Record<string, unknown>,\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:334:        }) as unknown as EventRecord,\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:43:**Dependencies:** Stories 0–2. **Hard gate, verify before story start (extended per design):** (1) Epic 02's requeue patch landed — live-work-only queue rows, no terminal-row collision; (2) the terminal-failure write path verified against landed code — exhausted forms persist a classifiable reason class (FC-0.4 proved the fixture side; this gate proves the production side). If the persisted reason is opaque, the named Epic 02 patch is: stamp the provider's `retryable` flag onto the failed form at exhaustion.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:51:  - **TC-3.1** (AC-3.1, AC-3.2, AC-3.3): Seed a thread with ready, pending, transiently-failed, non-transiently-failed, and blocked forms (fixture-manufactured states); sweep → returns immediately; transient failure requeued (work row exists, form pending), non-transient and blocked untouched and reported, pending untouched; provider fake observes zero calls from the sweep itself.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:58:  - **TC-3.4** (AC-3.6, AC-2.7): Compact with default options → receipt includes sweep section; compact with skip → receipt records the skip and no requeues occurred; drain after the default compact → requeued form heals; next compact's view includes the healed form. *(The drain leg exercises Epic 02 machinery through the provider fake — the one sanctioned test-setup use of inference machinery; no Epic 03 operation touches it.)*\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:65:The sweep is thread-view's only *writing* interaction with other domains, and it writes nothing itself — every mutation goes through `messages.requeue`/`turns.requeue`. It is the repair half of the degrade-don't-block posture: compact degrades around missing material; the sweep is why the same material isn't missing at the *next* compact. This story also completes the compact receipt: Story 2's `absent` placeholder becomes `SweepReceipt | { skipped: true }`.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:69:Gate first — both legs verified and recorded in the story log before any code (requeue patch landed; reason-class persistence verified against landed Epic 02 code, with FC-0.4 as the fixture-side proof). Then the classification table as data with its own unit legs, then the walk/bucket/receipt as a pure function over report outputs, then the requeue calls, then the compact embed + skip flag. Red: `sweep` stub + compact receipt still `absent`.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:103:Zero-provider assertion completes here across all five ops (the fake is in fixture scope all around the sweep — this assert is what keeps it out of the operation). Once-per-invocation dedupe is structural (owner noop) but asserted anyway — if Epic 02's requeue ever stops nooping, this is the test that notices.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:107:Buckets come from the *owners' report joins*, not raw form states: \"retrying\" is a report-level distinction (pending + queue detail), and the sweep must not re-derive it from `derived_form` reads. The receipt's `requeued` carries subject ids so TC-3.4 can follow specific forms through heal. The classification table starts minimal (the design's named classes); unknown codes landing in `permanentFailed` with their literal reason is the receipt's visibility mechanism — expanding the table is config-tier work later, not a redesign.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:162:| TC-1.2 | 1.1, 1.7 | view-pull | two pulls with nothing between are byte-identical and create no work or provider calls | provider fake call-count assert |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:166:| TC-2.1 | 2.2, 2.3, 2.7 | view-compact | profile compact succeeds with config in receipt; 105% sum and unknown profile reject with named violations, thread unchanged | read-back equality after rejections |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:178:| TC-4.2 | 4.1, 4.2 | view-boundary | flipped: usable summary renders summary; failed renders truncation + marker; interleaved assistant text full | |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:197:| zero-provider sweep across all five ops | view-sweep | The provider fake is in scope for fixtures; nothing stops an internal \"helpful\" derivation call except this assert. The epic's no-inference rule needs teeth. |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:216:Per-chunk TDD tables follow Epic 02's pattern; estimates: Chunk 0 ≈ 6, 1 ≈ 9, 2 ≈ 16 (incl. goldens + restart), 3 ≈ 10, 4 ≈ 13, 5 ≈ 11 — ~65 total. Red exits on the project `red-verify` (no behavior tests); structured-result stubs make Red failures assertion-shaped on the surface ops. Green exits on `green-verify` with test immutability. The process suite runs at story completion (`verify-all`), not in Red/Green loops.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:228:- current_summary: Story orchestration started and durable state has been initialized.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:274:  summary: \"Orient from 1 existing story artifact(s).\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:299:  summary: \"Story orchestration run started after orienting from 1 existing artifact(s).\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:385:{\"action\":\"accept-story\",\"rationale\":\"...\",\"inputs\":{\"summary\":\"...\",\"acceptanceCheckRefs\":[\"...\"],\"acceptanceChecks\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":[\"...\"],\"reasoning\":\"...\"}],\"recommendedImplLeadAction\":\"accept\"},\"verification\":{\"finalVerifierOutcome\":\"pass\",\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"...\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":[\"...\"]}]}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/04-tool-result-visibility/003-implementor.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-implement\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"ready-for-verification\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"6d65c327-9aad-4a18-a6cf-9fcf0f21a486\",\"provider\":\"claude-code\",\"model\":\"claude-fable-5\",\"role\":\"story_implementor\",\"sessionId\":\"a19a2d2c-079f-4c8b-a6d9-08d7c8df8763\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"claude-code\",\"sessionId\":\"a19a2d2c-079f-4c8b-a6d9-08d7c8df8763\",\"storyId\":\"04-tool-result-visibility\"},\"outcome\":\"ready-for-verification\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"04-tool-result-visibility\",\"title\":\"Story 4: Tool-Result Visibility\"},\"planSummary\":\"Built the visibility boundary's advance: a pure `advanceDecision` (over-max trigger, oldest-first flips to target, whole-message floor join with oversized-newest protected alone) plus an executor that consumes Story 1's shared deleted-filtered zone SUM and writes the new position in its own short post-commit transaction with a position-forward guard. Wired it through the sanctioned intake→thread-view surface import: intake's pipeline registers `runPostCommitBoundaryAdvance` on ctx.onCommit FIRST (before the walk's enqueue pokes, so flush order is advance-then-poke), wrapped so a throwing advance is diagnosed to stderr and never eats the poke or reaches intake's caller. The advance runs in both host modes; budgets resolve through the per-instance seam (SdkViewConfig.visibility) with the 32000/24000/8000 defaults for direct domain calls. No host-called advance surface exists — the SDK ThreadViewSurface still carries only the five operations, and every test advance fires through a real intake commit. Boundary G1 trajectory golden committed with hand-derived positions ([0,0,9,9,27], zone sums [40,80,60,70,80] from exact-token 'tok'-word contents); it matched on first run, as did all 12 new boundary tests.\",\"changedFiles\":[{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/boundary.ts\",\"reason\":\"advanceDecision (pure), readZoneToolResults (same WHERE as visibilityZoneTokens so the advance/status sums cannot diverge), readCompactPoint, executeBoundaryAdvance (own short transaction, never-backward UPDATE guard)\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/index.ts\",\"reason\":\"runPostCommitBoundaryAdvance: fires the Story-0 injection point, resolves instance budgets via the seam (defaults below SDK), delegates to the executor; documented as seam-only, not a host operation\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts\",\"reason\":\"the one registration: advance registered first on ctx.onCommit (pokes register later during the walk, so flush runs advance-then-poke), catch+stderr-diagnose wrapper, sanctioned thread-view surface import with the cycle note\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts\",\"reason\":\"TC-4.1 through TC-4.6, seam isolation both directions, both-host-modes proof, deleted-filter consistency leg, budget-validation legs (new file)\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/test/view-select-golden.test.ts\",\"reason\":\"sanctioned amendment: Boundary G1 trajectory golden case plus TC-4.5 replay-equality leg (second fresh thread, same script, same trajectory)\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/test/goldens/boundary-g1-trajectory.json\",\"reason\":\"committed trajectory golden: budgets 100/60/30, five scripted batches, hand-derived expected positions and zone sums including both floor legs (new file)\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/test/goldens/README.md\",\"reason\":\"golden table row for boundary-g1-trajectory.json\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/test/red-manifest.json\",\"reason\":\"recorded hashes for the new test file, the amended golden suite, and the new golden JSON\"}],\"tests\":{\"added\":[\"test/view-boundary.test.ts (12 tests: TC-4.1, TC-4.2, TC-4.3 ×2 legs, TC-4.4, TC-4.5 ×2 validation legs, TC-4.6, poke-failure isolation, deleted-filter consistency, both-modes ×2)\",\"test/goldens/boundary-g1-trajectory.json\"],\"modified\":[\"test/view-select-golden.test.ts (added Boundary G1 trajectory + replay-equality test)\",\"test/goldens/README.md\",\"test/red-manifest.json\"],\"removed\":[],\"totalAfterStory\":286,\"deltaFromPriorBaseline\":13},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"pnpm run green-verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm run verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"selfReview\":{\"passesRun\":0,\"findingsFixed\":[\"console.error in src/ violated the project lint rule (no console in src/; CLI output flows through render) — switched the advance-failure diagnostic to process.stderr.write\",\"TC-4.2 originally reached the provider double through sdk.config.provider with a cast — restructured to hold the double directly at construction\",\"DoD's deleted-filter consistency line had no direct test — added a leg that deletes a zone result and proves both the live status sum and the next advance decide over the filtered population\"],\"findingsSurfaced\":[\"The registration lives in src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts (where the operation context and commit hooks are built), not literally in src/domains/intake-stream/index.ts as the story's Implementation Targets table names; the tech design's requirement is that intake-stream registers it, which pipeline.ts is — index.ts is a thin delegation layer with no ctx in scope. Registration is placed before the event walk because enqueue registers pokes during the walk; registration order is flush order, which is what pins advance-first-poke-second.\",\"sdk.ts's `export * as threadView` re-exports the whole domain surface, so runPostCommitBoundaryAdvance is technically importable by a host (same as messages.createFromEvent and every other cross-domain surface function under the established pattern). The SDK's ThreadViewSurface and CLI expose only the five operations, satisfying the anti-shim rule's intent; no test calls it.\",\"A throwing fallback poke after a successful commit still turns intake's reported result into a storage_failure (pre-existing Epic 02 flush behavior, observable in the poke-isolation test which therefore asserts only the advance and the committed events). Not this story's scope; noting for the record.\",\"Compact reset can legally move the boundary backward to the compact point (new window per AC-4.6's 'within the same compact window' qualifier) — the never-backward UPDATE guard applies only to the advance's write path, matching the design.\"]},\"openQuestions\":[],\"specDeviations\":[],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"Proceed to verification, then Story 5 (render targets), which closes the named debt this story carries: the process-boundary CLI leg of the both-modes advance proof (spawned CLI intake on an over-max thread → flipped pulls, zone ≤ target) in cli-process-view.test.ts.\"},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/04-tool-result-visibility/003-implementor.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-11T17:28:45.770Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-11T17:45:43.057Z\"}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/001-current.json:1:{\"storyRunId\":\"00-foundation-story-run-001\",\"storyId\":\"00-foundation\",\"attempt\":1,\"status\":\"needs-ruling\",\"lifecycleState\":\"terminal\",\"currentSummary\":\"Terminal story-lead package is ready for impl-lead review.\",\"currentPhase\":\"terminal\",\"currentChildOperation\":null,\"latestArtifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"validation-result\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/00-foundation/001-story-validate.json\",\"provenance\":\"prior-run\"},{\"kind\":\"implementor-result\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/00-foundation/003-implementor.json\",\"provenance\":\"current-run\"},{\"kind\":\"verifier-result\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/00-foundation/004-verify.json\",\"provenance\":\"current-run\"},{\"kind\":\"final-package\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/001-final-package.json\",\"provenance\":\"current-run\"},{\"kind\":\"ruling-response\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/001-ruling-response-001.json\",\"provenance\":\"caller-input\"}],\"latestContinuationHandles\":{\"storyImplementor\":{\"provider\":\"claude-code\",\"sessionId\":\"9b79ae20-893f-4407-8201-b760b8487b13\",\"storyId\":\"00-foundation\"},\"storyVerifier\":{\"provider\":\"codex\",\"sessionId\":\"019eb712-e23a-79c0-86a3-b165e5a90711\",\"storyId\":\"00-foundation\"}},\"latestEventSequence\":20,\"callerInputHistory\":{\"reviewRequests\":[],\"rulings\":[{\"rulingRequestId\":\"00-foundation-story-run-001-ruling-spec-deviation\",\"decision\":\"approve\",\"rationale\":\"Both declared deviations approved by impl-lead. (1) ViewProfileOverride[] widening of SdkViewConfig.profiles is required to express FC-0.2's unknown-built-in-override-target violation and keeps complete ViewProfile assignable. (2) strftime seed timestamp in static migration SQL is a one-time seed; deterministic-clock requirements apply to production advance/reset writers (Stories 2/4), which use the injected clock. No behavior or contract drift.\",\"source\":\"impl-lead\"}]},\"nextIntent\":{\"actionType\":\"await-ruling\",\"summary\":\"Pause for caller ruling before impl-lead acceptance.\",\"artifactRef\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/001-final-package.json\"},\"replayBoundary\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-06-11T14:32:54.790Z\"}\npackages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/registry.ts:84:    .get(threadId) as unknown as RawRow | undefined;\npackages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/registry.ts:93:    .all() as unknown as RawRow[];\npackages/lhc/test/cli-process-mutations-delete.test.ts:102:async function readBack(filePath: string): Promise<unknown> {\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/00-foundation/streams/004-verify.stdout.log:11:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_4\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/00-foundation.md | sed -n '1,500p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t# Story 0: Foundation\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t### Summary\\n     4\\t<!-- Jira: Summary field -->\\n     5\\tMigration v6 (view, band, boundary tables), profile config parsing and validation, the advance-seam injection point, and the derived-thread fixture every later story compacts against.\\n     6\\t\\n     7\\t### Description\\n     8\\t<!-- Jira: Description field -->\\n     9\\t\\n    10\\t**User Profile (from epic):** the agentic harness (PI extension first), calling through the SDK on every model call; and the agent/operator running compacts and checking thread health through the CLI.\\n    11\\t\\n    12\\t**Objective:** establish the storage, config, and test substrate for the thread-view domain so Stories 1–5 build operations, not plumbing.\\n    13\\t\\n    14\\t**Scope in:**\\n    15\\t- Migration v6: `thread_view` (singleton row, CHECK-enforced), `thread_view_band`, `view_boundary` (singleton, seeded to position 0) — per tech design §Storage\\n    16\\t- Profile config: built-ins (`continuation`, `conversation`, `coding`), user profiles merged by name, band-sum and budget validation (`max > target ≥ floor`) with caller errors naming the violation\\n    17\\t- The test injection facility — one mechanism, two named points: the post-commit advance (TC-4.6's failure injection) and compact's write path between sweep and view write (TC-2.4's crash injection); production code carries the points as no-ops unless a test installs a hook\\n    18\\t- The derived-thread fixture: a recorded conversation (~12 turns, 4 chunks, tool-heavy middle) drained through real Epic 02 machinery into known form states — ready, failed-transient, failed-permanent, blocked — plus a canonical-corruption variant (Epic 01 fixture pattern) and a turnless-straggler variant (selection rule 6 / golden G4)\\n    19\\t- Sanctioned below-SDK fixture helpers in `test/fixtures/` (boundary-row seeding for TC-1.4; same sanctioning as the corruption fixture)\\n    20\\t\\n    21\\t**Scope out:** any thread-view operation; any rendering.\\n    22\\t\\n    23\\t**Dependencies:** Epic 02 schema (v5) as the migration baseline.\\n    24\\t\\n    25\\t### Acceptance Criteria\\n    26\\t<!-- Jira: Acceptance Criteria field -->\\n    27\\t\\n    28\\tFoundation criteria (owns no epic ACs):\\n    29\\t\\n    30\\t- **FC-0.1**: Migration v6 applies cleanly to an Epic-02 thread file; all three tables exist with their CHECK constraints; `view_boundary` is seeded with position 0; re-applying is a no-op.\\n    31\\t- **FC-0.2**: Invalid profile configs are rejected at SDK construction with errors naming the violation (band sum ≠ 100, `max ≤ target`, `target < floor`, non-positive lower bound, unknown built-in override target).\\n    32\\t- **FC-0.3**: Each fixture state (ready, failed-transient, failed-permanent, blocked) is proven by read-back through the owning domain's report surface before any downstream story consumes it; states are reached through production drains against the deterministic provider, never hand-written rows.\\n    33\\t- **FC-0.4**: The fixture's failed-transient and failed-permanent forms carry distinguishable reason classes on read-back (the Story 3 classification dependency, proven here).\\n    34\\t- **FC-0.5**: The corruption-variant fixture refuses canonical reads with `state_corruption`; the turnless-straggler variant carries a `turnId = null` message between two turns and one after the last turn.\\n    35\\t- **FC-0.6**: The injection facility exists with both named points — post-commit advance and compact write path — reachable from tests without touching production code paths; uninstalled, both points are no-ops.\\n    36\\t\\n    37\\t### Technical Design\\n    38\\t<!-- Jira: Technical Notes or sub-section of Description -->\\n    39\\t\\n    40\\t#### Architecture Context\\n    41\\t\\n    42\\tThread-view is a consumer at the top of the existing stack: it reads the record and Epic 02's derived forms, owns three new tables in the same thread file, and derives nothing. This story builds the substrate — storage, config, injection facility, fixture — so Stories 1–5 build operations. Nothing here is reachable from the SDK surface yet.\\n    43\\t\\n    44\\t#### Build Strategy\\n    45\\t\\n    46\\tMigration first (it gates everything), then profiles (pure functions, no IO), then the injection facility, then the fixture — the fixture is the long pole and consumes everything before it (it drains real Epic 02 work against the deterministic provider and must read states back through `messages.report`/`turns.report`). Red phase: FC checks written against the unmigrated/unconfigured package fail on missing tables and missing exports, not on import errors.\\n    47\\t\\n    48\\t#### Implementation Targets\\n    49\\t\\n    50\\t| Target | Work |\\n    51\\t|--------|------|\\n    52\\t| `src/shared/migrations.ts` (existing chain) | v6: `thread_view`, `thread_view_band`, `view_boundary` + seed boundary row at position 0 |\\n    53\\t| `src/domains/thread-view/internal/profiles.ts` | built-ins (`continuation` 120k/30/30/20/20, `conversation` 120k/12/48/20/20, `coding` 120k/25/35/20/20), merge-by-name, validation errors naming violations |\\n    54\\t| `src/shared/view.ts` | the vocabulary types (`ViewProfile`, `VisibilityBudgets`, `SdkViewConfig`, receipts — copy-paste from design §Interface Definitions) |\\n    55\\t| `src/sdk.ts` | `SdkConfig.view` accepted + validated at construction (throws on nonsense, Epic 02 rule); defaults 32000/24000/8000, threshold 160000 |\\n    56\\t| test injection facility | two named points: post-commit advance, compact write path; no-op unless a test installs a hook; lives with the seam utilities, pattern from Epic 02's crash-injection seam |\\n    57\\t| `test/fixtures/` | derived-thread fixture builder + boundary-seed helper (sanctioned below-SDK, marker comment) + corruption variant + turnless-straggler variant |\\n    58\\t\\n    59\\t#### Design References\\n    60\\t\\n    61\\t| Topic | Where |\\n    62\\t|-------|-------|\\n    63\\t| Storage DDL, singleton CHECKs, seeding, provenance rationale | tech-design.md L135–168 |\\n    64\\t| Profile/budget shapes and defaults | tech-design.md L302–307 (`ViewProfile`, `VisibilityBudgets`), L354–364 (`SdkViewConfig`, built-ins) |\\n    65\\t| Boundary-rules addition + sanctioned cycle (check-boundaries) | tech-design.md L115 |\\n    66\\t| Fixture composition, production-path state manufacture | tech-design.md L366–372; test-plan.md L5–16 |\\n    67\\t| Turnless-straggler variant purpose (G4) | tech-design.md L183; test-plan.md L72 |\\n    68\\t\\n    69\\t#### Test Mapping\\n    70\\t\\n    71\\t| Check | Test file | Asserts |\\n    72\\t|-------|-----------|---------|\\n    73\\t| FC-0.1 | `test/view-fixture.test.ts` + `thread-migration.test.ts` | v6 applies to an Epic-02 file; tables + CHECKs exist; boundary seeded 0; re-apply no-op |\\n    74\\t| FC-0.2 | `view-fixture.test.ts` | each invalid config rejected at construction with the named violation (sum≠100, max≤target, target<floor, bound≤0, unknown override) |\\n    75\\t| FC-0.3 | `view-fixture.test.ts` | each state (ready/failed-transient/failed-permanent/blocked) read back through the owning report surface |\\n    76\\t| FC-0.4 | `view-fixture.test.ts` | transient vs permanent forms carry distinguishable reason classes on read-back |\\n    77\\t| FC-0.5 | `view-fixture.test.ts` | corruption variant refuses canonical reads with `state_corruption`; straggler variant has `turnId=null` between turns and trailing |\\n    78\\t| FC-0.6 | `view-fixture.test.ts` | both injection points reachable from tests; uninstalled ⇒ no-ops |\\n    79\\t\\n    80\\t#### Architecture-Risk Tests\\n    81\\t\\n    82\\tNone owned; this story *creates* the fixture-fidelity guarantee every later architecture-risk test stands on (states via production drains, never hand-written rows — FC-0.3 is the enforcement).\\n    83\\t\\n    84\\t#### Technical Notes\\n    85\\t\\n    86\\tThe fixture conversation shape is pinned in the design (~12 turns, 4 chunks, tool-heavy middle): the tool-heavy middle is what gives Story 4 a realistic over-max zone, and the 4 chunks give Story 2's coverage edge something to exclude. Scripted provider failures manufacture the failed states (retryable-fail-exhaust for transient; non-retryable for permanent); blocked comes from source damage on a sacrificial sibling fixture, not the main one. FC-0.4 is the Story 3 gate's fixture-side proof — if it can't pass because Epic 02's persisted reason is opaque, stop and surface it immediately; that's the named Epic 02 patch trigger, not something to work around.\\n    87\\t\\n    88\\t#### Anti-Shim Requirements\\n    89\\t\\n    90\\tFixture states must be reached through real `intake → drain` paths against the deterministic provider. Hand-writing `derived_form` rows to fake a state is the exact fiction FC-0.3 exists to prevent — a hand-written row can encode a state shape the production writer never produces, and every downstream test would then prove compatibility with fiction. The boundary-seed helper is the one sanctioned below-SDK write, and only because boundary *mechanics* are Story 4's to prove.\\n    91\\t\\n    92\\t#### Production Path Proof\\n    93\\t\\n    94\\tMigration runs through the real chain (`thread-migration.test.ts` extension, same as v1–v5). Profile validation runs through real `createSdk` construction, not a standalone validator call.\\n    95\\t\\n    96\\t#### Verification\\n    97\\t\\n    98\\t`pnpm verify` (lint + typecheck + default suites). New tests land in the default suite; no process-suite involvement this story.\\n    99\\t\\n   100\\t#### Spec Deviations\\n   101\\t\\n   102\\tNone.\\n   103\\t\\n   104\\t### Definition of Done\\n   105\\t<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n   106\\t\\n   107\\t- [ ] FC-0.1–FC-0.6 green in `test/view-fixture.test.ts` (~6 checks)\\n   108\\t- [ ] Migration registered in the chain after v5; `thread-migration.test.ts` extended for v6\\n   109\\t- [ ] check-boundaries script gains thread-view's allowed-import lines and intake-stream's thread-view-surface line with the sanctioned-cycle annotation (tech design §Module Boundaries)\\n   110\\t- [ ] Fixture helpers live in `test/fixtures/` with the sanctioned below-SDK marker comment\\n   111\\t- [ ] `verify` green\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/00-foundation/streams/004-verify.stdout.log:12:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_3\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md | sed -n '1,500p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t# Epic 03: Thread Views and Smart Compact — Tech Design\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t**Status:** Draft, complete (companion test plan: `test-plan.md`)\\n     4\\t\\n     5\\tConsumed by: BA/SM (story sharding), Tech Lead (story technical sections), implementing agents (interface and mechanism authority). Epic: `epic.md` (38 ACs, 27 TCs, five flows). Tech arch: `../01-tech-arch.md`. Domain design: `../../01-onboard/02-domain-design.md`. Epic 02 surfaces: `../02-derivation-pipeline/tech-design.md`.\\n     6\\t\\n     7\\t---\\n     8\\t\\n     9\\t## Context\\n    10\\t\\n    11\\tEpics 01 and 02 built a thread record that knows things and a derivation pipeline that summarizes them, and neither produces anything a model can be prompted with. The record holds events, messages, turns, chunks; the pipeline lands seven kinds of derived form beside them. What a harness needs is one assembled artifact: the conversation, arranged as a fidelity gradient, sized to a budget, in the shape its provider API takes. This epic builds that artifact — the thread view — and the four operations around it: pull, compact, sweep, and the visibility boundary that keeps the live tail from drowning in tool output.\\n    12\\t\\n    13\\tTwo cost structures dominate the design, and they pull in the same direction: do nothing per-turn. The pull sits on the hot path between the user's action and the model call, so it must be reads and string assembly — every judgment (which chunk in which band, which tool result short) was made earlier by an explicit operation. And the harness caches its prompt prefix; every byte that changes above the newest content is money. The MVP's tool-result truncation re-decided every result's visibility on every message — the prefix churned every turn, which at Opus-class pricing is roughly $0.15 per turn, forever. The replacement design changes the prompt only at discrete, attributable events: a compact (explicit, rare), or a boundary advance (batched, budget-triggered). Between those events, identical pulls return identical bytes.\\n    14\\t\\n    15\\tThe view is a snapshot, not a projection-on-read. A compact selects the band arrangement, renders each band's text from stored artifacts, and stores the rendered snapshot; pulls serve those bytes verbatim until the next compact. Record mutations and repairs land in the record immediately and become visible at the next compact — this was settled deliberately in the epic round (edit-then-recompact, no live view patching, no force-refresh) because curation is an occasional batch act, not a runtime channel. The one self-acting piece is the boundary: old tool results in the tail age to short form in batches when a budget breaks, because tool bloat accumulates without anyone deciding it.\\n    16\\t\\n    17\\tThe design leans entirely on Epic 02's machinery and adds no derivation of its own. Band material is `derived_form` rows; health reads are the owners' `report` surfaces; repair is the owners' `requeue`; the post-commit trigger is the instance seam from epic-fix-001. One Epic 02 dependency is in flight at design time: the requeue patch (live-work-only queue rows) — Story 3 gates on it. The Epic 02 deviation table was read at design time; the in-flight fix batch (backoff wake, tool-run grouping) improves what this epic consumes but changes no interface this design binds to.\\n    18\\t\\n    19\\t## Spec Validation\\n    20\\t\\n    21\\tEpic 03 validated clean for design: every AC maps to implementation work, contracts are complete, edge TCs exist (corruption refusal, advance failure, monster turn, never-compacted thread). Design-time entries:\\n    22\\t\\n    23\\t| Issue | Spec Location | Resolution | Status |\\n    24\\t|-------|---------------|------------|--------|\\n    25\\t| Transient classification basis | AC-3.3, epic TD-Q9 | By **reason-code classification table** (per TD-Q9), owned by `sweep.ts`: rate-limit / timeout / provider-unavailable classes ⇒ transient; content-refusal / validation / `unknown_work_kind` ⇒ permanent; **unclassified codes ⇒ permanent** (reported in the receipt as unclassified, never requeued — the conservative default; the other way re-spends on a permanent failure at every compact). Attempt count distinguishes only retrying-vs-exhausted, never repairability. Dependency: exhausted forms must persist the final failure's reason class, not a bare retry-exhausted marker — the Story 0 fixture proves the two failed states carry distinguishable codes; if Epic 02's persisted reason is opaque, that is an Epic 02 patch named at the Story 3 gate. | Resolved — clarified |\\n    26\\t| Boundary advance in manual mode | AC-4.9 (\\\"automatic\\\") | The advance runs in **both** host modes: it registers on `ctx.onCommit` and executes synchronously at flush. Unlike the drain (inference, background-only), the advance is cheap and deterministic — a CLI intake must advance the boundary too, or CLI-driven threads bloat. \\\"Automatic\\\" means SDK-internal, not background-mode-only. | Resolved — clarified |\\n    27\\t| Brief band cannot always hold all remaining history | AC-2.4 sizing vs degrade-never-omit | The view has a **coverage edge**: oldest chunks beyond the brief budget are outside the view, recorded as `coveredFrom` on the view and in the receipt. This is the window's edge made explicit and reported — not a silent omission (the record keeps everything; inspect reaches it). | Resolved — clarified |\\n    28\\t| Band context messages need a role | AC-5.1 | Rendered as `user`-role messages with band-marker headers. Provider APIs reject unknown roles; `system` placement is harness-owned; `user` is what the MVP's injection used and what PI session files accept anywhere. | Resolved — clarified |\\n    29\\t\\n    30\\t## System View\\n    31\\t\\n    32\\tThe thread-view domain is a consumer at the top of the existing stack. Everything below it already exists; this epic adds the shaded surface and its storage:\\n    33\\t\\n    34\\t```mermaid\\n    35\\tflowchart TD\\n    36\\t    H[Harness / PI extension] -->|pull, status| TV[thread-view surface]\\n    37\\t    OP[Operator / agent via CLI] -->|compact, sweep, materialize| TV\\n    38\\t    TV -->|report, requeue| M[messages surface]\\n    39\\t    TV -->|report, requeue| T[turns surface]\\n    40\\t    TV -->|reads| DF[(derived_form rows)]\\n    41\\t    TV -->|reads| REC[(messages / turns / chunks)]\\n    42\\t    TV -->|owns| VS[(thread_view + view_boundary tables)]\\n    43\\t    IN[intake-stream] -.->|onCommit: advance check| TV\\n    44\\t    M & T -->|queue work| Q[(work_item)]\\n    45\\t```\\n    46\\t\\n    47\\tOne thread file holds all of it — the view tables live beside the record they render, so a thread file remains self-contained and snapshot-portable (tech arch). The harness's two calls (`pull`, `status`) are hot-path; everything else is operator-paced.\\n    48\\t\\n    49\\t### External Contracts\\n    50\\t\\n    51\\t**The pull result is the product.** What crosses the boundary to the harness:\\n    52\\t\\n    53\\t| Data | Shape | Consumer | Notes |\\n    54\\t|------|-------|----------|-------|\\n    55\\t| Pull result | `ViewMessage[]` + `ViewMeta` | PI extension context hook | Bands as labeled `user` messages, then tail in record order |\\n    56\\t| Status | `ViewStatus` | Extension turn-boundary checks, operators | Numbers only; the caller owns policy |\\n    57\\t| Compact receipt | `CompactReceipt` | Operator, extension logging | One JSON receipt; no streaming |\\n    58\\t| Sweep receipt | `SweepReceipt` | Operator, compact embedding | Per owner/kind/state accounting |\\n    59\\t| Materialized file | PI session JSONL | Closed harnesses, inspection | Format pinned below from PI source |\\n    60\\t\\n    61\\t**PI session file format** (pinned from `repo-ref/pi/packages/coding-agent/src/core/session-manager.ts`): JSONL; line 1 is the header `{ type: \\\"session\\\", version, id, timestamp, cwd }`; each subsequent line is `{ type: \\\"message\\\", id, parentId, timestamp, message: { role, content } }` with `parentId` chaining each entry to the previous. All generated fields derive from view metadata (AC-5.2): `id` from the thread id + view created-at, timestamps from view/message record times, never `Date.now()`. The conformance fixture is a structure-trimmed real PI session file checked into `test/fixtures/`.\\n    62\\t\\n    63\\t**Error contract** (inherited vocabulary, no new classes): `caller_error` (bad profile, bad budgets, unknown thread), `state_corruption` (canonical span unreadable at compact — AC-2.5), `system_error` (storage failures). All operations return `OpResult`; programmer errors at construction throw (Epic 02 rule).\\n    64\\t\\n    65\\t**Runtime prerequisites:** unchanged from Epic 02 — Node with `node:sqlite`, no new dependencies. No provider is required by any Epic 03 operation; the CLI view commands must work with no provider configured (they never call one).\\n    66\\t\\n    67\\t**CLI grammar** (full flag surface, Epic 01/02 convention):\\n    68\\t\\n    69\\t```\\n    70\\tlhc view pull        --file-path <p> | --thread-id <id>   [--json]\\n    71\\tlhc view status      --file-path <p> | --thread-id <id>   [--json]\\n    72\\tlhc view compact     --file-path <p> | --thread-id <id>   [--profile <name>]\\n    73\\t                     [--lower-bound <n>] [--full <n>] [--smooth <n>] [--detailed <n>] [--brief <n>]\\n    74\\t                     [--no-sweep] [--json]\\n    75\\tlhc view sweep       --file-path <p> | --thread-id <id>   [--json]\\n    76\\tlhc view materialize --file-path <p> | --thread-id <id>   --out <path> [--format pi-session]\\n    77\\t```\\n    78\\t\\n    79\\tBand flags override profile values field-wise (AC-2.2); validation errors name the violated constraint (AC-2.3). Visibility budgets are SDK config; no per-invocation CLI flags for them in this epic.\\n    80\\t\\n    81\\t## Module Boundaries\\n    82\\t\\n    83\\t### Top-Tier Surfaces\\n    84\\t\\n    85\\t| Surface | Source | This Epic's Role |\\n    86\\t|---------|--------|------------------|\\n    87\\t| `thread-view` | Tech arch (named, empty until now) | The epic's home: all five operations |\\n    88\\t| `messages`, `turns` | Inherited | Read-only consumers: report/requeue surfaces, record reads. **No changes to either domain.** |\\n    89\\t| `intake-stream` | Inherited | One additive touch: registers the advance check on `ctx.onCommit` (mirror of Epic 02's poke registration) |\\n    90\\t| `sdk.ts` / `cli/` | Inherited | SDK gains the `threadView` namespace + view config; CLI gains `lhc view *` commands |\\n    91\\t\\n    92\\t### Placement\\n    93\\t\\n    94\\t```\\n    95\\tsrc/\\n    96\\t  sdk.ts                          ← gains: threadView surface assembly; SdkConfig.view (profiles, budgets, threshold)\\n    97\\t  domains/\\n    98\\t    intake-stream/index.ts        ← gains: one onCommit registration (advance check), beside the existing poke\\n    99\\t    thread-view/\\n   100\\t      index.ts                    ← NEW: surface — pull, compact, sweep, status, materialize\\n   101\\t      internal/\\n   102\\t        select.ts                 ← NEW: band selection walk (deterministic arrangement from record + forms)\\n   103\\t        render.ts                 ← NEW: band text rendering, degrade ladders, subject keys, tail formatting\\n   104\\t        snapshot.ts               ← NEW: thread_view/thread_view_band row IO; atomic replace\\n   105\\t        boundary.ts               ← NEW: visibility boundary row IO; advance check; compact reset\\n   106\\t        sweep.ts                  ← NEW: report walk, transient classification, requeue calls, receipt\\n   107\\t        profiles.ts               ← NEW: built-in profiles; config resolution; validation\\n   108\\t        materialize.ts            ← NEW: PI session JSONL writer\\n   109\\t  cli/\\n   110\\t    view.ts                       ← NEW: lhc view pull|compact|sweep|status|materialize\\n   111\\t  shared/\\n   112\\t    view.ts                       ← NEW: view vocabulary (types below) — shared so cli/sdk/tests import one home\\n   113\\t```\\n   114\\t\\n   115\\tBoundary rules, one addition: `thread-view` imports `messages`/`turns` through their `index.ts` surfaces only, never internals; nothing imports `thread-view/internal`; **and `intake-stream` imports the `thread-view` surface** (the advance registration, Flow 4) — sanctioned by the surface-call rule, named here so Story 0's boundary gate expects it. The check-boundaries script gains both lines: thread-view's allowed imports, and intake-stream's added thread-view-surface line. Note for the script: this creates the domain graph's first surface-level cycle (intake → thread-view → messages ← intake) — runtime-safe (registration-then-flush, no import-time execution), but if the script models a DAG it needs a sanctioned-cycle annotation, not a silent pass.\\n   116\\t\\n   117\\t### Module Responsibility Matrix\\n   118\\t-0.x fixture invariants (each manufactured state proven by read-back; states reached through production drains) live in `view-fixture.test.ts` and run before everything in CI order.\\n\\n## Architecture-Risk Tests\\n\\nBeyond TC mapping — each exists because the architecture creates a hazard the ACs don't name:\\n\\n| Test | File | Hazard it guards |\\n|------|------|------------------|\\n| zero-provider sweep across all five ops | view-sweep | The provider fake is in scope for fixtures; nothing stops an internal \\\"helpful\\\" derivation call except this assert. The epic's no-inference rule needs teeth. |\\n| selection replay goldens (3 cases below) | view-select-golden | AC-2.9 says deterministic; only exact-arrangement goldens catch tie-breaker drift (≤ vs <, newest-first ordering) that replay-on-same-engine misses. |\\n| boundary trajectory golden | view-select-golden | Same: floor/target arithmetic off-by-one survives property tests, not goldens. |\\n| advance/poke seam isolation | view-boundary | TC-4.6's sibling: a *throwing* advance must not eat the queue poke (drain still runs), and a failing poke must not block the advance. Ordering pinned in design Flow 4. |\\n| restart serves snapshot | view-compact | Snapshot durability: compact, close SDK, reopen thread file fresh, pull → identical bytes. Real-file restart, not same-process reread. |\\n| coverage edge accounting | view-compact | When brief budget excludes old chunks: `covered_from` correct, receipt reports exclusion, no silent omission *and* no phantom gap entries for out-of-window chunks. |\\n| CLI parity: compact/status/sweep | cli-process-view | Scope promises five CLI commands; spawned legs: `view compact --profile` (receipt JSON = SDK shape), `view status` (status JSON = SDK shape), `view sweep` (receipt JSON = SDK shape), plus profile-violation exit-nonzero leg. Closes the gap between claimed CLI surface and proven CLI surface. |\\n| CLI intake advances boundary | cli-process-view | The design's both-modes advance rule proven at the process boundary: spawned CLI intake on an over-max thread → subsequent `view pull` shows flipped results, `view status` shows zone ≤ target. Guards the seam-install class (a createSdk-only install would pass every in-process test and fail this one). |\\n\\n## Golden Cases\\n\\n**Selection G1 — proportions:** fixture thread, `conversation` profile (120k/12/48/20/20 scaled down by fixture factor): exact expected arrangement (subject ids per band, compact point, covered_from) checked against committed JSON golden.\\n**Selection G2 — budget-edge inclusion:** a turn whose rendering exactly fills the smooth remainder → included (≤ rule); one token over → excluded and band stops.\\n**Selection G3 — oversized loner:** single turn larger than the whole smooth budget on an otherwise-empty band → included alone (empty-band exception).\\n**Selection G4 — turnless straggler:** fixture variant with a runtime note between `turn_end` and the next prompt, compacted so the note's neighborhood lands in a band → note rides the following turn's band entry (rule 6: `[inter-turn note]` marker before the entry, its tokens counted in that turn's fill cost); trailing-straggler leg: a note after the last turn → tail.\\n**Boundary G1 — trajectory:** scripted intake sequence (sums crossing max twice, one monster turn) → committed expected positions after each batch. Floor legs (whole-message rule): protected set = newest tool results joined until the set's sum first reaches/exceeds floor; an oversized newest result is protected alone and the zone legally sits above target (or max) that batch; boundary never lands inside the protected set; at least the newest result is full whenever any exists.\\n\\n## Chunk Red/Green Detail\\n\\nPer-chunk TDD tables follow Epic 02's pattern; estimates: Chunk 0 ≈ 6, 1 ≈ 9, 2 ≈ 16 (incl. goldens + restart), 3 ≈ 10, 4 ≈ 13, 5 ≈ 11 — ~65 total. Red exits on the project `red-verify` (no behavior tests); structured-result stubs make Red failures assertion-shaped on the surface ops. Green exits on `green-verify` with test immutability. The process suite runs at story completion (`verify-all`), not in Red/Green loops.\\n\\nSuite labels for `verify-all` accounting: default suites `ran`; process suite `ran` under flag; no absent/skipped suites in this epic.\\n\",\"numLines\":80,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":80}}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/streams/004-implementor.stdout.log:64:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_018A8bkh145AXniSjhPbvhVM\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\t// thread-view surface (Epic 03): pull, status, compact, sweep, materialize.\\n2\\t// Story 1 lands the skeleton with `pull` and `status` real — the hot-path\\n3\\t// reads: local reads and deterministic string assembly only, no inference,\\n4\\t// no network, no queue interaction, no writes (AC-1.1, AC-2.8). The other\\n5\\t// three are structured-result stubs until their stories (2, 3, 5) land.\\n6\\t// Story 0's substrate (profile resolution, consumed by createSdk) re-exports\\n7\\t// at the bottom.\\n8\\timport { existsSync } from \\\"node:fs\\\";\\n9\\timport {\\n10\\t  resolveInstanceViewConfig,\\n11\\t  runWithThreadTouchSuppressed,\\n12\\t} from \\\"../../shared/context.js\\\";\\n13\\timport type { FormReportEntry } from \\\"../../shared/derivation.js\\\";\\n14\\timport { storageFailure, type ErrorResult, type OpResult } from \\\"../../shared/errors.js\\\";\\n15\\timport type {\\n16\\t  CompactReceipt,\\n17\\t  PullResult,\\n18\\t  ResolvedViewConfig,\\n19\\t  SweepReceipt,\\n20\\t  ViewCompactParams,\\n21\\t  ViewMessage,\\n22\\t  ViewProfile,\\n23\\t  ViewStatus,\\n24\\t} from \\\"../../shared/view.js\\\";\\n25\\timport * as messagesDomain from \\\"../messages/index.js\\\";\\n26\\timport * as turnsDomain from \\\"../turns/index.js\\\";\\n27\\timport {\\n28\\t  openThreadDatabase,\\n29\\t  resolveThreadRef,\\n30\\t  type ThreadRef,\\n31\\t} from \\\"../threads/index.js\\\";\\n32\\timport { readBoundaryPosition, visibilityZoneTokens } from \\\"./internal/boundary.js\\\";\\n33\\timport { profileViolation, resolveViewConfig } from \\\"./internal/profiles.js\\\";\\n34\\timport {\\n35\\t  assembleBandText,\\n36\\t  renderBandMessage,\\n37\\t  renderTailMessage,\\n38\\t  toolNamesByCallId,\\n39\\t} from \\\"./internal/render.js\\\";\\n40\\timport { fireViewInjection } from \\\"./internal/seam.js\\\";\\n41\\timport {\\n42\\t  CanonicalCorruptionError,\\n43\\t  readSelectionInputs,\\n44\\t  selectArrangement,\\n45\\t  type ArrangementEntry,\\n46\\t} from \\\"./internal/select.js\\\";\\n47\\timport {\\n48\\t  readReadyToolResultSummaries,\\n49\\t  readTailMessages,\\n50\\t  readViewSnapshot,\\n51\\t  replaceViewSnapshot,\\n52\\t  tailTokenSum,\\n53\\t} from \\\"./internal/snapshot.js\\\";\\n54\\timport { estimateTokens } from \\\"../../tech-utils/token-counting/index.js\\\";\\n55\\timport type { Band } from \\\"../../shared/view.js\\\";\\n56\\t\\n57\\t// Config resolution for the operation in hand: the SDK instance's resolved\\n58\\t// view config rides the per-instance seam (epic-fix-001 pattern, tech design\\n59\\t// Flow 4); below-SDK direct domain calls fall back to the built-in defaults\\n60\\t// through the same one resolution path createSdk uses.\\n61\\tconst DEFAULT_VIEW_CONFIG: ResolvedViewConfig = resolveViewConfig();\\n62\\t\\n63\\tfunction viewConfig(): ResolvedViewConfig {\\n64\\t  return resolveInstanceViewConfig() ?? DEFAULT_VIEW_CONFIG;\\n65\\t}\\n66\\t\\n67\\tfunction threadNotFound(filePath: string): { ok: false; error: ErrorResult } {\\n68\\t  return {\\n69\\t    ok: false,\\n70\\t    error: {\\n71\\t      errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n72\\t      code: \\\"thread_not_found\\\",\\n73\\t      reason: `no thread file exists at ${filePath}`,\\n74\\t    },\\n75\\t  };\\n76\\t}\\n77\\t\\n78\\tfunction detail(cause: unknown): string {\\n79\\t  return cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n80\\t}\\n81\\t\\n82\\t// ── pull (Flow 1: AC-1.1–1.3, 1.5 default-boundary leg, 1.7) ─────\\n83\\t\\n84\\t// The hot-path read: view header + bands (if any), tail messages after the\\n85\\t// compact point (deleted-filtered, record order), boundary position; then\\n86\\t// format — band messages first, tail per the mapping table, tool results\\n87\\t// at-or-behind the boundary in short form. No view row ⇒ the whole record is\\n88\\t// tail from event 1 (AC-1.3) through this same code path with the compact\\n89\\t// point at its zero origin — snapshot-absent, never a separate branch.\\n90\\t//\\n91\\t// Reads-only is structural, not disciplined: the whole operation runs in the\\n92\\t// touch-suppressed scope, so the open announcement that would let a\\n93\\t// background SDK's scheduler hang a first-touch catch-up drain off this read\\n94\\t// (openThreadDatabase → fireThreadTouch → scheduler.touch) never fires —\\n95\\t// AC-1.1's no-queue-interaction holds in both host modes.\\n96\\texport async function pull(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<PullResult>> {\\n97\\t  return runWithThreadTouchSuppressed(() => pullInner(ref));\\n98\\t}\\n99\\t\\n100\\tasync function pullInner(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<PullResult>> {\\n101\\t  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(ref);\\n102\\t  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n103\\t  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n104\\t  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n105\\t\\n106\\t  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n107\\t  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n108\\t  const db = opened.value;\\n109\\t  try {\\n110\\t    const snapshot = readViewSnapshot(db);\\n111\\t    const compactPoint = snapshot?.compactPoint ?? 0;\\n112\\t    const boundaryPosition = readBoundaryPosition(db);\\n113\\t    const tailRows = readTailMessages(db, compactPoint);\\n114\\t    const renderCtx = {\\n115\\t      boundaryPosition,\\n116\\t      toolNameByCallId: toolNamesByCallId(tailRows),\\n117\\t      toolResultSummaries: readReadyToolResultSummaries(db),\\n118\\t    };\\n119\\t\\n120\\t    const messages: ViewMessage[] = [];\\n121\\t    if (snapshot !== null) {\\n122\\t      for (const band of snapshot.bands) {\\n123\\t        messages.push(renderBandMessage(band.band, band.renderedText));\\n124\\t      }\\n125\\t    }\\n126\\t    for (const row of tailRows) {\\n127\\t      messages.push(renderTailMessage(row, renderCtx));\\n128\\t    }\\n129\\t\\n130\\t    return {\\n131\\t      ok: true,\\n132\\t      value: {\\n133\\t        messages,\\n134\\t        meta: {\\n135\\t          compactPoint: snapshot?.compactPoint ?? null,\\n136\\t          coveredFrom: snapshot?.coveredFrom ?? null,\\n137\\t          boundaryPosition,\\n138\\t          gapCount: snapshot?.gapCount ?? 0,\\n139\\t          degradedCount: snapshot?.degradedCount ?? 0,\\n140\\t          viewId: snapshot?.viewId ?? null,\\n141\\t          createdAt: snapshot?.createdAt ?? null,\\n142\\t        },\\n143\\t      },\\n144\\t    };\\n145\\t  } catch (cause) {\\n146\\t    return storageFailure(`view pull failed: ${detail(cause)}`);\\n147\\t  } finally {\\n148\\t    db.close();\\n149\\t  }\\n150\\t}\\n151\\t\\n152\\t// ── status (AC-2.8) ───────────────────────────────────────────────\\n153\\t\\n154\\t// Derivation counts bucket from one report entry the way the report's own\\n155\\t// vocabulary reads (shared/derivation.ts): never-attempted or first-flight\\n156\\t// pending, retrying (pending with attempts spent), failed, blocked. Ready\\n157\\t// forms are healthy and not an operational situation.\\n158\\tfunction bucketDerivation(\\n159\\t  entries: readonly FormReportEntry[],\\n160\\t  counts: ViewStatus[\\\"derivation\\\"],\\n161\\t): void {\\n162\\t  for (const entry of entries) {\\n163\\t    switch (entry.state) {\\n164\\t      case \\\"pending\\\":\\n165\\t        if ((entry.queue?.attempts ?? 0) > 0) counts.retrying += 1;\\n166\\t        else counts.pending += 1;\\n167\\t        break;\\n168\\t      case \\\"failed\\\":\\n169\\t        counts.failed += 1;\\n170\\t        break;\\n171\\t      case \\\"blocked\\\":\\n172\\t        counts.blocked += 1;\\n173\\t        break;\\n174\\t      case \\\"ready\\\":\\n175\\t        break;\\n176\\t    }\\n177\\t  }\\n178\\t}\\n179\\t\\n180\\t// Reads only, callable any time, no side effects: tail size against the\\n181\\t// configured trigger threshold with a compact recommendation (`tailTokens >\\n182\\t// threshold`, nothing smarter — the caller owns policy), derivation counts\\n183\\t// by state read through the OWNERS' report surfaces (must-not-own: never a\\n184\\t// direct derived_form read here), the active view's health or null\\n185\\t// pre-compact, and the visibility zone's sum against its max — computed live\\n186\\t// by the same query the Story 4 advance will use, so \\\"visible in status\\\" is\\n187\\t// structural, not stored.\\n188\\t//\\n189\\t// Like pull, the whole read — including the owners' report surfaces it\\n190\\t// consumes — runs in the touch-suppressed scope, so a background SDK's\\n191\\t// status can never schedule a catch-up drain (AC-2.8 reads-only, both\\n192\\t// host modes).\\n193\\texport async function status(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<ViewStatus>> {\\n194\\t  return runWithThreadTouchSuppressed(() => statusInner(ref));\\n195\\t}\\n196\\t\\n197\\tasync function statusInner(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<ViewStatus>> {\\n198\\t  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(ref);\\n199\\t  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n200\\t  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n201\\t  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n202\\t\\n203\\t  const config = viewConfig();\\n204\\t  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n205\\t  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n206\\t  const db = opened.value;\\n207\\t  let tailTokens: number;\\n208\\t  let zoneTokens: number;\\n209\\t  let view: ViewStatus[\\\"view\\\"];\\n210\\t  try {\\n211\\t    const snapshot = readViewSnapshot(db);\\n212\\t    const compactPoint = snapshot?.compactPoint ?? 0;\\n213\\t    const boundaryPosition = readBoundaryPosition(db);\\n214\\t    tailTokens = tailTokenSum(db, compactPoint);\\n215\\t    zoneTokens = visibilityZoneTokens(db, boundaryPosition, compactPoint);\\n216\\t    view =\\n217\\t      snapshot === null\\n218\\t        ? null\\n219\\t        : {\\n220\\t            degraded: snapshot.degradedCount,\\n221\\t            gaps: snapshot.gapCount,\\n222\\t            builtAt: snapshot.createdAt,\\n223\\t          };\\n224\\t  } catch (cause) {\\n225\\t    return storageFailure(`view status failed: ${detail(cause)}`);\\n226\\t  } finally {\\n227\\t    db.close();\\n228\\t  }\\n229\\t\\n230\\t  // The owners' report surfaces open their own handles; ours is closed first\\n231\\t  // so the status read never holds two handles on one thread file.\\n232\\t  const messageReport = await messagesDomain.report({ filePath });\\n233\\t  if (!messageReport.ok) return messageReport;\\n234\\t  const turnReport = await turnsDomain.report({ filePath });\\n235\\t  if (!turnReport.ok) return turnReport;\\n236\\t  const derivation: ViewStatus[\\\"derivation\\\"] = {\\n237\\t    pending: 0,\\n238\\t    retrying: 0,\\n239\\t    failed: 0,\\n240\\t    blocked: 0,\\n241\\t  };\\n242\\t  bucketDerivation(messageReport.value, derivation);\\n243\\t  bucketDerivation(turnReport.value, derivation);\\n244\\t\\n245\\t  return {\\n246\\t    ok: true,\\n247\\t    value: {\\n248\\t      tailTokens,\\n249\\t      threshold: config.compactThreshold,\\n250\\t      compactRecommended: tailTokens > config.compactThreshold,\\n251\\t      derivation,\\n252\\t      view,\\n253\\t      visibility: { zoneTokens, maxTokens: config.visibility.maxTokens },\\n254\\t    },\\n255\\t  };\\n256\\t}\\n257\\t\\n258\\t// ── compact (Flow 2: AC-2.1–2.7, 2.9, 2.10) ──────────────────────\\n259\\t\\n260\\t// The default base when no profile is named: the first built-in, matching\\n261\\t// the epic's primary user (the PI continuation harness). Explicit params\\n262\\t// override the base field-wise (AC-2.2).\\n263\\tconst DEFAULT_PROFILE_NAME = \\\"continuation\\\";\\n264\\t\\n265\\tfunction callerError(\\n266\\t  code: \\\"unknown_profile\\\" | \\\"invalid_view_config\\\",\\n267\\t  reason: string,\\n268\\t): { ok: false; error: ErrorResult } {\\n269\\t  return { ok: false, error: { errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\", code, reason } };\\n270\\t}\\n271\\t\\n272\\tconst BAND_ORDER: readonly Band[] = [\\\"brief\\\", \\\"detailed\\\", \\\"smooth\\\"];\\n273\\t\\n274\\t// Compact runs only when invoked through this surface (AC-2.1: no code path\\n275\\t// in core calls it). Flow, in order: validate profile/params (pre-IO, so a\\n276\\t// rejection provably touches nothing) → [sweep step ABSENT this story — the\\n277\\t// receipt's sweep field reports the literal \\\"absent\\\"; Story 3 embeds the\\n278\\t// real sweep here per stories/02-smart-compact.md §Scope out] → read record\\n279\\t// + forms with the corruption check in the reads (pre-transaction, prior\\n280\\t// view trivially intact on refusal) → selection walk → band rendering → one\\n281\\t// BEGIN IMMEDIATE replacing the view and resetting the boundary → receipt.\\n282\\t// Assembly is entirely from stored artifacts: nothing here can reach a\\n283\\t// provider (AC-2.4 zero-inference is structural).\\n284\\texport async function compact(\\n285\\t  ref: ThreadRef,\\n286\\t  opts: { profile?: string; params?: ViewCompactParams; sweep?: boolean },\\n287\\t): Promise<OpResult<CompactReceipt>> {\\n288\\t  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(ref);\\n289\\t  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n290\\t  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n291\\t  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n292\\t\\n293\\t  const config = viewConfig();\\n294\\t  const baseName = opts.profile ?? DEFAULT_PROFILE_NAME;\\n295\\t  const base = config.profiles[baseName];\\n296\\t  if (base === undefined) {\\n297\\t    return callerError(\\n298\\t      \\\"unknown_profile\\\",\\n299\\t      `unknown profile \\\"${baseName}\\\"; configured profiles are ${Object.keys(config.profiles)\\n300\\t        .map((name) => `\\\"${name}\\\"`)\\n301\\t        .join(\\\", \\\")}`,\\n302\\t    );\\n303\\t  }\\n304\\t  const merged: ViewProfile = {\\n305\\t    name: base.name,\\n306\\t    lowerBound: opts.params?.lowerBound ?? base.lowerBound,\\n307\\t    percentages: { ...base.percentages, ...opts.params?.percentages },\\n308\\t  };\\n309\\t  const violation = profileViolation(merged);\\n310\\t  if (violation !== null) return callerError(\\\"invalid_view_config\\\", violation);\\n311\\t  // Receipt provenance: \\\"null when explicit params\\\" (tech design §Storage) —\\n312\\t  // any param override means the config is no longer a named profile's mix,\\n313\\t  // even when one served as the merge base; the receipt's config carries the\\n314\\t  // resolved truth. A bare or profile-only call names its profile.\\n315\\t  const profileName = opts.params === undefined ? baseName : null;\\n316\\t\\n317\\t  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n318\\t  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n319\\t  const db = opened.value;\\n320\\t  try {\\n321\\t    let inputs;\\n322\\t    try {\\n323\\t      inputs = readSelectionInputs(db);\\n324\\t    } catch (cause) {\\n325\\t      if (cause instanceof CanonicalCorruptionError) {\\n326\\t        // Pre-transaction refusal: nothing was written, the prior view and\\n327\\t        // the record are untouched (AC-2.5).\\n328\\t        return {\\n329\\t          ok: false,\\n330\\t          error: { errorClass: \\\"state_corruption\\\", code: cause.code, reason: cause.message },\\n331\\t        };\\n332\\t      }\\n333\\t      throw cause;\\n334\\t    }\\n335\\t    const selection = selectArrangement(inputs, {\\n336\\t      lowerBound: merged.lowerBound,\\n337\\t      percentages: merged.percentages,\\n338\\t    });\\n339\\t\\n340\\t    const entriesByBand = (band: Band): ArrangementEntry[] =>\\n341\\t      selection.entries.filter((entry) => entry.band === band);\\n342\\t    const bands = BAND_ORDER.flatMap((band) => {\\n343\\t      const entries = entriesByBand(band);\\n344\\t      if (entries.length === 0) return [];\\n345\\t      const renderedText = assembleBandText(entries.map((entry) => entry.text));\\n346\\t      return [{ band, renderedText, tokenCount: estimateTokens(renderedText) }];\\n347\\t    });\\n348\\t\\n349\\t    const createdAt = new Date().toISOString();\\n350\\t    // view_id is v<compact event order> — deterministic, and deliberately\\n351\\t    // reused by an intake-free recompact (tech design L395: do not \\\"fix\\\"\\n352\\t    // into a uniqueness scheme; the singleton row is replaced whole).\\n353\\t    const viewId = `v${inputs.maxEventOrder}`;\\n354\\t\\n355\\t    // Story-0 injection point: TC-2.4's crash between the (absent) sweep and\\n356\\t    // the view-write transaction. An installed hook's throw aborts here —\\n357\\t    // before BEGIN — so the previous view keeps serving.\\n358\\t    fireViewInjection(\\\"compact-write\\\");\\n359\\t\\n360\\t    replaceViewSnapshot(db, {\\n361\\t      viewId,\\n362\\t      createdAt,\\n363\\t      compactPoint: selection.compactPoint,\\n364\\t      coveredFrom: selection.coveredFrom,\\n365\\t      profileName,\\n366\\t      configJson: JSON.stringify({\\n367\\t        lowerBound: merged.lowerBound,\\n368\\t        percentages: merged.percentages,\\n369\\t      }),\\n370\\t      arrangementJson: JSON.stringify(\\n371\\t        selection.entries.map((entry) => ({\\n372\\t          band: entry.band,\\n373\\t          subjectKind: entry.subjectKind,\\n374\\t          subjectId: entry.subjectId,\\n375\\t          formUsed: entry.formUsed,\\n376\\t          degraded: entry.degraded,\\n377\\t        })),\\n378\\t      ),\\n379\\t      gapsJson: JSON.stringify(\\n380\\t        selection.entries\\n381\\t          .filter((entry) => entry.gap)\\n382\\t          .map((entry) => ({\\n383\\t            band: entry.band,\\n384\\t            subjectId: entry.subjectId,\\n385\\t            reason: entry.reason ?? \\\"unknown\\\",\\n386\\t          })),\\n387\\t      ),\\n388\\t      sourceStateJson: JSON.stringify({\\n389\\t        maxEventOrder: inputs.maxEventOrder,\\n390\\t        formCounts: inputs.formCounts,\\n391\\t      }),\\n392\\t      bands,\\n393\\t    });\\n394\\t\\n395\\t    const bandReport = {} as CompactReceipt[\\\"bands\\\"];\\n396\\t    for (const band of BAND_ORDER) {\\n397\\t      const stored = bands.find((row) => row.band === band);\\n398\\t      bandReport[band] = {\\n399\\t        entries: entriesByBand(band).length,\\n400\\t        tokens: stored?.tokenCount ?? 0,\\n401\\t      };\\n402\\t    }\\n403\\t    const tailTokens = tailTokenSum(db, selection.compactPoint);\\n404\\t    return {\\n405\\t      ok: true,\\n406\\t      value: {\\n407\\t        viewId,\\n408\\t        profile: profileName,\\n409\\t        config: { ...merged.percentages, lowerBound: merged.lowerBound },\\n410\\t        bands: bandReport,\\n411\\t        tailTokens,\\n412\\t        // Actual assembled total vs the bound (target, not cap — AC-2.4).\\n413\\t        totalTokens:\\n414\\t          bandReport.brief.tokens +\\n415\\t          bandReport.detailed.tokens +\\n416\\t          bandReport.smooth.tokens +\\n417\\t          tailTokens,\\n418\\t        coveredFrom: selection.coveredFrom,\\n419\\t        compactPoint: selection.compactPoint,\\n420\\t        degraded: selection.entries\\n421\\t          .filter((entry) => entry.degraded)\\n422\\t          .map((entry) => ({\\n423\\t            band: entry.band,\\n424\\t            subjectId: entry.subjectId,\\n425\\t            usedForm: entry.formUsed,\\n426\\t          })),\\n427\\t        gaps: selection.entries\\n428\\t          .filter((entry) => entry.gap)\\n429\\t          .map((entry) => ({\\n430\\t            band: entry.band,\\n431\\t            subjectId: entry.subjectId,\\n432\\t            reason: entry.reason ?? \\\"unknown\\\",\\n433\\t          })),\\n434\\t        // Sweep step absent this story (NOT skipped, NOT an empty receipt):\\n435\\t        // Story 3 embeds the sweep and flips this field's vocabulary.\\n436\\t        sweep: \\\"absent\\\",\\n437\\t      },\\n438\\t    };\\n439\\t  } catch (cause) {\\n440\\t    return storageFailure(`view compact failed: ${detail(cause)}`);\\n441\\t  } finally {\\n442\\t    db.close();\\n443\\t  }\\n444\\t}\\n445\\t\\n446\\t// ── stubs (Stories 3, 5) ─────────────────────────────────────────\\n447\\t\\n448\\t// The skeleton's stub contract (tech design §Interface Definitions):\\n449\\t// structured result, machine-readable, never a throw on this surface.\\n450\\tfunction notImplemented(op: string): { ok: false; error: ErrorResult } {\\n451\\t  return {\\n452\\t    ok: false,\\n453\\t    error: {\\n454\\t      errorClass: \\\"system_error\\\",\\n455\\t      code: \\\"not_implemented\\\",\\n456\\t      reason: `not implemented: ${op}`,\\n457\\t    },\\n458\\t  };\\n459\\t}\\n460\\t\\n461\\texport async function sweep(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<SweepReceipt>> {\\n462\\t  void ref;\\n463\\t  return notImplemented(\\\"sweep\\\");\\n464\\t}\\n465\\t\\n466\\texport async function materialize(\\n467\\t  ref: ThreadRef,\\n468\\t  opts: { path: string; format?: \\\"pi-session\\\" },\\n469\\t): Promise<OpResult<{ writtenPath: string }>> {\\n470\\t  void ref;\\n471\\t  void opts;\\n472\\t  return notImplemented(\\\"materialize\\\");\\n473\\t}\\n474\\t\\n475\\t// ── Story 0 substrate (consumed by createSdk at construction) ─────\\n476\\texport {\\n477\\t  BUILT_IN_PROFILES,\\n478\\t  DEFAULT_COMPACT_THRESHOLD,\\n479\\t  DEFAULT_VISIBILITY,\\n480\\t  resolveViewConfig,\\n481\\t} from \\\"./internal/profiles.js\\\";\\n482\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"f006cddb-2184-479e-939b-55dccd3023e3\",\"uuid\":\"55b73318-02e7-4c75-92d4-8b8ab3c9a3f6\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-11T16:35:28.321Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/index.ts\",\"content\":\"// thread-view surface (Epic 03): pull, status, compact, sweep, materialize.\\n// Story 1 lands the skeleton with `pull` and `status` real — the hot-path\\n// reads: local reads and deterministic string assembly only, no inference,\\n// no network, no queue interaction, no writes (AC-1.1, AC-2.8). The other\\n// three are structured-result stubs until their stories (2, 3, 5) land.\\n// Story 0's substrate (profile resolution, consumed by createSdk) re-exports\\n// at the bottom.\\nimport { existsSync } from \\\"node:fs\\\";\\nimport {\\n  resolveInstanceViewConfig,\\n  runWithThreadTouchSuppressed,\\n} from \\\"../../shared/context.js\\\";\\nimport type { FormReportEntry } from \\\"../../shared/derivation.js\\\";\\nimport { storageFailure, type ErrorResult, type OpResult } from \\\"../../shared/errors.js\\\";\\nimport type {\\n  CompactReceipt,\\n  PullResult,\\n  ResolvedViewConfig,\\n  SweepReceipt,\\n  ViewCompactParams,\\n  ViewMessage,\\n  ViewProfile,\\n  ViewStatus,\\n} from \\\"../../shared/view.js\\\";\\nimport * as messagesDomain from \\\"../messages/index.js\\\";\\nimport * as turnsDomain from \\\"../turns/index.js\\\";\\nimport {\\n  openThreadDatabase,\\n  resolveThreadRef,\\n  type ThreadRef,\\n} from \\\"../threads/index.js\\\";\\nimport { readBoundaryPosition, visibilityZoneTokens } from \\\"./internal/boundary.js\\\";\\nimport { profileViolation, resolveViewConfig } from \\\"./internal/profiles.js\\\";\\nimport {\\n  assembleBandText,\\n  renderBandMessage,\\n  renderTailMessage,\\n  toolNamesByCallId,\\n} from \\\"./internal/render.js\\\";\\nimport { fireViewInjection } from \\\"./internal/seam.js\\\";\\nimport {\\n  CanonicalCorruptionError,\\n  readSelectionInputs,\\n  selectArrangement,\\n  type ArrangementEntry,\\n} from \\\"./internal/select.js\\\";\\nimport {\\n  readReadyToolResultSummaries,\\n  readTailMessages,\\n  readViewSnapshot,\\n  replaceViewSnapshot,\\n  tailTokenSum,\\n} from \\\"./internal/snapshot.js\\\";\\nimport { estimateTokens } from \\\"../../tech-utils/token-counting/index.js\\\";\\nimport type { Band } from \\\"../../shared/view.js\\\";\\n\\n// Config resolution for the operation in hand: the SDK instance's resolved\\n// view config rides the per-instance seam (epic-fix-001 pattern, tech design\\n// Flow 4); below-SDK direct domain calls fall back to the built-in defaults\\n// through the same one resolution path createSdk uses.\\nconst DEFAULT_VIEW_CONFIG: ResolvedViewConfig = resolveViewConfig();\\n\\nfunction viewConfig(): ResolvedViewConfig {\\n  return resolveInstanceViewConfig() ?? DEFAULT_VIEW_CONFIG;\\n}\\n\\nfunction threadNotFound(filePath: string): { ok: false; error: ErrorResult } {\\n  return {\\n    ok: false,\\n    error: {\\n      errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n      code: \\\"thread_not_found\\\",\\n      reason: `no thread file exists at ${filePath}`,\\n    },\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nfunction detail(cause: unknown): string {\\n  return cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n}\\n\\n// ── pull (Flow 1: AC-1.1–1.3, 1.5 default-boundary leg, 1.7) ─────\\n\\n// The hot-path read: view header + bands (if any), tail messages after the\\n// compact point (deleted-filtered, record order), boundary position; then\\n// format — band messages first, tail per the mapping table, tool results\\n// at-or-behind the boundary in short form. No view row ⇒ the whole record is\\n// tail from event 1 (AC-1.3) through this same code path with the compact\\n// point at its zero origin — snapshot-absent, never a separate branch.\\n//\\n// Reads-only is structural, not disciplined: the whole operation runs in the\\n// touch-suppressed scope, so the open announcement that would let a\\n// background SDK's scheduler hang a first-touch catch-up drain off this read\\n// (openThreadDatabase → fireThreadTouch → scheduler.touch) never fires —\\n// AC-1.1's no-queue-interaction holds in both host modes.\\nexport async function pull(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<PullResult>> {\\n  return runWithThreadTouchSuppressed(() => pullInner(ref));\\n}\\n\\nasync function pullInner(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<PullResult>> {\\n  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(ref);\\n  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n\\n  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n  const db = opened.value;\\n  try {\\n    const snapshot = readViewSnapshot(db);\\n    const compactPoint = snapshot?.compactPoint ?? 0;\\n    const boundaryPosition = readBoundaryPosition(db);\\n    const tailRows = readTailMessages(db, compactPoint);\\n    const renderCtx = {\\n      boundaryPosition,\\n      toolNameByCallId: toolNamesByCallId(tailRows),\\n      toolResultSummaries: readReadyToolResultSummaries(db),\\n    };\\n\\n    const messages: ViewMessage[] = [];\\n    if (snapshot !== null) {\\n      for (const band of snapshot.bands) {\\n        messages.push(renderBandMessage(band.band, band.renderedText));\\n      }\\n    }\\n    for (const row of tailRows) {\\n      messages.push(renderTailMessage(row, renderCtx));\\n    }\\n\\n    return {\\n      ok: true,\\n      value: {\\n        messages,\\n        meta: {\\n          compactPoint: snapshot?.compactPoint ?? null,\\n          coveredFrom: snapshot?.coveredFrom ?? null,\\n          boundaryPosition,\\n          gapCount: snapshot?.gapCount ?? 0,\\n          degradedCount: snapshot?.degradedCount ?? 0,\\n          viewId: snapshot?.viewId ?? null,\\n          createdAt: snapshot?.createdAt ?? null,\\n        },\\n      },\\n    };\\n  } catch (cause) {\\n    return storageFailure(`view pull failed: ${detail(cause)}`);\\n  } finally {\\n    db.close();\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// ── status (AC-2.8) ───────────────────────────────────────────────\\n\\n// Derivation counts bucket from one report entry the way the report's own\\n// vocabulary reads (shared/derivation.ts): never-attempted or first-flight\\n// pending, retrying (pending with attempts spent), failed, blocked. Ready\\n// forms are healthy and not an operational situation.\\nfunction bucketDerivation(\\n  entries: readonly FormReportEntry[],\\n  counts: ViewStatus[\\\"derivation\\\"],\\n): void {\\n  for (const entry of entries) {\\n    switch (entry.state) {\\n      case \\\"pending\\\":\\n        if ((entry.queue?.attempts ?? 0) > 0) counts.retrying += 1;\\n        else counts.pending += 1;\\n        break;\\n      case \\\"failed\\\":\\n        counts.failed += 1;\\n        break;\\n      case \\\"blocked\\\":\\n        counts.blocked += 1;\\n        break;\\n      case \\\"ready\\\":\\n        break;\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// Reads only, callable any time, no side effects: tail size against the\\n// configured trigger threshold with a compact recommendation (`tailTokens >\\n// threshold`, nothing smarter — the caller owns policy), derivation counts\\n// by state read through the OWNERS' report surfaces (must-not-own: never a\\n// direct derived_form read here), the active view's health or null\\n// pre-compact, and the visibility zone's sum against its max — computed live\\n// by the same query the Story 4 advance will use, so \\\"visible in status\\\" is\\n// structural, not stored.\\n//\\n// Like pull, the whole read — including the owners' report surfaces it\\n// consumes — runs in the touch-suppressed scope, so a background SDK's\\n// status can never schedule a catch-up drain (AC-2.8 reads-only, both\\n// host modes).\\nexport async function status(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<ViewStatus>> {\\n  return runWithThreadTouchSuppressed(() => statusInner(ref));\\n}\\n\\nasync function statusInner(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<ViewStatus>> {\\n  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(ref);\\n  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n\\n  const config = viewConfig();\\n  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n  const db = opened.value;\\n  let tailTokens: number;\\n  let zoneTokens: number;\\n  let view: ViewStatus[\\\"view\\\"];\\n  try {\\n    const snapshot = readViewSnapshot(db);\\n    const compactPoint = snapshot?.compactPoint ?? 0;\\n    const boundaryPosition = readBoundaryPosition(db);\\n    tailTokens = tailTokenSum(db, compactPoint);\\n    zoneTokens = visibilityZoneTokens(db, boundaryPosition, compactPoint);\\n    view =\\n      snapshot === null\\n        ? null\\n        : {\\n            degraded: snapshot.degradedCount,\\n            gaps: snapshot.gapCount,\\n            builtAt: snapshot.createdAt,\\n          };\\n  } catch (cause) {\\n    return storageFailure(`view status failed: ${detail(cause)}`);\\n  } finally {\\n    db.close();\\n  }\\n\\n  // The owners' report surfaces open their own handles; ours is closed first\\n  // so the status read never holds two handles on one thread file.\\n  const messageReport = await messagesDomain.report({ filePath });\\n  if (!messageReport.ok) return messageReport;\\n  const turnReport = await turnsDomain.report({ filePath });\\n  if (!turnReport.ok) return turnReport;\\n  const derivation: ViewStatus[\\\"derivation\\\"] = {\\n    pending: 0,\\n    retrying: 0,\\n    failed: 0,\\n    blocked: 0,\\n  };\\n  bucketDerivation(messageReport.value, derivation);\\n  bucketDerivation(turnReport.value, derivation);\\n\\n  return {\\n    ok: true,\\n    value: {\\n      tailTokens,\\n      threshold: config.compactThreshold,\\n      compactRecommended: tailTokens > config.compactThreshold,\\n      derivation,\\n      view,\\n      visibility: { zoneTokens, maxTokens: config.visibility.maxTokens },\\n    },\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n// ── compact (Flow 2: AC-2.1–2.7, 2.9, 2.10) ──────────────────────\\n\\n// The default base when no profile is named: the first built-in, matching\\n// the epic's primary user (the PI continuation harness). Explicit params\\n// override the base field-wise (AC-2.2).\\nconst DEFAULT_PROFILE_NAME = \\\"continuation\\\";\\n\\nfunction callerError(\\n  code: \\\"unknown_profile\\\" | \\\"invalid_view_config\\\",\\n  reason: string,\\n): { ok: false; error: ErrorResult } {\\n  return { ok: false, error: { errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\", code, reason } };\\n}\\n\\nconst BAND_ORDER: readonly Band[] = [\\\"brief\\\", \\\"detailed\\\", \\\"smooth\\\"];\\n\\n// Compact runs only when invoked through this surface (AC-2.1: no code path\\n// in core calls it). Flow, in order: validate profile/params (pre-IO, so a\\n// rejection provably touches nothing) → [sweep step ABSENT this story — the\\n// receipt's sweep field reports the literal \\\"absent\\\"; Story 3 embeds the\\n// real sweep here per stories/02-smart-compact.md §Scope out] → read record\\n// + forms with the corruption check in the reads (pre-transaction, prior\\n// view trivially intact on refusal) → selection walk → band rendering → one\\n// BEGIN IMMEDIATE replacing the view and resetting the boundary → receipt.\\n// Assembly is entirely from stored artifacts: nothing here can reach a\\n// provider (AC-2.4 zero-inference is structural).\\nexport async function compact(\\n  ref: ThreadRef,\\n  opts: { profile?: string; params?: ViewCompactParams; sweep?: boolean },\\n): Promise<OpResult<CompactReceipt>> {\\n  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(ref);\\n  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n\\n  const config = viewConfig();\\n  const baseName = opts.profile ?? DEFAULT_PROFILE_NAME;\\n  const base = config.profiles[baseName];\\n  if (base === undefined) {\\n    return callerError(\\n      \\\"unknown_profile\\\",\\n      `unknown profile \\\"${baseName}\\\"; configured profiles are ${Object.keys(config.profiles)\\n        .map((name) => `\\\"${name}\\\"`)\\n        .join(\\\", \\\")}`,\\n    );\\n  }\\n  const merged: ViewProfile = {\\n    name: base.name,\\n    lowerBound: opts.params?.lowerBound ?? base.lowerBound,\\n    percentages: { ...base.percentages, ...opts.params?.percentages },\\n  };\\n  const violation = profileViolation(merged);\\n  if (violation !== null) return callerError(\\\"invalid_view_config\\\", violation);\\n  // Receipt provenance: \\\"null when explicit params\\\" (tech design §Storage) —\\n  // any param override means the config is no longer a named profile's mix,\\n  // even when one served as the merge base; the receipt's config carries the\\n  // resolved truth. A bare or profile-only call names its profile.\\n  const profileName = opts.params === undefined ? baseName : null;\\n\\n  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n  const db = opened.value;\\n  try {\\n    let inputs;\\n    try {\\n      inputs = readSelectionInputs(db);\\n    } catch (cause) {\\n      if (cause instanceof CanonicalCorruptionError) {\\n        // Pre-transaction refusal: nothing was written, the prior view and\\n        // the record are untouched (AC-2.5).\\n        return {\\n          ok: false,\\n          error: { errorClass: \\\"state_corruption\\\", code: cause.code, reason: cause.message },\\n        };\\n      }\\n      throw cause;\\n    }\\n    const selection = selectArrangement(inputs, {\\n      lowerBound: merged.lowerBound,\\n      percentages: merged.percentages,\\n    });\\n\\n    const entriesByBand = (band: Band): ArrangementEntry[] =>\\n      selection.entries.filter((entry) => entry.band === band);\\n    const bands = BAND_ORDER.flatMap((band) => {\\n      const entries = entriesByBand(band);\\n      if (entries.length === 0) return [];\\n      const renderedText = assembleBandText(entries.map((entry) => entry.text));\\n      return [{ band, renderedText, tokenCount: estimateTokens(renderedText) }];\\n    });\\n\\n    const createdAt = new Date().toISOString();\\n    // view_id is v<compact event order> — deterministic, and deliberately\\n    // reused by an intake-free recompact (tech design L395: do not \\\"fix\\\"\\n    // into a uniqueness scheme; the singleton row is replaced whole).\\n    const viewId = `v${inputs.maxEventOrder}`;\\n\\n    // Story-0 injection point: TC-2.4's crash between the (absent) sweep and\\n    // the view-write transaction. An installed hook's throw aborts here —\\n    // before BEGIN — so the previous view keeps serving.\\n    fireViewInjection(\\\"compact-write\\\");\\n\\n    replaceViewSnapshot(db, {\\n      viewId,\\n      createdAt,\\n      compactPoint: selection.compactPoint,\\n      coveredFrom: selection.coveredFrom,\\n      profileName,\\n      configJson: JSON.stringify({\\n        lowerBound: merged.lowerBound,\\n        percentages: merged.percentages,\\n      }),\\n      arrangementJson: JSON.stringify(\\n        selection.entries.map((entry) => ({\\n          band: entry.band,\\n          subjectKind: entry.subjectKind,\\n          subjectId: entry.subjectId,\\n          formUsed: entry.formUsed,\\n          degraded: entry.degraded,\\n        })),\\n      ),\\n      gapsJson: JSON.stringify(\\n        selection.entries\\n          .filter((entry) => entry.gap)\\n          .map((entry) => ({\\n            band: entry.band,\\n            subjectId: entry.subjectId,\\n            reason: entry.reason ?? \\\"unknown\\\",\\n          })),\\n      ),\\n      sourceStateJson: JSON.stringify({\\n        maxEventOrder: inputs.maxEventOrder,\\n        formCounts: inputs.formCounts,\\n      }),\\n      bands,\\n    });\\n\\n    const bandReport = {} as CompactReceipt[\\\"bands\\\"];\\n    for (const band of BAND_ORDER) {\\n      const stored = bands.find((row) => row.band === band);\\n      bandReport[band] = {\\n        entries: entriesByBand(band).length,\\n        tokens: stored?.tokenCount ?? 0,\\n      };\\n    }\\n    const tailTokens = tailTokenSum(db, selection.compactPoint);\\n    return {\\n      ok: true,\\n      value: {\\n        viewId,\\n        profile: profileName,\\n        config: { ...merged.percentages, lowerBound: merged.lowerBound },\\n        bands: bandReport,\\n        tailTokens,\\n        // Actual assembled total vs the bound (target, not cap — AC-2.4).\\n        totalTokens:\\n          bandReport.brief.tokens +\\n          bandReport.detailed.tokens +\\n          bandReport.smooth.tokens +\\n          tailTokens,\\n        coveredFrom: selection.coveredFrom,\\n        compactPoint: selection.compactPoint,\\n        degraded: selection.entries\\n          .filter((entry) => entry.degraded)\\n          .map((entry) => ({\\n            band: entry.band,\\n            subjectId: entry.subjectId,\\n            usedForm: entry.formUsed,\\n          })),\\n        gaps: selection.entries\\n          .filter((entry) => entry.gap)\\n          .map((entry) => ({\\n            band: entry.band,\\n            subjectId: entry.subjectId,\\n            reason: entry.reason ?? \\\"unknown\\\",\\n          })),\\n        // Sweep step absent this story (NOT skipped, NOT an empty receipt):\\n        // Story 3 embeds the sweep and flips this field's vocabulary.\\n        sweep: \\\"absent\\\",\\n      },\\n    };\\n  } catch (cause) {\\n    return storageFailure(`view compact failed: ${detail(cause)}`);\\n  } finally {\\n    db.close();\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// ── stubs (Stories 3, 5) ─────────────────────────────────────────\\n\\n// The skeleton's stub contract (tech design §Interface Definitions):\\n// structured result, machine-readable, never a throw on this surface.\\nfunction notImplemented(op: string): { ok: false; error: ErrorResult } {\\n  return {\\n    ok: false,\\n    error: {\\n      errorClass: \\\"system_error\\\",\\n      code: \\\"not_implemented\\\",\\n      reason: `not implemented: ${op}`,\\n    },\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport async function sweep(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<SweepReceipt>> {\\n  void ref;\\n  return notImplemented(\\\"sweep\\\");\\n}\\n\\nexport async function materialize(\\n  ref: ThreadRef,\\n  opts: { path: string; format?: \\\"pi-session\\\" },\\n): Promise<OpResult<{ writtenPath: string }>> {\\n  void ref;\\n  void opts;\\n  return notImplemented(\\\"materialize\\\");\\n}\\n\\n// ── Story 0 substrate (consumed by createSdk at construction) ─────\\nexport {\\n  BUILT_IN_PROFILES,\\n  DEFAULT_COMPACT_THRESHOLD,\\n  DEFAULT_VISIBILITY,\\n  resolveViewConfig,\\n} from \\\"./internal/profiles.js\\\";\\n\",\"numLines\":482,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":482}}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/streams/004-implementor.stdout.log:74:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01T4qPeTwq9dHVMXEV933t62\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/:\\n001-story-validate.json\\n002-story-orchestrate-run.json\\n003-verify.json\\n004-implementor.json\\nprogress\\nstory-lead\\nstreams\\n\\n/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/preflight/:\\n001-preflight.json\\n002-preflight.json\\n003-preflight.json\\n004-preflight.json\\n005-preflight.json\\n\\n/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/:\\nboundary.ts\\nprofiles.ts\\nrender.ts\\nseam.ts\\nselect.ts\\nsnapshot.ts\\n\\n/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/test/:\\ncli-process-fix.test.ts\\ncli-process-intake.test.ts\\ncli-process-mutations-delete.test.ts\\ncli-process-mutations.test.ts\\ncli-process-projection.test.ts\\ncli-process-report-repair.test.ts\\ncli-process-turns.test.ts\\ncli-process-work-queue.test.ts\\ncli-process-work.test.ts\\ncli-process.test.ts\\nderivation-messages.test.ts\\nderivation-turns.test.ts\\nepic-fix-02.test.ts\\nepic-fix.test.ts\\nfixtures\\nfixtures.test.ts\\ngoldens\\nidempotency.test.ts\\nintake.test.ts\\nmutations-delete.test.ts\\nmutations.test.ts\\nprojection.test.ts\\nred-manifest.json\\nreport-repair.test.ts\\nsmoke.test.ts\\nstate-machine.test.ts\\nthread-migration.test.ts\\nthreads.test.ts\\nturns.test.ts\\nvalidation.test.ts\\nview-compact.test.ts\\nview-fixture.test.ts\\nview-pull.test.ts\\nview-select-golden.test.ts\\nwork-execution-legacy.test.ts\\nwork-execution.tes