\":\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/001-story-validate.json\\\",\\\"provenance\\\":\\\"prior-run\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"verifier-result\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/003-verify.json\\\",\\\"provenance\\\":\\\"current-run\\\"}],\\\"latestContinuationHandles\\\":{\\\"storyVerifier\\\":{\\\"provider\\\":\\\"codex\\\",\\\"sessionId\\\":\\\"019eb786-e7ae-7d92-84c3-8daefeb333c6\\\",\\\"storyId\\\":\\\"03-readiness-sweep\\\"}},\\\"latestEventSequence\\\":8,\\\"callerInputHistory\\\":{\\\"reviewRequests\\\":[],\\\"rulings\\\":[]},\\\"nextIntent\\\":{\\\"actionType\\\":\\\"await-story-implement\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Hard-gate evidence is now recorded in the verifier result, and the latest verifier outcome is revise with blocking implementation/test gaps. The smallest safe next action is implementation against SV-03-001 and SV-03-002.\\\"},\\\"replayBoundary\\\":null,\\\"updatedAt\\\":\\\"2026-06-11T16:35:09.050Z\\\"}\\n\\n---\\n{\\\"storyRunId\\\":\\\"03-readiness-sweep-story-run-001\\\",\\\"sequence\\\":4,\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-06-11T16:32:12.016Z\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"story-lead-self-note-recorded\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Story-lead recorded a durable self-note for a future planner turn.\\\",\\\"data\\\":{\\\"note\\\":\\\"Await hard-gate verifier result before selecting implementation; Story 3 code must not start until both gate legs are recorded.\\\",\\\"actionSequence\\\":3,\\\"actionType\\\":\\\"run-verify\\\",\\\"turn\\\":1}}\\n{\\\"storyRunId\\\":\\\"03-readiness-sweep-story-run-001\\\",\\\"sequence\\\":5,\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-06-11T16:34:58.875Z\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"child-operation-completed\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"story-verify completed with outcome revise and status ok.\\\",\\\"artifact\\\":\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/003-verify.json\\\",\\\"data\\\":{\\\"actionType\\\":\\\"run-verify\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"story-verify\\\",\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"revise\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"ok\\\"}}\\n{\\\"storyRunId\\\":\\\"03-readiness-sweep-story-run-001\\\",\\\"sequence\\\":6,\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-06-11T16:35:09.009Z\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"story-lead-provider-started\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Fresh story-lead provider turn executed without planner session resume.\\\",\\\"data\\\":{\\\"provider\\\":\\\"codex\\\",\\\"model\\\":\\\"gpt-5.5\\\",\\\"reasoningEffort\\\":\\\"high\\\",\\\"promptArtifactPath\\\":\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md\\\",\\\"sessionId\\\":\\\"019eb789-735f-7101-b913-3b22885de9c7\\\"}}\\n{\\\"storyRunId\\\":\\\"03-readiness-sweep-story-run-001\\\",\\\"sequence\\\":7,\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-06-11T16:35:09.030Z\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"story-lead-action-selected\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Story-lead selected run-implement.\\\",\\\"data\\\":{\\\"actionType\\\":\\\"run-implement\\\",\\\"turn\\\":2,\\\"selfNote\\\":\\\"After implementor result, run verifier continuation against the implementation artifact; do not accept unless final verifier outcome is pass with no open findings and story gate evidence is present.\\\"}}\\n{\\\"storyRunId\\\":\\\"03-readiness-sweep-story-run-001\\\",\\\"sequence\\\":8,\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-06-11T16:35:09.030Z\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"story-lead-self-note-recorded\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Story-lead recorded a durable self-note for a future planner turn.\\\",\\\"data\\\":{\\\"note\\\":\\\"After implementor result, run verifier continuation against the implementation artifact; do not accept unless final verifier outcome is pass with no open findings and story gate evidence is present.\\\",\\\"actionSequence\\\":7,\\\"actionType\\\":\\\"run-implement\\\",\\\"turn\\\":2}}\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/streams/004-implementor.stdout.log:201:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01Bh2pwwyWKAaSRLHnxdw3RP\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"    DR->>WQ: complete / failAttempt — short txn, version-checked write\\n  end\\n  DR->>SCH: finished → rerun once if pending\\n```\\n\\nThe drain claims under `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` (claim is a write); runs the handler with **no open transaction** (provider call lives here); completes in a second short transaction. A drain finding the head item claimed with an unexpired lease stops with `stoppedBecause: \\\"in_flight\\\"` and processes nothing (AC-1.4); a head gated by backoff stops it with `\\\"waiting\\\"` — the never-skip-ahead rule in Part 3b governs both. Expired lease → reclaim: attempts increment, item runs again; the source-version check and idempotent artifact write make a double-run harmless (the first run's write either landed before reclaim — completing the item — or lands stale and discards). Lease default 120s (config), chosen >> p99 provider latency.\\n\\nRetry/backoff: budget 3 attempts (config). `failAttempt` under budget: status back to `queued`, `attempts++`, eligibility delayed by `min(2^attempts × 5s, 60s)` encoded as a `claim_expires_at`-style `eligible_at` check in `claimNext`'s WHERE. At budget: status `failed_terminal`, form → `failed` with the final reason (AC-1.9). Backoff values are config; tests set them to 0.\\n\\n**Flow 2 — Message-level derivation.** Handlers read the message row + blocks; tool-call summary additionally reads its paired result by `tool_call_id` (`outcome.ts` derives `succeeded | failed | unknown` mechanically from `isError`/presence — the provider's text never touches the outcome field, AC-2.4). The outcome lands in `derived_form.metadata`, not in `content`: machine-readable apart from provider text. Intake's `MESSAGE_WORK_KINDS` map gains `tool_call: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\"` (AC-2.2). The second intake touch is the late-result repair (AC-2.8): when projecting a `tool_result`, one indexed lookup — does a `tool_call_summary` form exist for the paired call with `metadata.outcome = \\\"unknown\\\"`? If so, requeue it in the batch transaction (the requeue no-op rule makes this idempotent). Both touches are deterministic and local. Forms land via `forms.ts` **UPDATE-only writes with the source-version check** (never upsert — the pending row exists from enqueue; a write that finds no matching row discards as stale).\\n\\n**Flow 3 — Turn composition and chunks.** `turn_derivation` handler: load member messages (deleted-filtered), collect their message-level forms, compose rendering (`compose.ts`) — ready forms verbatim, non-ready fall back to raw/truncated content **recording a gap per fallback** (AC-3.2); tool runs become outcome-explicit accounts grouped by consecutive tool activity (AC-3.4). Rendering → provider `composeTurnRendering`; projection → `projectLowerBand`. Both land as turn forms; placement then runs in the completion transaction: append to open chunk (`chunks.ts`), close on accumulated policy (DD-9), closing enqueues `chunk_summary_detailed` + `chunk_summary_brief` (two items, independent retry — AC-3.8) whose handlers read member projections and call their provider ops.\\n\\nGap semantics (AC-3.3): gaps are recorded facts on the landed artifact. A dependency later repairing does not touch dependents; `report` surfaces gapped artifacts; explicit `requeue` rebuilds (next source version, gaps recomputed from current dependency states).\\n\\n**Flow 4 — Report and repair.** `report(ref, { owner, notReady? })` is one query: `derived_form` LEFT JOIN live `work_item` rows for the subject's forms, exposing state + reason + gaps + queue detail (`attempts`, `last_error`, `eligible_at`). The five distinctions read: `pending` & no attempts = waiting; `pending` & attempts>0 = retrying; `ready`; `failed`; `blocked`. `requeue(ref, { subjectKind, subjectId, form })`: refused for `blocked` (with the blocking reason) and for missing rows; no-op if a live item already targets the form at its current source version (AC-4.5, one EXISTS check); otherwise enqueue at the form's current source version. Requeue of a `failed` form never collides with old work: the failed item's row was deleted at terminal transition (DD-1), and the deterministic id is scoped to the current source version.\\n\\n**Flows 5/6 — Mutations.** One transaction (`runInTransaction`): validate (exists via deleted-filtered read; turn closed; for message-delete: not turn-initiating — else `message_initiates_turn` naming the turn and the turns-delete path), apply record change (content+blocks+token re-stamp for edit; `deleted_at` stamp for deletes), run cascade (DD-8): bump source version + `pending` on cleared forms, drop forms whose subject is deleted (state rows removed — dropped, not failed, AC-6.6), supersede-delete still-queued old-version items (issue 1), enqueue replacements with target source version, register poke. Claimed old-version items may still finish; DD-3 discards their stale results because their source version no longer matches. Result reports changed/cleared/dropped/queued/superseded. Refusals: `turn_open`, `message_not_found`/`turn_not_found`, second delete of the same id → `message_not_found` by the filtered read (AC-6.7's \\\"refusal, not silent success\\\").\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Part 3: Interfaces\\n\\n```typescript\\n// ── shared/derivation.ts ─────────────────────────────────────────\\nexport type FormKind =\\n  | \\\"smoothed_prompt\\\" | \\\"tool_call_summary\\\" | \\\"tool_result_summary\\\"\\n  | \\\"turn_rendering\\\" | \\\"lower_band_projection\\\"\\n  | \\\"chunk_summary_detailed\\\" | \\\"chunk_summary_brief\\\";\\n\\nexport type DerivedFormState = \\\"pending\\\" | \\\"ready\\\" | \\\"failed\\\" | \\\"blocked\\\";\\n\\nexport interface DependencyGap { subjectKind: \\\"message\\\" | \\\"turn\\\" | \\\"chunk\\\"; subjectId: string; form: FormKind; }\\n\\nexport interface DerivedForm {\\n  subjectKind: \\\"message\\\" | \\\"turn\\\" | \\\"chunk\\\";\\n  subjectId: string;\\n  form: FormKind;\\n  state: DerivedFormState;\\n  content?: string;          // ready only\\n  reason?: string;           // failed | blocked\\n  sourceVersion: number;     // which version of the source this form derives from (DD-3)\\n  gaps?: DependencyGap[];    // composed forms; landed-with-fallback record\\n  metadata?: { outcome?: ToolOutcome };  // mechanically stamped fields; never provider-authored\\n  derivedAt?: string;\\n}\\n\\n// outcome on tool-activity summaries — mechanically stamped (AC-2.4)\\nexport type ToolOutcome = \\\"succeeded\\\" | \\\"failed\\\" | \\\"unknown\\\";\\n\\n// ── provider seam (injected at createSdk) ────────────────────────\\n    lastError?: string; eligibleAt?: string };   // live item, if any\\n}\\nexport interface MessagesSurface /* extends Epic 01 */ {\\n  workHandlers: Record<WorkKind, WorkHandler>;\\n  report(ref: ThreadRef, opts?: { notReady?: boolean; messageId?: string }):\\n    Promise<OpResult<FormReportEntry[]>>;\\n  requeue(ref: ThreadRef, target: { messageId: string; form: FormKind }):\\n    Promise<OpResult<{ workItemId: string } | { noop: \\\"already_queued\\\" }>>;\\n  edit(ref: ThreadRef, input: { messageId: string; content: string }):\\n    Promise<OpResult<MutationResult>>;\\n  deleteMessage(ref: ThreadRef, input: { messageId: string }):\\n    Promise<OpResult<MutationResult>>;\\n}\\nexport interface TurnsSurface /* extends Epic 01 */ {\\n  workHandlers: Record<WorkKind, WorkHandler>;\\n  report(ref: ThreadRef, opts?: { notReady?: boolean; turnId?: string; chunkId?: string }):\\n    Promise<OpResult<FormReportEntry[]>>;\\n  requeue(ref: ThreadRef, target: { subjectKind: \\\"turn\\\" | \\\"chunk\\\"; subjectId: string; form: FormKind }):\\n    Promise<OpResult<{ workItemId: string } | { noop: \\\"already_queued\\\" }>>;\\n  deleteTurn(ref: ThreadRef, input: { turnId: string }): Promise<OpResult<MutationResult>>;\\n}\\nexport interface MutationResult {\\n  changed: { messageIds: string[]; turnIds: string[] };\\n  cleared: Array<{ subjectKind: string; subjectId: string; form: FormKind }>;\\n  dropped: Array<{ subjectKind: string; subjectId: string; form: FormKind }>;\\n  queued: Array<{ workItemId: string; kind: WorkKind }>;\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"f006cddb-2184-479e-939b-55dccd3023e3\",\"uuid\":\"cd3d08af-776a-4c0f-9d2f-e76a3bc280ed\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-11T16:36:19.058Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"stdout\":\"    DR->>WQ: complete / failAttempt — short txn, version-checked write\\n  end\\n  DR->>SCH: finished → rerun once if pending\\n```\\n\\nThe drain claims under `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` (claim is a write); runs the handler with **no open transaction** (provider call lives here); completes in a second short transaction. A drain finding the head item claimed with an unexpired lease stops with `stoppedBecause: \\\"in_flight\\\"` and processes nothing (AC-1.4); a head gated by backoff stops it with `\\\"waiting\\\"` — the never-skip-ahead rule in Part 3b governs both. Expired lease → reclaim: attempts increment, item runs again; the source-version check and idempotent artifact write make a double-run harmless (the first run's write either landed before reclaim — completing the item — or lands stale and discards). Lease default 120s (config), chosen >> p99 provider latency.\\n\\nRetry/backoff: budget 3 attempts (config). `failAttempt` under budget: status back to `queued`, `attempts++`, eligibility delayed by `min(2^attempts × 5s, 60s)` encoded as a `claim_expires_at`-style `eligible_at` check in `claimNext`'s WHERE. At budget: status `failed_terminal`, form → `failed` with the final reason (AC-1.9). Backoff values are config; tests set them to 0.\\n\\n**Flow 2 — Message-level derivation.** Handlers read the message row + blocks; tool-call summary additionally reads its paired result by `tool_call_id` (`outcome.ts` derives `succeeded | failed | unknown` mechanically from `isError`/presence — the provider's text never touches the outcome field, AC-2.4). The outcome lands in `derived_form.metadata`, not in `content`: machine-readable apart from provider text. Intake's `MESSAGE_WORK_KINDS` map gains `tool_call: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\"` (AC-2.2). The second intake touch is the late-result repair (AC-2.8): when projecting a `tool_result`, one indexed lookup — does a `tool_call_summary` form exist for the paired call with `metadata.outcome = \\\"unknown\\\"`? If so, requeue it in the batch transaction (the requeue no-op rule makes this idempotent). Both touches are deterministic and local. Forms land via `forms.ts` **UPDATE-only writes with the source-version check** (never upsert — the pending row exists from enqueue; a write that finds no matching row discards as stale).\\n\\n**Flow 3 — Turn composition and chunks.** `turn_derivation` handler: load member messages (deleted-filtered), collect their message-level forms, compose rendering (`compose.ts`) — ready forms verbatim, non-ready fall back to raw/truncated content **recording a gap per fallback** (AC-3.2); tool runs become outcome-explicit accounts grouped by consecutive tool activity (AC-3.4). Rendering → provider `composeTurnRendering`; projection → `projectLowerBand`. Both land as turn forms; placement then runs in the completion transaction: append to open chunk (`chunks.ts`), close on accumulated policy (DD-9), closing enqueues `chunk_summary_detailed` + `chunk_summary_brief` (two items, independent retry — AC-3.8) whose handlers read member projections and call their provider ops.\\n\\nGap semantics (AC-3.3): gaps are recorded facts on the landed artifact. A dependency later repairing does not touch dependents; `report` surfaces gapped artifacts; explicit `requeue` rebuilds (next source version, gaps recomputed from current dependency states).\\n\\n**Flow 4 — Report and repair.** `report(ref, { owner, notReady? })` is one query: `derived_form` LEFT JOIN live `work_item` rows for the subject's forms, exposing state + reason + gaps + queue detail (`attempts`, `last_error`, `eligible_at`). The five distinctions read: `pending` & no attempts = waiting; `pending` & attempts>0 = retrying; `ready`; `failed`; `blocked`. `requeue(ref, { subjectKind, subjectId, form })`: refused for `blocked` (with the blocking reason) and for missing rows; no-op if a live item already targets the form at its current source version (AC-4.5, one EXISTS check); otherwise enqueue at the form's current source version. Requeue of a `failed` form never collides with old work: the failed item's row was deleted at terminal transition (DD-1), and the deterministic id is scoped to the current source version.\\n\\n**Flows 5/6 — Mutations.** One transaction (`runInTransaction`): validate (exists via deleted-filtered read; turn closed; for message-delete: not turn-initiating — else `message_initiates_turn` naming the turn and the turns-delete path), apply record change (content+blocks+token re-stamp for edit; `deleted_at` stamp for deletes), run cascade (DD-8): bump source version + `pending` on cleared forms, drop forms whose subject is deleted (state rows removed — dropped, not failed, AC-6.6), supersede-delete still-queued old-version items (issue 1), enqueue replacements with target source version, register poke. Claimed old-version items may still finish; DD-3 discards their stale results because their source version no longer matches. Result reports changed/cleared/dropped/queued/superseded. Refusals: `turn_open`, `message_not_found`/`turn_not_found`, second delete of the same id → `message_not_found` by the filtered read (AC-6.7's \\\"refusal, not silent success\\\").\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Part 3: Interfaces\\n\\n```typescript\\n// ── shared/derivation.ts ─────────────────────────────────────────\\nexport type FormKind =\\n  | \\\"smoothed_prompt\\\" | \\\"tool_call_summary\\\" | \\\"tool_result_summary\\\"\\n  | \\\"turn_rendering\\\" | \\\"lower_band_projection\\\"\\n  | \\\"chunk_summary_detailed\\\" | \\\"chunk_summary_brief\\\";\\n\\nexport type DerivedFormState = \\\"pending\\\" | \\\"ready\\\" | \\\"failed\\\" | \\\"blocked\\\";\\n\\nexport interface DependencyGap { subjectKind: \\\"message\\\" | \\\"turn\\\" | \\\"chunk\\\"; subjectId: string; form: FormKind; }\\n\\nexport interface DerivedForm {\\n  subjectKind: \\\"message\\\" | \\\"turn\\\" | \\\"chunk\\\";\\n  subjectId: string;\\n  form: FormKind;\\n  state: DerivedFormState;\\n  content?: string;          // ready only\\n  reason?: string;           // failed | blocked\\n  sourceVersion: number;     // which version of the source this form derives from (DD-3)\\n  gaps?: DependencyGap[];    // composed forms; landed-with-fallback record\\n  metadata?: { outcome?: ToolOutcome };  // mechanically stamped fields; never provider-authored\\n  derivedAt?: string;\\n}\\n\\n// outcome on tool-activity summaries — mechanically stamped (AC-2.4)\\nexport type ToolOutcome = \\\"succeeded\\\" | \\\"failed\\\" | \\\"unknown\\\";\\n\\n// ── provider seam (injected at createSdk) ────────────────────────\\n    lastError?: string; eligibleAt?: string };   // live item, if any\\n}\\nexport interface MessagesSurface /* extends Epic 01 */ {\\n  workHandlers: Record<WorkKind, WorkHandler>;\\n  report(ref: ThreadRef, opts?: { notReady?: boolean; messageId?: string }):\\n    Promise<OpResult<FormReportEntry[]>>;\\n  requeue(ref: ThreadRef, target: { messageId: string; form: FormKind }):\\n    Promise<OpResult<{ workItemId: string } | { noop: \\\"already_queued\\\" }>>;\\n  edit(ref: ThreadRef, input: { messageId: string; content: string }):\\n    Promise<OpResult<MutationResult>>;\\n  deleteMessage(ref: ThreadRef, input: { messageId: string }):\\n    Promise<OpResult<MutationResult>>;\\n}\\nexport interface TurnsSurface /* extends Epic 01 */ {\\n  workHandlers: Record<WorkKind, WorkHandler>;\\n  report(ref: ThreadRef, opts?: { notReady?: boolean; turnId?: string; chunkId?: string }):\\n    Promise<OpResult<FormReportEntry[]>>;\\n  requeue(ref: ThreadRef, target: { subjectKind: \\\"turn\\\" | \\\"chunk\\\"; subjectId: string; form: FormKind }):\\n    Promise<OpResult<{ workItemId: string } | { noop: \\\"already_queued\\\" }>>;\\n  deleteTurn(ref: ThreadRef, input: { turnId: string }): Promise<OpResult<MutationResult>>;\\n}\\nexport interface MutationResult {\\n  changed: { messageIds: string[]; turnIds: string[] };\\n  cleared: Array<{ subjectKind: string; subjectId: string; form: FormKind }>;\\n  dropped: Array<{ subjectKind: string; subjectId: string; form: FormKind }>;\\n  queued: Array<{ workItemId: string; kind: WorkKind }>;\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/streams/004-implementor.stdout.log:208:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01JuBqmgAe5xo7NgFenGp8sM\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\t// Epic 02 shared vocabulary: the derived-form state machine's types, the\\n2\\t// provider seam, and the handler contract. Both owning domains (messages,\\n3\\t// turns) consume these; neither owns them — the repair report, the mutation\\n4\\t// cascade, and the drain all speak this vocabulary across domain lines, so it\\n5\\t// lives in shared/ (tech design §Interfaces, DD-2/DD-7).\\n6\\timport type { DatabaseSync } from \\\"node:sqlite\\\";\\n7\\timport type { ResolvedViewConfig, SdkViewConfig } from \\\"./view.js\\\";\\n8\\t\\n9\\texport type SubjectKind = \\\"message\\\" | \\\"turn\\\" | \\\"chunk\\\";\\n10\\t\\n11\\texport type FormKind =\\n12\\t  | \\\"smoothed_prompt\\\"\\n13\\t  | \\\"tool_call_summary\\\"\\n14\\t  | \\\"tool_result_summary\\\"\\n15\\t  | \\\"turn_rendering\\\"\\n16\\t  | \\\"lower_band_projection\\\"\\n17\\t  | \\\"chunk_summary_detailed\\\"\\n18\\t  | \\\"chunk_summary_brief\\\";\\n19\\t\\n20\\texport type DerivedFormState = \\\"pending\\\" | \\\"ready\\\" | \\\"failed\\\" | \\\"blocked\\\";\\n21\\t\\n22\\t// Outcome on tool-activity summaries — mechanically stamped from the record\\n23\\t// (isError/presence), never authored by the provider (AC-2.4).\\n24\\texport type ToolOutcome = \\\"succeeded\\\" | \\\"failed\\\" | \\\"unknown\\\";\\n25\\t\\n26\\t// A composed form's record of a dependency that fell back during composition:\\n27\\t// names the source record and the form that was not ready (AC-3.2/3.3).\\n28\\texport interface DependencyGap {\\n29\\t  subjectKind: SubjectKind;\\n30\\t  subjectId: string;\\n31\\t  form: FormKind;\\n32\\t}\\n33\\t\\n34\\t// The read shape for one derived form's state row (DD-2, DD-3).\\n35\\texport interface DerivedForm {\\n36\\t  subjectKind: SubjectKind;\\n37\\t  subjectId: string;\\n38\\t  form: FormKind;\\n39\\t  state: DerivedFormState;\\n40\\t  content?: string; // ready only\\n41\\t  reason?: string; // failed | blocked\\n42\\t  sourceVersion: number; // which version of the source this form derives from (DD-3)\\n43\\t  gaps?: DependencyGap[]; // composed forms; landed-with-fallback record\\n44\\t  metadata?: DerivedFormMetadata; // mechanically stamped fields; never provider-authored\\n45\\t  derivedAt?: string;\\n46\\t}\\n47\\t\\n48\\t// One tool call's or result's receipt within a turn's composed account\\n49\\t// (AC-3.8): the account text — what changed, as composed — plus the\\n50\\t// mechanically derived outcome. Derived from the composition input, never\\n51\\t// from provider prose; stamped on the turn_rendering form so the chunk\\n52\\t// summaries can read receipts machine-readably in turn order.\\n53\\texport interface ToolRunReceipt {\\n54\\t  messageId: string;\\n55\\t  activity: \\\"tool_call\\\" | \\\"tool_result\\\";\\n56\\t  account: string;\\n57\\t  outcome: ToolOutcome;\\n58\\t}\\n59\\t\\n60\\t// Mechanically stamped form metadata: tool outcomes (AC-2.4), the turn\\n61\\t// rendering's tool-run receipts (AC-3.8), plus — at retry exhaustion — the\\n62\\t// final attempts/last-error copied from the work item before its row is\\n63\\t// deleted (DD-1: the queue is not an audit table; durable outcome detail\\n64\\t// lives here).\\n65\\texport interface DerivedFormMetadata {\\n66\\t  outcome?: ToolOutcome;\\n67\\t  receipts?: ToolRunReceipt[];\\n68\\t  attempts?: number;\\n69\\t  lastError?: string;\\n70\\t}\\n71\\t\\n72\\t// One row of an owner's repair report (Flow 4): the form's durable state\\n73\\t// joined with the queue's mechanical detail for the live item still working\\n74\\t// toward it, if any. The five operational situations read from this one row:\\n75\\t// never-attempted (pending, no queue), retrying (pending + queue with\\n76\\t// attempts > 0), ready, failed (+ reason), blocked (+ reason) — no caller\\n77\\t// ever needs a queue API.\\n78\\texport interface FormReportEntry extends DerivedForm {\\n79\\t  queue?: {\\n80\\t    status: \\\"queued\\\" | \\\"claimed\\\";\\n81\\t    attempts: number;\\n82\\t    lastError?: string;\\n83\\t    eligibleAt?: string;\\n84\\t  };\\n85\\t}\\n86\\t\\n87\\t// ── provider seam (DD-7) ─────────────────────────────────────────\\n88\\t// Every operation returns content or a structured failure carrying\\n89\\t// retryable-or-not; classification is the adapter's duty.\\n90\\texport type ProviderResult =\\n91\\t  | { ok: true; text: string }\\n92\\t  | { ok: false; retryable: boolean; reason: string };\\n93\\t\\n94\\t// Message kinds a rendering part can carry — mirrors the intake event-kind\\n95\\t// vocabulary minus turn_end (turn_end never projects a message). Mirrored\\n96\\t// rather than imported: shared/ may not import domains/.\\n97\\texport type RenderingPartKind =\\n98\\t  | \\\"user_prompt\\\"\\n99\\t  | \\\"assistant_text\\\"\\n100\\t  | \\\"assistant_thinking\\\"\\n101\\t  | \\\"runtime_note\\\"\\n102\\t  | \\\"tool_call\\\"\\n103\\t  | \\\"tool_result\\\";\\n104\\t\\n105\\texport interface RenderingPart {\\n106\\t  messageId: string;\\n107\\t  kind: RenderingPartKind;\\n108\\t  text: string; // ready form content, or raw/truncated fallback\\n109\\t  fallback: boolean; // true ⇒ gap recorded\\n110\\t  outcome?: ToolOutcome; // tool activity only\\n111\\t}\\n112\\t\\n113\\texport interface DerivationProvider {\\n114\\t  smoothPrompt(i: { text: string }): Promise<ProviderResult>;\\n115\\t  summarizeToolCall(i: {\\n116\\t    toolName: string;\\n117\\t    argsJson: string;\\n118\\t    pairedResult?: { content: string; isError: boolean };\\n119\\t  }): Promise<ProviderResult>;\\n120\\t  summarizeToolResult(i: { toolName: string; content: string }): Promise<ProviderResult>;\\n121\\t  composeTurnRendering(i: { parts: RenderingPart[] }): Promise<ProviderResult>;\\n122\\t  projectLowerBand(i: { rendering: string }): Promise<ProviderResult>;\\n123\\t  // The two summary inputs differ by contract (AC-3.8): detailed receives\\n124\\t  // the members' tool-run receipts (what changed, outcome) alongside the\\n125\\t  // projections; brief receives outcomes only — receipt text is stripped\\n126\\t  // before the provider is called, so brief structurally cannot leak it.\\n127\\t  // The receipt fields are optional in the type for callers without member\\n128\\t  // context (the production chunk handlers always pass them).\\n129\\t  summarizeChunkDetailed(i: {\\n130\\t    memberProjections: string[];\\n131\\t    memberReceipts?: ToolRunReceipt[][];\\n132\\t  }): Promise<ProviderResult>;\\n133\\t  summarizeChunkBrief(i: {\\n134\\t    memberProjections: string[];\\n135\\t    memberOutcomes?: ToolOutcome[][];\\n136\\t  }): Promise<ProviderResult>;\\n137\\t}\\n138\\t\\n139\\texport const PROVIDER_OPERATIONS = [\\n140\\t  \\\"smoothPrompt\\\",\\n141\\t  \\\"summarizeToolCall\\\",\\n142\\t  \\\"summarizeToolResult\\\",\\n143\\t  \\\"composeTurnRendering\\\",\\n144\\t  \\\"projectLowerBand\\\",\\n145\\t  \\\"summarizeChunkDetailed\\\",\\n146\\t  \\\"summarizeChunkBrief\\\",\\n147\\t] as const;\\n148\\t\\n149\\texport type ProviderOperationName = (typeof PROVIDER_OPERATIONS)[number];\\n150\\t\\n151\\t// ── SDK assembly config (tech design §Interfaces) ────────────────\\n152\\texport interface SdkConfig {\\n153\\t  provider: DerivationProvider;\\n154\\t  mode: \\\"background\\\" | \\\"manual\\\";\\n155\\t  clock?: () => Date;\\n156\\t  retry?: { budget: number; backoffBaseMs: number; backoffCapMs: number }; // 3 / 5000 / 60000\\n157\\t  lease?: { durationMs: number }; // 120000\\n158\\t  chunkPolicy?: { targetProjectedTokens: number; maxProjectedTokens: number }; // 2200 / 4400\\n159\\t  view?: SdkViewConfig; // Epic 03: profiles, visibility budgets, compact threshold\\n160\\t}\\n161\\t\\n162\\t// Every optional filled by createSdk's central defaults.\\n163\\texport interface ResolvedSdkConfig {\\n164\\t  provider: DerivationProvider;\\n165\\t  mode: \\\"background\\\" | \\\"manual\\\";\\n166\\t  clock: () => Date;\\n167\\t  retry: { budget: number; backoffBaseMs: number; backoffCapMs: number };\\n168\\t  lease: { durationMs: number };\\n169\\t  chunkPolicy: { targetProjectedTokens: number; maxProjectedTokens: number };\\n170\\t  view: ResolvedViewConfig;\\n171\\t}\\n172\\t\\n173\\t// ── handler contract (DD-6; the map's value type) ────────────────\\n174\\texport interface HandlerRunContext {\\n175\\t  openDb(): DatabaseSync; // short-txn access; NEVER held across provider calls\\n176\\t  provider: DerivationProvider;\\n177\\t  clock: () => Date;\\n178\\t  config: ResolvedSdkConfig;\\n179\\t}\\n180\\t\\n181\\t// A successful handler hands its derived-form content back as data; the\\n182\\t// drain's completion transaction performs the version-checked UPDATE and the\\n183\\t// item-row deletion atomically (tech design §Mechanics: completion is one\\n184\\t// short BEGIN IMMEDIATE doing the form write and the delete). The handler\\n185\\t// never opens that transaction itself, so the version check and the\\n186\\t// done/stale_discarded disposition stay in one place — the queue util.\\n187\\texport interface HandlerFormWrite {\\n188\\t  subjectKind: SubjectKind;\\n189\\t  subjectId: string;\\n190\\t  form: FormKind;\\n191\\t  content: string;\\n192\\t  metadata?: DerivedFormMetadata;\\n193\\t  gaps?: DependencyGap[];\\n194\\t}\\n195\\t\\n196\\t// The completion-transaction hook (Story 3): work that must land atomically\\n197\\t// with the version-checked form writes — chunk placement and the\\n198\\t// close→summary enqueues above all. The queue util invokes it inside the\\n199\\t// completion's BEGIN IMMEDIATE, after the form writes and only when they hit\\n200\\t// (a stale completion must not place a turn or enqueue summaries); onCommit\\n201\\t// registrations flush after that COMMIT succeeds and drop on rollback, so a\\n202\\t// crash leaves either a placed turn with its enqueues or nothing — never a\\n203\\t// derived-but-unplaced turn.\\n204\\texport interface CompletionTx {\\n205\\t  db: DatabaseSync;\\n206\\t  onCommit: (fn: () => void) => void;\\n207\\t}\\n208\\t\\n209\\texport type HandlerOutcome =\\n210\\t  | { ok: true; forms?: HandlerFormWrite[]; onApplied?: (tx: CompletionTx) => void }\\n211\\t  | { ok: false; retryable: boolean; reason: string }\\n212\\t  | { ok: false; blocked: true; reason: string }; // source damage → form blocked, item terminal\\n213\\t\\n214\\t// item is the queue util's WorkItemRecord; typed structurally here so the\\n215\\t// shared layer does not depend on the util's module (and vice versa stays\\n216\\t// one-directional: tech-utils imports shared).\\n217\\texport type WorkHandler = (\\n218\\t  run: HandlerRunContext,\\n219\\t  item: { workItemId: string; kind: string; sourceRef: Record<string, string> },\\n220\\t) => Promise<HandlerOutcome>;\\n221\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"f006cddb-2184-479e-939b-55dccd3023e3\",\"uuid\":\"5bb343cd-a620-46bf-984a-11ce3014e14d\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-11T16:36:19.394Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/shared/derivation.ts\",\"content\":\"// Epic 02 shared vocabulary: the derived-form state machine's types, the\\n// provider seam, and the handler contract. Both owning domains (messages,\\n// turns) consume these; neither owns them — the repair report, the mutation\\n// cascade, and the drain all speak this vocabulary across domain lines, so it\\n// lives in shared/ (tech design §Interfaces, DD-2/DD-7).\\nimport type { DatabaseSync } from \\\"node:sqlite\\\";\\nimport type { ResolvedViewConfig, SdkViewConfig } from \\\"./view.js\\\";\\n\\nexport type SubjectKind = \\\"message\\\" | \\\"turn\\\" | \\\"chunk\\\";\\n\\nexport type FormKind =\\n  | \\\"smoothed_prompt\\\"\\n  | \\\"tool_call_summary\\\"\\n  | \\\"tool_result_summary\\\"\\n  | \\\"turn_rendering\\\"\\n  | \\\"lower_band_projection\\\"\\n  | \\\"chunk_summary_detailed\\\"\\n  | \\\"chunk_summary_brief\\\";\\n\\nexport type DerivedFormState = \\\"pending\\\" | \\\"ready\\\" | \\\"failed\\\" | \\\"blocked\\\";\\n\\n// Outcome on tool-activity summaries — mechanically stamped from the record\\n// (isError/presence), never authored by the provider (AC-2.4).\\nexport type ToolOutcome = \\\"succeeded\\\" | \\\"failed\\\" | \\\"unknown\\\";\\n\\n// A composed form's record of a dependency that fell back during composition:\\n// names the source record and the form that was not ready (AC-3.2/3.3).\\nexport interface DependencyGap {\\n  subjectKind: SubjectKind;\\n  subjectId: string;\\n  form: FormKind;\\n}\\n\\n// The read shape for one derived form's state row (DD-2, DD-3).\\nexport interface DerivedForm {\\n  subjectKind: SubjectKind;\\n  subjectId: string;\\n  form: FormKind;\\n  state: DerivedFormState;\\n  content?: string; // ready only\\n  reason?: string; // failed | blocked\\n  sourceVersion: number; // which version of the source this form derives from (DD-3)\\n  gaps?: DependencyGap[]; // composed forms; landed-with-fallback record\\n  metadata?: DerivedFormMetadata; // mechanically stamped fields; never provider-authored\\n  derivedAt?: string;\\n}\\n\\n// One tool call's or result's receipt within a turn's composed account\\n// (AC-3.8): the account text — what changed, as composed — plus the\\n// mechanically derived outcome. Derived from the composition input, never\\n// from provider prose; stamped on the turn_rendering form so the chunk\\n// summaries can read receipts machine-readably in turn order.\\nexport interface ToolRunReceipt {\\n  messageId: string;\\n  activity: \\\"tool_call\\\" | \\\"tool_result\\\";\\n  account: string;\\n  outcome: ToolOutcome;\\n}\\n\\n// Mechanically stamped form metadata: tool outcomes (AC-2.4), the turn\\n// rendering's tool-run receipts (AC-3.8), plus — at retry exhaustion — the\\n// final attempts/last-error copied from the work item before its row is\\n// deleted (DD-1: the queue is not an audit table; durable outcome detail\\n// lives here).\\nexport interface DerivedFormMetadata {\\n  outcome?: ToolOutcome;\\n  receipts?: ToolRunReceipt[];\\n  attempts?: number;\\n  lastError?: string;\\n}\\n\\n// One row of an owner's repair report (Flow 4): the form's durable state\\n// joined with the queue's mechanical detail for the live item still working\\n// toward it, if any. The five operational situations read from this one row:\\n// never-attempted (pending, no queue), retrying (pending + queue with\\n// attempts > 0), ready, failed (+ reason), blocked (+ reason) — no caller\\n// ever needs a queue API.\\nexport interface FormReportEntry extends DerivedForm {\\n  queue?: {\\n    status: \\\"queued\\\" | \\\"claimed\\\";\\n    attempts: number;\\n    lastError?: string;\\n    eligibleAt?: string;\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n// ── provider seam (DD-7) ─────────────────────────────────────────\\n// Every operation returns content or a structured failure carrying\\n// retryable-or-not; classification is the adapter's duty.\\nexport type ProviderResult =\\n  | { ok: true; text: string }\\n  | { ok: false; retryable: boolean; reason: string };\\n\\n// Message kinds a rendering part can carry — mirrors the intake event-kind\\n// vocabulary minus turn_end (turn_end never projects a message). Mirrored\\n// rather than imported: shared/ may not import domains/.\\nexport type RenderingPartKind =\\n  | \\\"user_prompt\\\"\\n  | \\\"assistant_text\\\"\\n  | \\\"assistant_thinking\\\"\\n  | \\\"runtime_note\\\"\\n  | \\\"tool_call\\\"\\n  | \\\"tool_result\\\";\\n\\nexport interface RenderingPart {\\n  messageId: string;\\n  kind: RenderingPartKind;\\n  text: string; // ready form content, or raw/truncated fallback\\n  fallback: boolean; // true ⇒ gap recorded\\n  outcome?: ToolOutcome; // tool activity only\\n}\\n\\nexport interface DerivationProvider {\\n  smoothPrompt(i: { text: string }): Promise<ProviderResult>;\\n  summarizeToolCall(i: {\\n    toolName: string;\\n    argsJson: string;\\n    pairedResult?: { content: string; isError: boolean };\\n  }): Promise<ProviderResult>;\\n  summarizeToolResult(i: { toolName: string; content: string }): Promise<ProviderResult>;\\n  composeTurnRendering(i: { parts: RenderingPart[] }): Promise<ProviderResult>;\\n  projectLowerBand(i: { rendering: string }): Promise<ProviderResult>;\\n  // The two summary inputs differ by contract (AC-3.8): detailed receives\\n  // the members' tool-run receipts (what changed, outcome) alongside the\\n  // projections; brief receives outcomes only — receipt text is stripped\\n  // before the provider is called, so brief structurally cannot leak it.\\n  // The receipt fields are optional in the type for callers without member\\n  // context (the production chunk handlers always pass them).\\n  summarizeChunkDetailed(i: {\\n    memberProjections: string[];\\n    memberReceipts?: ToolRunReceipt[][];\\n  }): Promise<ProviderResult>;\\n  summarizeChunkBrief(i: {\\n    memberProjections: string[];\\n    memberOutcomes?: ToolOutcome[][];\\n  }): Promise<ProviderResult>;\\n}\\n\\nexport const PROVIDER_OPERATIONS = [\\n  \\\"smoothPrompt\\\",\\n  \\\"summarizeToolCall\\\",\\n  \\\"summarizeToolResult\\\",\\n  \\\"composeTurnRendering\\\",\\n  \\\"projectLowerBand\\\",\\n  \\\"summarizeChunkDetailed\\\",\\n  \\\"summarizeChunkBrief\\\",\\n] as const;\\n\\nexport type ProviderOperationName = (typeof PROVIDER_OPERATIONS)[number];\\n\\n// ── SDK assembly config (tech design §Interfaces) ────────────────\\nexport interface SdkConfig {\\n  provider: DerivationProvider;\\n  mode: \\\"background\\\" | \\\"manual\\\";\\n  clock?: () => Date;\\n  retry?: { budget: number; backoffBaseMs: number; backoffCapMs: number }; // 3 / 5000 / 60000\\n  lease?: { durationMs: number }; // 120000\\n  chunkPolicy?: { targetProjectedTokens: number; maxProjectedTokens: number }; // 2200 / 4400\\n  view?: SdkViewConfig; // Epic 03: profiles, visibility budgets, compact threshold\\n}\\n\\n// Every optional filled by createSdk's central defaults.\\nexport interface ResolvedSdkConfig {\\n  provider: DerivationProvider;\\n  mode: \\\"background\\\" | \\\"manual\\\";\\n  clock: () => Date;\\n  retry: { budget: number; backoffBaseMs: number; backoffCapMs: number };\\n  lease: { durationMs: number };\\n  chunkPolicy: { targetProjectedTokens: number; maxProjectedTokens: number };\\n  view: ResolvedViewConfig;\\n}\\n\\n// ── handler contract (DD-6; the map's value type) ────────────────\\nexport interface HandlerRunContext {\\n  openDb(): DatabaseSync; // short-txn access; NEVER held across provider calls\\n  provider: DerivationProvider;\\n  clock: () => Date;\\n  config: ResolvedSdkConfig;\\n}\\n\\n// A successful handler hands its derived-form content back as data; the\\n// drain's completion transaction performs the version-checked UPDATE and the\\n// item-row deletion atomically (tech design §Mechanics: completion is one\\n// short BEGIN IMMEDIATE doing the form write and the delete). The handler\\n// never opens that transaction itself, so the version check and the\\n// done/stale_discarded disposition stay in one place — the queue util.\\nexport interface HandlerFormWrite {\\n  subjectKind: SubjectKind;\\n  subjectId: string;\\n  form: FormKind;\\n  content: string;\\n  metadata?: DerivedFormMetadata;\\n  gaps?: DependencyGap[];\\n}\\n\\n// The completion-transaction hook (Story 3): work that must land atomically\\n// with the version-checked form writes — chunk placement and the\\n// close→summary enqueues above all. The queue util invokes it inside the\\n// completion's BEGIN IMMEDIATE, after the form writes and only when they hit\\n// (a stale completion must not place a turn or enqueue summaries); onCommit\\n// registrations flush after that COMMIT succeeds and drop on rollback, so a\\n// crash leaves either a placed turn with its enqueues or nothing — never a\\n// derived-but-unplaced turn.\\nexport interface CompletionTx {\\n  db: DatabaseSync;\\n  onCommit: (fn: () => void) => void;\\n}\\n\\nexport type HandlerOutcome =\\n  | { ok: true; forms?: HandlerFormWrite[]; onApplied?: (tx: CompletionTx) => void }\\n  | { ok: false; retryable: boolean; reason: string }\\n  | { ok: false; blocked: true; reason: string }; // source damage → form blocked, item terminal\\n\\n// item is the queue util's WorkItemRecord; typed structurally here so the\\n// shared layer does not depend on the util's module (and vice versa stays\\n// one-directional: tech-utils imports shared).\\nexport type WorkHandler = (\\n  run: HandlerRunContext,\\n  item: { workItemId: string; kind: string; sourceRef: Record<string, string> },\\n) => Promise<HandlerOutcome>;\\n\",\"numLines\":221,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":221}}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/streams/004-implementor.stdout.log:214:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01S1kivpvBqziSoPhB7DeiWV\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\t// Epic 03 shared vocabulary: the thread-view types (tech design §Interface\\n2\\t// Definitions). Shared so cli/sdk/tests import one home; the thread-view\\n3\\t// domain owns the behavior, this module owns only the shapes.\\n4\\t\\n5\\texport type Band = \\\"brief\\\" | \\\"detailed\\\" | \\\"smooth\\\";\\n6\\t\\n7\\texport interface ViewProfile {\\n8\\t  name: string;\\n9\\t  // Target assembled size; whole-entry fills may land under or over (epic\\n10\\t  // Data Contracts — the bound is a target, not a cap).\\n11\\t  lowerBound: number;\\n12\\t  // Band shares of the lower bound; must sum to 100 (AC-2.3).\\n13\\t  percentages: { full: number; smooth: number; detailed: number; brief: number };\\n14\\t}\\n15\\t\\n16\\t// A user profile entry as configured: a full profile under a new name, or a\\n17\\t// field-wise override of a built-in (merged by name, AC-2.2). A partial entry\\n18\\t// whose name matches no built-in has nothing to merge over and is rejected at\\n19\\t// construction (FC-0.2's unknown-override violation).\\n20\\texport interface ViewProfileOverride {\\n21\\t  name: string;\\n22\\t  lowerBound?: number;\\n23\\t  percentages?: Partial<ViewProfile[\\\"percentages\\\"]>;\\n24\\t}\\n25\\t\\n26\\t// Compact-time explicit parameters (AC-2.2): field-wise overrides of the\\n27\\t// base profile, down to single band percentages — the same depth the CLI's\\n28\\t// per-band flags override at. A nested-partial deepening of the tech\\n29\\t// design's `Partial<ViewProfile>` sketch, which could not express a\\n30\\t// single-band override.\\n31\\texport interface ViewCompactParams {\\n32\\t  lowerBound?: number;\\n33\\t  percentages?: Partial<ViewProfile[\\\"percentages\\\"]>;\\n34\\t}\\n35\\t\\n36\\t// Visibility-boundary budgets (AC-4.x): max > target ≥ floor, all positive.\\n37\\texport interface VisibilityBudgets {\\n38\\t  maxTokens: number;\\n39\\t  targetTokens: number;\\n40\\t  floorTokens: number;\\n41\\t}\\n42\\t\\n43\\t// ── SDK assembly config (validated at construction, throws on nonsense\\n44\\t// per the Epic 02 rule) ───────────────────────────────────────────\\n45\\texport interface SdkViewConfig {\\n46\\t  profiles?: ViewProfileOverride[]; // merged over built-ins by name\\n47\\t  visibility?: Partial<VisibilityBudgets>; // defaults: 32000 / 24000 / 8000\\n48\\t  compactThreshold?: number; // status trigger; default 160000\\n49\\t}\\n50\\t\\n51\\t// Every optional filled by createSdk's central defaults; profiles resolved\\n52\\t// to complete, validated entries keyed by name.\\n53\\texport interface ResolvedViewConfig {\\n54\\t  profiles: Readonly<Record<string, ViewProfile>>;\\n55\\t  visibility: VisibilityBudgets;\\n56\\t  compactThreshold: number;\\n57\\t}\\n58\\t\\n59\\t// ── pull / status shapes (the product crossing to the harness) ────\\n60\\t//\\n61\\t// The pull's array shape (Story 1, load-bearing for Stories 2–5): band\\n62\\t// messages first — one `user` message per non-empty band, gradient order\\n63\\t// brief → detailed → smooth, marker header + snapshot bytes verbatim — then\\n64\\t// the tail in record order. Tail messages render by the message-kind mapping\\n65\\t// table (tech design §Tail message rendering), the contract every later\\n66\\t// story renders into:\\n67\\t//\\n68\\t//   | Message kind                       | Role      | Content shape |\\n69\\t//   |------------------------------------|-----------|---------------|\\n70\\t//   | user_prompt                        | user      | text verbatim |\\n71\\t//   | assistant_text                     | assistant | text verbatim |\\n72\\t//   | assistant_thinking                 | assistant | fenced: `[thinking]\\\\n<text>\\\\n[/thinking]` — included (the tail is full fidelity) |\\n73\\t//   | tool_call                          | assistant | `[tool call · <name>] <compact args>` — deterministic arg rendering, abbreviation rule for oversized args |\\n74\\t//   | tool_result (ahead of boundary)    | user      | `[tool result · <name>]\\\\n<full content>` |\\n75\\t//   | tool_result (at-or-behind boundary)| user      | `[tool result · <name> · abridged]\\\\n<summary or deterministic truncation>` (short-form ladder) |\\n76\\t//   | runtime_note                       | user      | `[runtime note] <text>` |\\n77\\texport interface ViewMessage {\\n78\\t  role: \\\"user\\\" | \\\"assistant\\\";\\n79\\t  content: string;\\n80\\t  band?: Band; // band absent ⇒ tail\\n81\\t}\\n82\\t\\n83\\texport interface ViewMeta {\\n84\\t  compactPoint: number | null; // null ⇒ never compacted (AC-1.3)\\n85\\t  coveredFrom: number | null;\\n86\\t  boundaryPosition: number;\\n87\\t  gapCount: number;\\n88\\t  degradedCount: number;\\n89\\t  viewId: string | null;\\n90\\t  createdAt: string | null;\\n91\\t}\\n92\\t\\n93\\texport interface PullResult {\\n94\\t  messages: ViewMessage[];\\n95\\t  meta: ViewMeta;\\n96\\t}\\n97\\t\\n98\\texport interface ViewStatus {\\n99\\t  tailTokens: number;\\n100\\t  threshold: number;\\n101\\t  compactRecommended: boolean;\\n102\\t  derivation: { pending: number; retrying: number; failed: number; blocked: number };\\n103\\t  view: { degraded: number; gaps: number; builtAt: string } | null;\\n104\\t  visibility: { zoneTokens: number; maxTokens: number };\\n105\\t}\\n106\\t\\n107\\t// ── receipts (AC-2.7, AC-3.x) ─────────────────────────────────────\\n108\\texport interface CompactReceipt {\\n109\\t  viewId: string;\\n110\\t  profile: string | null;\\n111\\t  config: ViewProfile[\\\"percentages\\\"] & { lowerBound: number };\\n112\\t  bands: Record<Band, { entries: number; tokens: number }>;\\n113\\t  tailTokens: number;\\n114\\t  // The assembled view's actual total (band tokens + tail tokens) against\\n115\\t  // the configured lower bound — a target, not a cap: whole-entry fills may\\n116\\t  // land under it, indivisible entries over it (AC-2.4; ruling 013).\\n117\\t  totalTokens: number;\\n118\\t  coveredFrom: number;\\n119\\t  compactPoint: number;\\n120\\t  degraded: Array<{ band: Band; subjectId: string; usedForm: string }>;\\n121\\t  gaps: Array<{ band: Band; subjectId: string; reason: string }>;\\n122\\t  // Story 2 ships the compact with the sweep step ABSENT: the field reports\\n123\\t  // the honest literal \\\"absent\\\" — never a fake empty SweepReceipt. Story 3\\n124\\t  // adds the embedded sweep and flips this to SweepReceipt | { skipped: true }\\n125\\t  // (cross-story debt, stated: stories/02-smart-compact.md §Scope out).\\n126\\t  sweep: SweepReceipt | { skipped: true } | \\\"absent\\\";\\n127\\t}\\n128\\t\\n129\\texport interface SweepReceipt {\\n130\\t  owners: Array<{\\n131\\t    owner: \\\"messages\\\" | \\\"turns\\\";\\n132\\t    kind: string;\\n133\\t    ready: number;\\n134\\t    inFlight: number;\\n135\\t    requeued: string[]; // subject ids\\n136\\t    blocked: Array<{ subjectId: string; reason: string }>;\\n137\\t    permanentFailed: Array<{ subjectId: string; reason: string }>;\\n138\\t  }>;\\n139\\t}\\n140\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"f006cddb-2184-479e-939b-55dccd3023e3\",\"uuid\":\"cc2bf78f-9342-4847-86e3-3649f0acaa4f\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-11T16:36:19.926Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/shared/view.ts\",\"content\":\"// Epic 03 shared vocabulary: the thread-view types (tech design §Interface\\n// Definitions). Shared so cli/sdk/tests import one home; the thread-view\\n// domain owns the behavior, this module owns only the shapes.\\n\\nexport type Band = \\\"brief\\\" | \\\"detailed\\\" | \\\"smooth\\\";\\n\\nexport interface ViewProfile {\\n  name: string;\\n  // Target assembled size; whole-entry fills may land under or over (epic\\n  // Data Contracts — the bound is a target, not a cap).\\n  lowerBound: number;\\n  // Band shares of the lower bound; must sum to 100 (AC-2.3).\\n  percentages: { full: number; smooth: number; detailed: number; brief: number };\\n}\\n\\n// A user profile entry as configured: a full profile under a new name, or a\\n// field-wise override of a built-in (merged by name, AC-2.2). A partial entry\\n// whose name matches no built-in has nothing to merge over and is rejected at\\n// construction (FC-0.2's unknown-override violation).\\nexport interface ViewProfileOverride {\\n  name: string;\\n  lowerBound?: number;\\n  percentages?: Partial<ViewProfile[\\\"percentages\\\"]>;\\n}\\n\\n// Compact-time explicit parameters (AC-2.2): field-wise overrides of the\\n// base profile, down to single band percentages — the same depth the CLI's\\n// per-band flags override at. A nested-partial deepening of the tech\\n// design's `Partial<ViewProfile>` sketch, which could not express a\\n// single-band override.\\nexport interface ViewCompactParams {\\n  lowerBound?: number;\\n  percentages?: Partial<ViewProfile[\\\"percentages\\\"]>;\\n}\\n\\n// Visibility-boundary budgets (AC-4.x): max > target ≥ floor, all positive.\\nexport interface VisibilityBudgets {\\n  maxTokens: number;\\n  targetTokens: number;\\n  floorTokens: number;\\n}\\n\\n// ── SDK assembly config (validated at construction, throws on nonsense\\n// per the Epic 02 rule) ───────────────────────────────────────────\\nexport interface SdkViewConfig {\\n  profiles?: ViewProfileOverride[]; // merged over built-ins by name\\n  visibility?: Partial<VisibilityBudgets>; // defaults: 32000 / 24000 / 8000\\n  compactThreshold?: number; // status trigger; default 160000\\n}\\n\\n// Every optional filled by createSdk's central defaults; profiles resolved\\n// to complete, validated entries keyed by name.\\nexport interface ResolvedViewConfig {\\n  profiles: Readonly<Record<string, ViewProfile>>;\\n  visibility: VisibilityBudgets;\\n  compactThreshold: number;\\n}\\n\\n// ── pull / status shapes (the product crossing to the harness) ────\\n//\\n// The pull's array shape (Story 1, load-bearing for Stories 2–5): band\\n// messages first — one `user` message per non-empty band, gradient order\\n// brief → detailed → smooth, marker header + snapshot bytes verbatim — then\\n// the tail in record order. Tail messages render by the message-kind mapping\\n// table (tech design §Tail message rendering), the contract every later\\n// story renders into:\\n//\\n//   | Message kind                       | Role      | Content shape |\\n//   |------------------------------------|-----------|---------------|\\n//   | user_prompt                        | user      | text verbatim |\\n//   | assistant_text                     | assistant | text verbatim |\\n//   | assistant_thinking                 | assistant | fenced: `[thinking]\\\\n<text>\\\\n[/thinking]` — included (the tail is full fidelity) |\\n//   | tool_call                          | assistant | `[tool call · <name>] <compact args>` — deterministic arg rendering, abbreviation rule for oversized args |\\n//   | tool_result (ahead of boundary)    | user      | `[tool result · <name>]\\\\n<full content>` |\\n//   | tool_result (at-or-behind boundary)| user      | `[tool result · <name> · abridged]\\\\n<summary or deterministic truncation>` (short-form ladder) |\\n//   | runtime_note                       | user      | `[runtime note] <text>` |\\nexport interface ViewMessage {\\n  role: \\\"user\\\" | \\\"assistant\\\";\\n  content: string;\\n  band?: Band; // band absent ⇒ tail\\n}\\n\\nexport interface ViewMeta {\\n  compactPoint: number | null; // null ⇒ never compacted (AC-1.3)\\n  coveredFrom: number | null;\\n  boundaryPosition: number;\\n  gapCount: number;\\n  degradedCount: number;\\n  viewId: string | null;\\n  createdAt: string | null;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface PullResult {\\n  messages: ViewMessage[];\\n  meta: ViewMeta;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface ViewStatus {\\n  tailTokens: number;\\n  threshold: number;\\n  compactRecommended: boolean;\\n  derivation: { pending: number; retrying: number; failed: number; blocked: number };\\n  view: { degraded: number; gaps: number; builtAt: string } | null;\\n  visibility: { zoneTokens: number; maxTokens: number };\\n}\\n\\n// ── receipts (AC-2.7, AC-3.x) ─────────────────────────────────────\\nexport interface CompactReceipt {\\n  viewId: string;\\n  profile: string | null;\\n  config: ViewProfile[\\\"percentages\\\"] & { lowerBound: number };\\n  bands: Record<Band, { entries: number; tokens: number }>;\\n  tailTokens: number;\\n  // The assembled view's actual total (band tokens + tail tokens) against\\n  // the configured lower bound — a target, not a cap: whole-entry fills may\\n  // land under it, indivisible entries over it (AC-2.4; ruling 013).\\n  totalTokens: number;\\n  coveredFrom: number;\\n  compactPoint: number;\\n  degraded: Array<{ band: Band; subjectId: string; usedForm: string }>;\\n  gaps: Array<{ band: Band; subjectId: string; reason: string }>;\\n  // Story 2 ships the compact with the sweep step ABSENT: the field reports\\n  // the honest literal \\\"absent\\\" — never a fake empty SweepReceipt. Story 3\\n  // adds the embedded sweep and flips this to SweepReceipt | { skipped: true }\\n  // (cross-story debt, stated: stories/02-smart-compact.md §Scope out).\\n  sweep: SweepReceipt | { skipped: true } | \\\"absent\\\";\\n}\\n\\nexport interface SweepReceipt {\\n  owners: Array<{\\n    owner: \\\"messages\\\" | \\\"turns\\\";\\n    kind: string;\\n    ready: number;\\n    inFlight: number;\\n    requeued: string[]; // subject ids\\n    blocked: Array<{ subjectId: string; reason: string }>;\\n    permanentFailed: Array<{ subjectId: string; reason: string }>;\\n  }>;\\n}\\n\",\"numLines\":140,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":140}}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/streams/004-implementor.stdout.log:245:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01UU2jvuZ5g2CouTywN2GNSE\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"167:  // version-scoped item id keeps the requeue idempotent.\\n287:// inverted; the requeue's join from the named form back to its queue site.\\n303:export async function requeue(\\n314:        reason: `form ${target.form} is not message-owned; messages.requeue repairs smoothed_prompt, tool_call_summary, tool_result_summary`,\\n370:    return storageFailure(`requeue failed: ${reason}`);\\n323:// messages.requeue — blocked refused with the stored damage reason, missing\\n325:// the no-op check + enqueue in one transaction. A successful requeue rebuilds\\n328:export async function requeue(\\n339:        reason: `form ${target.form} is not a ${target.subjectKind}-owned form; turns.requeue repairs turn_rendering and lower_band_projection (turn) or chunk_summary_detailed and chunk_summary_brief (chunk)`,\\n396:    return storageFailure(`requeue failed: ${reason}`);\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"f006cddb-2184-479e-939b-55dccd3023e3\",\"uuid\":\"1b29f6e9-3317-4b2b-a497-0b038930b68a\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-11T16:36:29.110Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"stdout\":\"167:  // version-scoped item id keeps the requeue idempotent.\\n287:// inverted; the requeue's join from the named form back to its queue site.\\n303:export async function requeue(\\n314:        reason: `form ${target.form} is not message-owned; messages.requeue repairs smoothed_prompt, tool_call_summary, tool_result_summary`,\\n370:    return storageFailure(`requeue failed: ${reason}`);\\n323:// messages.requeue — blocked refused with the stored damage reason, missing\\n325:// the no-op check + enqueue in one transaction. A successful requeue rebuilds\\n328:export async function requeue(\\n339:        reason: `form ${target.form} is not a ${target.subjectKind}-owned form; turns.requeue repairs turn_rendering and lower_band_projection (turn) or chunk_summary_detailed and chunk_summary_brief (chunk)`,\\n396:    return storageFailure(`requeue failed: ${reason}`);\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/streams/004-implementor.stdout.log:278:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01T8jfMv4sZq57ZvvEa7ZYem\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"    db.exec(\\\"BEGIN IMMEDIATE;\\\");\\n    try {\\n      db.prepare(\\n        `UPDATE work_item\\n         SET status = 'queued', attempts = ?, last_error = ?,\\n             claimed_at = NULL, claim_expires_at = NULL, eligible_at = ?\\n         WHERE work_item_id = ?`,\\n      ).run(attempts, opts.reason, eligibleAt, item.workItemId);\\n      db.exec(\\\"COMMIT;\\\");\\n    } catch (cause) {\\n      db.exec(\\\"ROLLBACK;\\\");\\n      throw cause;\\n    }\\n    return { terminal: false, attempts, eligibleAt };\\n  }\\n  failTerminal(db, item, { reason: opts.reason, formState: \\\"failed\\\", attempts, now: opts.now });\\n  return { terminal: true, attempts };\\n}\\n\\n// Cascade tidy (tech design issue 1): delete still-queued items for the given\\n// (kind, sourceRef) targets, returning the deleted ids for the mutation\\n// result's `superseded` list. Runs inside the caller's ambient transaction —\\n// the cascade owns the BEGIN/COMMIT — so no transaction is opened here.\\n// Claimed items are deliberately left alone: the source-version check (DD-3)\\n// discards their stale completions. Ships here as mechanics; its only caller\\n// is Story 5's cascade.\\nexport function supersedeQueued(\\n  db: DatabaseSync,\\n  targets: ReadonlyArray<{ kind: WorkKind; sourceRef: WorkSourceRef }>,\\n): string[] {\\n  const ids: string[] = [];\\n  const remove = db.prepare(\\n    `DELETE FROM work_item WHERE status = 'queued' AND kind = ? AND source_ref = ?\\n     RETURNING work_item_id`,\\n  );\\n  for (const target of targets) {\\n    const rows = remove.all(target.kind, JSON.stringify(target.sourceRef)) as unknown as Array<{\\n      work_item_id: string;\\n    }>;\\n    for (const row of rows) ids.push(row.work_item_id);\\n  }\\n  return ids;\\n}\\n\\n// The requeue no-op rule's EXISTS check (AC-4.5): is there a live item —\\n// queued or in flight — for this kind and source at this source version?\\n// Runs inside the caller's requeue transaction so the check and the enqueue\\n// commit together (anti-shim: a check-then-enqueue split across transactions\\n// reintroduces the duplicate-work race). Version-scoped on purpose: a\\n// claimed pre-mutation item at an older version is dying work whose\\n// completion DD-3 will discard — it must not block the repair.\\nexport function hasLiveItem(\\n  db: DatabaseSync,\\n  kind: WorkKind,\\n  sourceRef: WorkSourceRef,\\n  sourceVersion: number,\\n): boolean {\\n  const row = db\\n    .prepare(\\n      `SELECT 1 FROM work_item\\n       WHERE status IN ('queued', 'claimed') AND kind = ? AND source_ref = ?\\n         AND COALESCE(json_extract(payload, '$.sourceVersion'), 1) = ?\\n       LIMIT 1`,\\n    )\\n    .get(kind, JSON.stringify(sourceRef), sourceVersion);\\n  return row !== undefined;\\n}\\n\\n// Live items left in the queue — the drain report's `remaining` and the\\n// repair report's join source (Story 4).\\nexport function countLiveItems(db: DatabaseSync): number {\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"f006cddb-2184-479e-939b-55dccd3023e3\",\"uuid\":\"2c16ac78-a73b-4620-b8c4-0677ca0e7a93\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-11T16:36:41.034Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"stdout\":\"    db.exec(\\\"BEGIN IMMEDIATE;\\\");\\n    try {\\n      db.prepare(\\n        `UPDATE work_item\\n         SET status = 'queued', attempts = ?, last_error = ?,\\n             claimed_at = NULL, claim_expires_at = NULL, eligible_at = ?\\n         WHERE work_item_id = ?`,\\n      ).run(attempts, opts.reason, eligibleAt, item.workItemId);\\n      db.exec(\\\"COMMIT;\\\");\\n    } catch (cause) {\\n      db.exec(\\\"ROLLBACK;\\\");\\n      throw cause;\\n    }\\n    return { terminal: false, attempts, eligibleAt };\\n  }\\n  failTerminal(db, item, { reason: opts.reason, formState: \\\"failed\\\", attempts, now: opts.now });\\n  return { terminal: true, attempts };\\n}\\n\\n// Cascade tidy (tech design issue 1): delete still-queued items for the given\\n// (kind, sourceRef) targets, returning the deleted ids for the mutation\\n// result's `superseded` list. Runs inside the caller's ambient transaction —\\n// the cascade owns the BEGIN/COMMIT — so no transaction is opened here.\\n// Claimed items are deliberately left alone: the source-version check (DD-3)\\n// discards their stale completions. Ships here as mechanics; its only caller\\n// is Story 5's cascade.\\nexport function supersedeQueued(\\n  db: DatabaseSync,\\n  targets: ReadonlyArray<{ kind: WorkKind; sourceRef: WorkSourceRef }>,\\n): string[] {\\n  const ids: string[] = [];\\n  const remove = db.prepare(\\n    `DELETE FROM work_item WHERE status = 'queued' AND kind = ? AND source_ref = ?\\n     RETURNING work_item_id`,\\n  );\\n  for (const target of targets) {\\n    const rows = remove.all(target.kind, JSON.stringify(target.sourceRef)) as unknown as Array<{\\n      work_item_id: string;\\n    }>;\\n    for (const row of rows) ids.push(row.work_item_id);\\n  }\\n  return ids;\\n}\\n\\n// The requeue no-op rule's EXISTS check (AC-4.5): is there a live item —\\n// queued or in flight — for this kind and source at this source version?\\n// Runs inside the caller's requeue transaction so the check and the enqueue\\n// commit together (anti-shim: a check-then-enqueue split across transactions\\n// reintroduces the duplicate-work race). Version-scoped on purpose: a\\n// claimed pre-mutation item at an older version is dying work whose\\n// completion DD-3 will discard — it must not block the repair.\\nexport function hasLiveItem(\\n  db: DatabaseSync,\\n  kind: WorkKind,\\n  sourceRef: WorkSourceRef,\\n  sourceVersion: number,\\n): boolean {\\n  const row = db\\n    .prepare(\\n      `SELECT 1 FROM work_item\\n       WHERE status IN ('queued', 'claimed') AND kind = ? AND source_ref = ?\\n         AND COALESCE(json_extract(payload, '$.sourceVersion'), 1) = ?\\n       LIMIT 1`,\\n    )\\n    .get(kind, JSON.stringify(sourceRef), sourceVersion);\\n  return row !== undefined;\\n}\\n\\n// Live items left in the queue — the drain report's `remaining` and the\\n// repair report's join source (Story 4).\\nexport function countLiveItems(db: DatabaseSync): number {\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/streams/004-implementor.stdout.log:285:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01EE1dYbvNZjY4heDA9U9jU9\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\t// The Epic 03 derived-thread fixture (Story 0, FC-0.3/0.4/0.5): one recorded\\n2\\t// conversation — 12 turns, 4 chunks, tool-heavy middle — drained through the\\n3\\t// real Epic 02 machinery (intake → enqueue → drain → handlers) against the\\n4\\t// deterministic provider double into known form states. States are reached\\n5\\t// through production paths, never hand-written rows (the anti-shim line\\n6\\t// FC-0.3 enforces): the failed states come from scripted provider failures\\n7\\t// consumed by the real retry/exhaustion mechanics, and blocked comes from\\n8\\t// real source damage on a sacrificial sibling thread. Every later Epic 03\\n9\\t// story compacts against what this builder returns.\\n10\\timport {\\n11\\t  createSdk,\\n12\\t  type FormReportEntry,\\n13\\t  type Lhc,\\n14\\t  type MessageEventInput,\\n15\\t} from \\\"../../src/index.js\\\";\\n16\\timport { corruptTwoOpenTurns } from \\\"./corrupt.js\\\";\\n17\\timport { createProviderDouble, type ProviderDouble } from \\\"./provider-double.js\\\";\\n18\\timport { readChunks, type ChunkSnapshot } from \\\"./threads.js\\\";\\n19\\timport { validEvent, type TempStore } from \\\"./index.js\\\";\\n20\\t\\n21\\t// Reason classes the scripted failures stamp, chosen from the sweep\\n22\\t// classification table's vocabulary (tech design §Spec Validation): a\\n23\\t// rate-limit class reads transient, a content-refusal class reads permanent —\\n24\\t// FC-0.4's distinguishable-on-read-back guarantee, proven here before\\n25\\t// Story 3 depends on it.\\n26\\texport const TRANSIENT_EXHAUST_REASON =\\n27\\t  \\\"rate_limit: scripted transient exhaustion (fixture)\\\";\\n28\\texport const PERMANENT_FAILURE_REASON =\\n29\\t  \\\"content_refusal: scripted permanent failure (fixture)\\\";\\n30\\t\\n31\\t// Chunk policy pinned so the 12 fixed-shape turns cut into exactly 4 chunks\\n32\\t// (3 members each; c1–c3 closed, c4 still open). Projections from the\\n33\\t// deterministic double are near-constant in size (`projection(<digest>:<40\\n34\\t// chars>)`), so the cut is stable; the builder asserts the shape and throws\\n35\\t// if drift ever moves it.\\n36\\tconst FIXTURE_CHUNK_POLICY = { targetProjectedTokens: 90, maxProjectedTokens: 4400 };\\n37\\t\\n38\\tconst TURN_COUNT = 12;\\n39\\tconst TOOL_HEAVY_TURNS = new Set([5, 6, 7, 8]);\\n40\\t\\n41\\tfunction turnEvents(turn: number): MessageEventInput[] {\\n42\\t  const events: MessageEventInput[] = [\\n43\\t    validEvent(\\\"user_prompt\\\", {\\n44\\t      payload: { text: `turn ${turn}: please investigate area ${turn}` },\\n45\\t    }),\\n46\\t    validEvent(\\\"assistant_thinking\\\", {\\n47\\t      payload: { text: `considering what area ${turn} contains` },\\n48\\t    }),\\n49\\t  ];\\n50\\t  if (TOOL_HEAVY_TURNS.has(turn)) {\\n51\\t    // The tool-heavy middle: two tool runs per turn — what gives Story 4 a\\n52\\t    // realistic over-max zone of tool results to age behind the boundary.\\n53\\t    for (const run of [1, 2]) {\\n54\\t      const toolCallId = `call-fx-${turn}-${run}`;\\n55\\t      events.push(\\n56\\t        validEvent(\\\"tool_call\\\", {\\n57\\t          payload: {\\n58\\t            toolCallId,\\n59\\t            toolName: \\\"read_file\\\",\\n60\\t            arguments: { path: `area-${turn}/file-${run}.txt` },\\n61\\t          },\\n62\\t        }),\\n63\\t        validEvent(\\\"tool_result\\\", {\\n64\\t          payload: {\\n65\\t            toolCallId,\\n66\\t            content: `contents of area-${turn}/file-${run}.txt: detail ${turn}.${run} with enough text to summarize`,\\n67\\t            isError: false,\\n68\\t          },\\n69\\t        }),\\n70\\t      );\\n71\\t    }\\n72\\t  }\\n73\\t  events.push(\\n74\\t    validEvent(\\\"assistant_text\\\", { payload: { text: `findings for area ${turn}` } }),\\n75\\t    validEvent(\\\"turn_end\\\"),\\n76\\t  );\\n77\\t  return events;\\n78\\t}\\n79\\t\\n80\\texport interface DerivedThreadFixture {\\n81\\t  filePath: string;\\n82\\t  sdk: Lhc;\\n83\\t  double: ProviderDouble;\\n84\\t  turnIds: string[]; // t1..t12\\n85\\t  chunks: ChunkSnapshot;\\n86\\t  // The two manufactured failed subjects (tool_result_summary forms), reached\\n87\\t  // through real retry exhaustion / terminal failure — absent when failures\\n88\\t  // are disabled for a variant.\\n89\\t  failedTransientMessageId?: string;\\n90\\t  failedPermanentMessageId?: string;\\n91\\t  // The straggler variant's turnId-null messages: one between two turns, one\\n92\\t  // after the last turn — absent unless stragglers are enabled.\\n93\\t  stragglerBetweenMessageId?: string;\\n94\\t  stragglerTrailingMessageId?: string;\\n95\\t}\\n96\\t\\n97\\texport interface DerivedThreadOptions {\\n98\\t  failures?: boolean; // default true: manufacture the two failed states\\n99\\t  stragglers?: boolean; // default false: insert the turnless runtime notes\\n100\\t}\\n101\\t\\n102\\tasync function send(\\n103\\t  sdk: Lhc,\\n104\\t  filePath: string,\\n105\\t  batch: readonly MessageEventInput[],\\n106\\t): Promise<string[]> {\\n107\\t  const result = await sdk.intakeStream.messageEvents({ filePath }, batch);\\n108\\t  if (!result.ok) throw new Error(`fixture batch failed: ${result.error.reason}`);\\n109\\t  return result.value.events.map((entry) => entry.messageId ?? \\\"\\\");\\n110\\t}\\n111\\t\\n112\\tasync function drain(sdk: Lhc, filePath: string): Promise<void> {\\n113\\t  const report = await sdk.work.drain({ filePath });\\n114\\t  if (!report.ok) throw new Error(`fixture drain failed: ${report.error.reason}`);\\n115\\t  if (report.value.stoppedBecause !== \\\"empty\\\" || report.value.remaining !== 0) {\\n116\\t    throw new Error(\\n117\\t      `fixture drain left work behind (stopped: ${report.value.stoppedBecause}, remaining: ${report.value.remaining})`,\\n118\\t    );\\n119\\t  }\\n120\\t}\\n121\\t\\n122\\tfunction failedEntries(entries: readonly FormReportEntry[], reason: string): FormReportEntry[] {\\n123\\t  return entries.filter((entry) => entry.state === \\\"failed\\\" && entry.reason === reason);\\n124\\t}\\n125\\t\\n126\\texport async function derivedThreadFixture(\\n127\\t  store: TempStore,\\n128\\t  opts: DerivedThreadOptions = {},\\n129\\t): Promise<DerivedThreadFixture> {\\n130\\t  const failures = opts.failures ?? true;\\n131\\t  const stragglers = opts.stragglers ?? false;\\n132\\t\\n133\\t  const double = createProviderDouble();\\n134\\t  const sdk = createSdk({\\n135\\t    provider: double,\\n136\\t    mode: \\\"manual\\\",\\n137\\t    retry: { budget: 3, backoffBaseMs: 0, backoffCapMs: 0 },\\n138\\t    chunkPolicy: FIXTURE_CHUNK_POLICY,\\n139\\t  });\\n140\\t\\n141\\t  const filePath = store.threadPath();\\n142\\t  const created = await sdk.threads.newThread({ filePath, registryPath: store.registryPath });\\n143\\t  if (!created.ok) throw new Error(`fixture thread creation failed: ${created.error.reason}`);\\n144\\t\\n145\\t  const turnIds: string[] = [];\\n146\\t  const fixture: DerivedThreadFixture = {\\n147\\t    filePath,\\n148\\t    sdk,\\n149\\t    double,\\n150\\t    turnIds,\\n151\\t    chunks: { chunks: [], members: [] },\\n152\\t  };\\n153\\t\\n154\\t  for (let turn = 1; turn <= TURN_COUNT; turn += 1) {\\n155\\t    if (failures && turn === 6) {\\n156\\t      // Retryable failures consumed to exhaustion by the head-first drain:\\n157\\t      // the first tool_result_summary item of this batch takes all three\\n158\\t      // attempts and lands failed with the transient reason class.\\n159\\t      double.failKind(\\\"tool_result_summary\\\", 3, {\\n160\\t        retryable: true,\\n161\\t        reason: TRANSIENT_EXHAUST_REASON,\\n162\\t      });\\n163\\t    }\\n164\\t    if (failures && turn === 7) {\\n165\\t      // One non-retryable failure: terminal on the first attempt — the\\n166\\t      // permanent reason class, attempts 1.\\n167\\t      double.failKind(\\\"tool_result_summary\\\", 1, {\\n168\\t        retryable: false,\\n169\\t        reason: PERMANENT_FAILURE_REASON,\\n170\\t      });\\n171\\t    }\\n172\\t    const messageIds = await send(sdk, filePath, turnEvents(turn));\\n173\\t    // Batch shape is fixed for tool-heavy turns: prompt, thinking, call,\\n174\\t    // result, call, result, text, end — index 3 is the first tool result,\\n175\\t    // the scripted failures' subject.\\n176\\t    const firstToolResultId = messageIds[3];\\n177\\t    if (failures && (turn === 6 || turn === 7)) {\\n178\\t      if (firstToolResultId === undefined || firstToolResultId === \\\"\\\") {\\n179\\t        throw new Error(`fixture invariant: turn ${turn} carries no first tool result message`);\\n180\\t      }\\n181\\t      if (turn === 6) fixture.failedTransientMessageId = firstToolResultId;\\n182\\t      else fixture.failedPermanentMessageId = firstToolResultId;\\n183\\t    }\\n184\\t    await drain(sdk, filePath);\\n185\\t\\n186\\t    if (stragglers && turn === 3) {\\n187\\t      // A runtime note between turn 3's end and turn 4's prompt: projected\\n188\\t      // with turnId = null (the Epic 01 straggler), selection rule 6 / G4.\\n189\\t      const noteIds = await send(sdk, filePath, [\\n190\\t        validEvent(\\\"runtime_note\\\", {\\n191\\t          payload: { text: \\\"harness restarted between turns (fixture straggler)\\\" },\\n192\\t        }),\\n193\\t      ]);\\n194\\t      const noteId = noteIds[0];\\n195\\t      if (noteId === undefined || noteId === \\\"\\\") {\\n196\\t        throw new Error(\\\"fixture invariant: between-turns straggler did not project\\\");\\n197\\t      }\\n198\\t      fixture.stragglerBetweenMessageId = noteId;\\n199\\t    }\\n200\\t    turnIds.push(`t${turn}`);\\n201\\t  }\\n202\\t\\n203\\t  if (stragglers) {\\n204\\t    const noteIds = await send(sdk, filePath, [\\n205\\t      validEvent(\\\"runtime_note\\\", {\\n206\\t        payload: { text: \\\"session closing note after the last turn (fixture straggler)\\\" },\\n207\\t      }),\\n208\\t    ]);\\n209\\t    const noteId = noteIds[0];\\n210\\t    if (noteId === undefined || noteId === \\\"\\\") {\\n211\\t      throw new Error(\\\"fixture invariant: trailing straggler did not project\\\");\\n212\\t    }\\n213\\t    fixture.stragglerTrailingMessageId = noteId;\\n214\\t    await drain(sdk, filePath);\\n215\\t  }\\n216\\t\\n217\\t  // Shape invariants the chunk policy is pinned for: 12 closed turns in 4\\n218\\t  // chunks, the first three closed. A failure here means the deterministic\\n219\\t  // substrate moved (provider output or tokenizer), not a flaky test.\\n220\\t  fixture.chunks = readChunks(filePath);\\n221\\t  if (fixture.chunks.chunks.length !== 4) {\\n222\\t    throw new Error(\\n223\\t      `fixture invariant: expected 4 chunks, got ${fixture.chunks.chunks.length} — re-pin FIXTURE_CHUNK_POLICY`,\\n224\\t    );\\n225\\t  }\\n226\\t  const closed = fixture.chunks.chunks.filter((chunk) => chunk.status === \\\"closed\\\").length;\\n227\\t  if (closed !== 3) {\\n228\\t    throw new Error(\\n229\\t      `fixture invariant: expected chunks c1–c3 closed, got ${closed} closed — re-pin FIXTURE_CHUNK_POLICY`,\\n230\\t    );\\n231\\t  }\\n232\\t\\n233\\t  if (failures) {\\n234\\t    // Verify the manufactured states by read-back through the owning report\\n235\\t    // surface before handing the fixture to any test (FC-0.3's enforcement\\n236\\t    // lives in the tests; this guards the builder's own contract).\\n237\\t    const report = await sdk.messages.report({ filePath });\\n238\\t    if (!report.ok) throw new Error(`fixture report failed: ${report.error.reason}`);\\n239\\t    const transient = failedEntries(report.value, TRANSIENT_EXHAUST_REASON);\\n240\\t    const permanent = failedEntries(report.value, PERMANENT_FAILURE_REASON);\\n241\\t    if (\\n242\\t      transient.length !== 1 ||\\n243\\t      transient[0]?.subjectId !== fixture.failedTransientMessageId ||\\n244\\t      permanent.length !== 1 ||\\n245\\t      permanent[0]?.subjectId !== fixture.failedPermanentMessageId\\n246\\t    ) {\\n247\\t      throw new Error(\\n248\\t        `fixture invariant: expected exactly one transient-failed and one permanent-failed tool_result_summary on the named subjects`,\\n249\\t      );\\n250\\t    }\\n251\\t  }\\n252\\t\\n253\\t  return fixture;\\n254\\t}\\n255\\t\\n256\\t// The turnless-straggler variant (FC-0.5, golden G4's substrate): the same\\n257\\t// conversation with a runtime note between two turns and one after the last\\n258\\t// turn, fully drained, no manufactured failures.\\n259\\texport async function stragglerVariantThread(store: TempStore): Promise<DerivedThreadFixture> {\\n260\\t  return derivedThreadFixture(store, { failures: false, stragglers: true });\\n261\\t}\\n262\\t\\n263\\t// The canonical-corruption variant (FC-0.5, Epic 01 fixture pattern): a\\n264\\t// short real conversation, drained clean, then damaged below the SDK into\\n265\\t// the two-open-turns state no public operation can produce. Canonical\\n266\\t// consumers refuse it with state_corruption.\\n267\\texport async function corruptedVariantThread(\\n268\\t  store: TempStore,\\n269\\t): Promise<{ filePath: string; sdk: Lhc }> {\\n270\\t  const double = createProviderDouble();\\n271\\t  const sdk = createSdk({ provider: double, mode: \\\"manual\\\" });\\n272\\t  const filePath = store.threadPath();\\n273\\t  const created = await sdk.threads.newThread({ filePath, registryPath: store.registryPath });\\n274\\t  if (!created.ok) throw new Error(`fixture thread creation failed: ${created.error.reason}`);\\n275\\t  for (let turn = 1; turn <= 3; turn += 1) {\\n276\\t    await send(sdk, filePath, turnEvents(turn));\\n277\\t  }\\n278\\t  await drain(sdk, filePath);\\n279\\t  // Open a turn through real intake, then add a second open row: two open\\n280\\t  // turns, the Epic 01 invariant violation.\\n281\\t  await send(sdk, filePath, [\\n282\\t    validEvent(\\\"user_prompt\\\", { payload: { text: \\\"left open before the damage\\\" } }),\\n283\\t  ]);\\n284\\t  corruptTwoOpenTurns(filePath);\\n285\\t  return { filePath, sdk };\\n286\\t}\\n287\\t\\n288\\t// The blocked state's sacrificial sibling (FC-0.3): a closed turn whose\\n289\\t// queued derivation meets real source damage at drain time — the handler\\n290\\t// finds two open turns and lands the turn forms blocked through the\\n291\\t// production terminal path, never a hand-written row.\\n292\\texport async function blockedSiblingThread(\\n293\\t  store: TempStore,\\n294\\t): Promise<{ filePath: string; sdk: Lhc; blockedTurnId: string }> {\\n295\\t  const double = createProviderDouble();\\n296\\t  const sdk = createSdk({ provider: double, mode: \\\"manual\\\" });\\n297\\t  const filePath = store.threadPath();\\n298\\t  const created = await sdk.threads.newThread({ filePath, registryPath: store.registryPath });\\n299\\t  if (!created.ok) throw new Error(`fixture thread creation failed: ${created.error.reason}`);\\n300\\t  // Turn 1 closes (its turn_derivation queues); a second turn opens through\\n301\\t  // real intake; the corruption writer adds another open row. The drain then\\n302\\t  // claims t1's derivation against a record with two open turns.\\n303\\t  await send(sdk, filePath, turnEvents(1));\\n304\\t  await send(sdk, filePath, [\\n305\\t    validEvent(\\\"user_prompt\\\", { payload: { text: \\\"left open before the damage\\\" } }),\\n306\\t  ]);\\n307\\t  corruptTwoOpenTurns(filePath);\\n308\\t  const report = await sdk.work.drain({ filePath });\\n309\\t  if (!report.ok) throw new Error(`fixture drain failed: ${report.error.reason}`);\\n310\\t  const blocked = report.value.ran.find(\\n311\\t    (entry) => entry.kind === \\\"turn_derivation\\\" && entry.disposition === \\\"failed_terminal\\\",\\n312\\t  );\\n313\\t  if (blocked === undefined) {\\n314\\t    throw new Error(\\\"fixture invariant: turn_derivation expected to land terminal on damage\\\");\\n315\\t  }\\n316\\t  return { filePath, sdk, blockedTurnId: \\\"t1\\\" };\\n317\\t}\\n318\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"f006cddb-2184-479e-939b-55dccd3023e3\",\"uuid\":\"3996bdbd-b8f8-49fc-ac54-1e2022834f28\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-11T16:36:42.047Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/test/fixtures/view-thread.ts\",\"content\":\"// The Epic 03 derived-thread fixture (Story 0, FC-0.3/0.4/0.5): one recorded\\n// conversation — 12 turns, 4 chunks, tool-heavy middle — drained through the\\n// real Epic 02 machinery (intake → enqueue → drain → handlers) against the\\n// deterministic provider double into known form states. States are reached\\n// through production paths, never hand-written rows (the anti-shim line\\n// FC-0.3 enforces): the failed states come from scripted provider failures\\n// consumed by the real retry/exhaustion mechanics, and blocked comes from\\n// real source damage on a sacrificial sibling thread. Every later Epic 03\\n// story compacts against what this builder returns.\\nimport {\\n  createSdk,\\n  type FormReportEntry,\\n  type Lhc,\\n  type MessageEventInput,\\n} from \\\"../../src/index.js\\\";\\nimport { corruptTwoOpenTurns } from \\\"./corrupt.js\\\";\\nimport { createProviderDouble, type ProviderDouble } from \\\"./provider-double.js\\\";\\nimport { readChunks, type ChunkSnapshot } from \\\"./threads.js\\\";\\nimport { validEvent, type TempStore } from \\\"./index.js\\\";\\n\\n// Reason classes the scripted failures stamp, chosen from the sweep\\n// classification table's vocabulary (tech design §Spec Validation): a\\n// rate-limit class reads transient, a content-refusal class reads permanent —\\n// FC-0.4's distinguishable-on-read-back guarantee, proven here before\\n// Story 3 depends on it.\\nexport const TRANSIENT_EXHAUST_REASON =\\n  \\\"rate_limit: scripted transient exhaustion (fixture)\\\";\\nexport const PERMANENT_FAILURE_REASON =\\n  \\\"content_refusal: scripted permanent failure (fixture)\\\";\\n\\n// Chunk policy pinned so the 12 fixed-shape turns cut into exactly 4 chunks\\n// (3 members each; c1–c3 closed, c4 still open). Projections from the\\n// deterministic double are near-constant in size (`projection(<digest>:<40\\n// chars>)`), so the cut is stable; the builder asserts the shape and throws\\n// if drift ever moves it.\\nconst FIXTURE_CHUNK_POLICY = { targetProjectedTokens: 90, maxProjectedTokens: 4400 };\\n\\nconst TURN_COUNT = 12;\\nconst TOOL_HEAVY_TURNS = new Set([5, 6, 7, 8]);\\n\\nfunction turnEvents(turn: number): MessageEventInput[] {\\n  const events: MessageEventInput[] = [\\n    validEvent(\\\"user_prompt\\\", {\\n      payload: { text: `turn ${turn}: please investigate area ${turn}` },\\n    }),\\n    validEvent(\\\"assistant_thinking\\\", {\\n      payload: { text: `considering what area ${turn} contains` },\\n    }),\\n  ];\\n  if (TOOL_HEAVY_TURNS.has(turn)) {\\n    // The tool-heavy middle: two tool runs per turn — what gives Story 4 a\\n    // realistic over-max zone of tool results to age behind the boundary.\\n    for (const run of [1, 2]) {\\n      const toolCallId = `call-fx-${turn}-${run}`;\\n      events.push(\\n        validEvent(\\\"tool_call\\\", {\\n          payload: {\\n            toolCallId,\\n            toolName: \\\"read_file\\\",\\n            arguments: { path: `area-${turn}/file-${run}.txt` },\\n          },\\n        }),\\n        validEvent(\\\"tool_result\\\", {\\n          payload: {\\n            toolCallId,\\n            content: `contents of area-${turn}/file-${run}.txt: detail ${turn}.${run} with enough text to summarize`,\\n            isError: false,\\n          },\\n        }),\\n      );\\n    }\\n  }\\n  events.push(\\n    validEvent(\\\"assistant_text\\\", { payload: { text: `findings for area ${turn}` } }),\\n    validEvent(\\\"turn_end\\\"),\\n  );\\n  return events;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface DerivedThreadFixture {\\n  filePath: string;\\n  sdk: Lhc;\\n  double: ProviderDouble;\\n  turnIds: string[]; // t1..t12\\n  chunks: ChunkSnapshot;\\n  // The two manufactured failed subjects (tool_result_summary forms), reached\\n  // through real retry exhaustion / terminal failure — absent when failures\\n  // are disabled for a variant.\\n  failedTransientMessageId?: string;\\n  failedPermanentMessageId?: string;\\n  // The straggler variant's turnId-null messages: one between two turns, one\\n  // after the last turn — absent unless stragglers are enabled.\\n  stragglerBetweenMessageId?: string;\\n  stragglerTrailingMessageId?: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface DerivedThreadOptions {\\n  failures?: boolean; // default true: manufacture the two failed states\\n  stragglers?: boolean; // default false: insert the turnless runtime notes\\n}\\n\\nasync function send(\\n  sdk: Lhc,\\n  filePath: string,\\n  batch: readonly MessageEventInput[],\\n): Promise<string[]> {\\n  const result = await sdk.intakeStream.messageEvents({ filePath }, batch);\\n  if (!result.ok) throw new Error(`fixture batch failed: ${result.error.reason}`);\\n  return result.value.events.map((entry) => entry.messageId ?? \\\"\\\");\\n}\\n\\nasync function drain(sdk: Lhc, filePath: string): Promise<void> {\\n  const report = await sdk.work.drain({ filePath });\\n  if (!report.ok) throw new Error(`fixture drain failed: ${report.error.reason}`);\\n  if (report.value.stoppedBecause !== \\\"empty\\\" || report.value.remaining !== 0) {\\n    throw new Error(\\n      `fixture drain left work behind (stopped: ${report.value.stoppedBecause}, remaining: ${report.value.remaining})`,\\n    );\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction failedEntries(entries: readonly FormReportEntry[], reason: string): FormReportEntry[] {\\n  return entries.filter((entry) => entry.state === \\\"failed\\\" && entry.reason === reason);\\n}\\n\\nexport async function derivedThreadFixture(\\n  store: TempStore,\\n  opts: DerivedThreadOptions = {},\\n): Promise<DerivedThreadFixture> {\\n  const failures = opts.failures ?? true;\\n  const stragglers = opts.stragglers ?? false;\\n\\n  const double = createProviderDouble();\\n  const sdk = createSdk({\\n    provider: double,\\n    mode: \\\"manual\\\",\\n    retry: { budget: 3, backoffBaseMs: 0, backoffCapMs: 0 },\\n    chunkPolicy: FIXTURE_CHUNK_POLICY,\\n  });\\n\\n  const filePath = store.threadPath();\\n  const created = await sdk.threads.newThread({ filePath, registryPath: store.registryPath });\\n  if (!created.ok) throw new Error(`fixture thread creation failed: ${created.error.reason}`);\\n\\n  const turnIds: string[] = [];\\n  const fixture: DerivedThreadFixture = {\\n    filePath,\\n    sdk,\\n    double,\\n    turnIds,\\n    chunks: { chunks: [], members: [] },\\n  };\\n\\n  for (let turn = 1; turn <= TURN_COUNT; turn += 1) {\\n    if (failures && turn === 6) {\\n      // Retryable failures consumed to exhaustion by the head-first drain:\\n      // the first tool_result_summary item of this batch takes all three\\n      // attempts and lands failed with the transient reason class.\\n      double.failKind(\\\"tool_result_summary\\\", 3, {\\n        retryable: true,\\n        reason: TRANSIENT_EXHAUST_REASON,\\n      });\\n    }\\n    if (failures && turn === 7) {\\n      // One non-retryable failure: terminal on the first attempt — the\\n      // permanent reason class, attempts 1.\\n      double.failKind(\\\"tool_result_summary\\\", 1, {\\n        retryable: false,\\n        reason: PERMANENT_FAILURE_REASON,\\n      });\\n    }\\n    const messageIds = await send(sdk, filePath, turnEvents(turn));\\n    // Batch shape is fixed for tool-heavy turns: prompt, thinking, call,\\n    // result, call, result, text, end — index 3 is the first tool result,\\n    // the scripted failures' subject.\\n    const firstToolResultId = messageIds[3];\\n    if (failures && (turn === 6 || turn === 7)) {\\n      if (firstToolResultId === undefined || firstToolResultId === \\\"\\\") {\\n        throw new Error(`fixture invariant: turn ${turn} carries no first tool result message`);\\n      }\\n      if (turn === 6) fixture.failedTransientMessageId = firstToolResultId;\\n      else fixture.failedPermanentMessageId = firstToolResultId;\\n    }\\n    await drain(sdk, filePath);\\n\\n    if (stragglers && turn === 3) {\\n      // A runtime note between turn 3's end and turn 4's prompt: projected\\n      // with turnId = null (the Epic 01 straggler), selection rule 6 / G4.\\n      const noteIds = await send(sdk, filePath, [\\n        validEvent(\\\"runtime_note\\\", {\\n          payload: { text: \\\"harness restarted between turns (fixture straggler)\\\" },\\n        }),\\n      ]);\\n      const noteId = noteIds[0];\\n      if (noteId === undefined || noteId === \\\"\\\") {\\n        throw new Error(\\\"fixture invariant: between-turns straggler did not project\\\");\\n      }\\n      fixture.stragglerBetweenMessageId = noteId;\\n    }\\n    turnIds.push(`t${turn}`);\\n  }\\n\\n  if (stragglers) {\\n    const noteIds = await send(sdk, filePath, [\\n      validEvent(\\\"runtime_note\\\", {\\n        payload: { text: \\\"session closing note after the last turn (fixture straggler)\\\" },\\n      }),\\n    ]);\\n    const noteId = noteIds[0];\\n    if (noteId === undefined || noteId === \\\"\\\") {\\n      throw new Error(\\\"fixture invariant: trailing straggler did not project\\\");\\n    }\\n    fixture.stragglerTrailingMessageId = noteId;\\n    await drain(sdk, filePath);\\n  }\\n\\n  // Shape invariants the chunk policy is pinned for: 12 closed turns in 4\\n  // chunks, the first three closed. A failure here means the deterministic\\n  // substrate moved (provider output or tokenizer), not a flaky test.\\n  fixture.chunks = readChunks(filePath);\\n  if (fixture.chunks.chunks.length !== 4) {\\n    throw new Error(\\n      `fixture invariant: expected 4 chunks, got ${fixture.chunks.chunks.length} — re-pin FIXTURE_CHUNK_POLICY`,\\n    );\\n  }\\n  const closed = fixture.chunks.chunks.filter((chunk) => chunk.status === \\\"closed\\\").length;\\n  if (closed !== 3) {\\n    throw new Error(\\n      `fixture invariant: expected chunks c1–c3 closed, got ${closed} closed — re-pin FIXTURE_CHUNK_POLICY`,\\n    );\\n  }\\n\\n  if (failures) {\\n    // Verify the manufactured states by read-back through the owning report\\n    // surface before handing the fixture to any test (FC-0.3's enforcement\\n    // lives in the tests; this guards the builder's own contract).\\n    const report = await sdk.messages.report({ filePath });\\n    if (!report.ok) throw new Error(`fixture report failed: ${report.error.reason}`);\\n    const transient = failedEntries(report.value, TRANSIENT_EXHAUST_REASON);\\n    const permanent = failedEntries(report.value, PERMANENT_FAILURE_REASON);\\n    if (\\n      transient.length !== 1 ||\\n      transient[0]?.subjectId !== fixture.failedTransientMessageId ||\\n      permanent.length !== 1 ||\\n      permanent[0]?.subjectId !== fixture.failedPermanentMessageId\\n    ) {\\n      throw new Error(\\n        `fixture invariant: expected exactly one transient-failed and one permanent-failed tool_result_summary on the named subjects`,\\n      );\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  return fixture;\\n}\\n\\n// The turnless-straggler variant (FC-0.5, golden G4's substrate): the same\\n// conversation with a runtime note between two turns and one after the last\\n// turn, fully drained, no manufactured failures.\\nexport async function stragglerVariantThread(store: TempStore): Promise<DerivedThreadFixture> {\\n  return derivedThreadFixture(store, { failures: false, stragglers: true });\\n}\\n\\n// The canonical-corruption variant (FC-0.5, Epic 01 fixture pattern): a\\n// short real conversation, drained clean, then damaged below the SDK into\\n// the two-open-turns state no public operation can produce. Canonical\\n// consumers refuse it with state_corruption.\\nexport async function corruptedVariantThread(\\n  store: TempStore,\\n): Promise<{ filePath: string; sdk: Lhc }> {\\n  const double = createProviderDouble();\\n  const sdk = createSdk({ provider: double, mode: \\\"manual\\\" });\\n  const filePath = store.threadPath();\\n  const created = await sdk.threads.newThread({ filePath, registryPath: store.registryPath });\\n  if (!created.ok) throw new Error(`fixture thread creation failed: ${created.error.reason}`);\\n  for (let turn = 1; turn <= 3; turn += 1) {\\n    await send(sdk, filePath, turnEvents(turn));\\n  }\\n  await drain(sdk, filePath);\\n  // Open a turn through real intake, then add a second open row: two open\\n  // turns, the Epic 01 invariant violation.\\n  await send(sdk, filePath, [\\n    validEvent(\\\"user_prompt\\\", { payload: { text: \\\"left open before the damage\\\" } }),\\n  ]);\\n  corruptTwoOpenTurns(filePath);\\n  return { filePath, sdk };\\n}\\n\\n// The blocked state's sacrificial sibling (FC-0.3): a closed turn whose\\n// queued derivation meets real source damage at drain time — the handler\\n// finds two open turns and lands the turn forms blocked through the\\n// production terminal path, never a hand-written row.\\nexport async function blockedSiblingThread(\\n  store: TempStore,\\n): Promise<{ filePath: string; sdk: Lhc; blockedTurnId: string }> {\\n  const double = createProviderDouble();\\n  const sdk = createSdk({ provider: double, mode: \\\"manual\\\" });\\n  const filePath = store.threadPath();\\n  const created = await sdk.threads.newThread({ filePath, registryPath: store.registryPath });\\n  if (!created.ok) throw new Error(`fixture thread creation failed: ${created.error.reason}`);\\n  // Turn 1 closes (its turn_derivation queues); a second turn opens through\\n  // real intake; the corruption writer adds another open row. The drain then\\n  // claims t1's derivation against a record with two open turns.\\n  await send(sdk, filePath, turnEvents(1));\\n  await send(sdk, filePath, [\\n    validEvent(\\\"user_prompt\\\", { payload: { text: \\\"left open before the damage\\\" } }),\\n  ]);\\n  corruptTwoOpenTurns(filePath);\\n  const report = await sdk.work.drain({ filePath });\\n  if (!report.ok) throw new Error(`fixture drain failed: ${report.error.reason}`);\\n  const blocked = report.value.ran.find(\\n    (entry) => entry.kind === \\\"turn_derivation\\\" && entry.disposition === \\\"failed_terminal\\\",\\n  );\\n  if (blocked === undefined) {\\n    throw new Error(\\\"fixture invariant: turn_derivation expected to land terminal on damage\\\");\\n  }\\n  return { filePath, sdk, blockedTurnId: \\\"t1\\\" };\\n}\\n\",\"numLines\":318,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":318}}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/streams/004-implementor.stdout.log:410:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":3,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"input_json_delta\",\"partial_json\":\"\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Read placeholder assertions in existing tests\"}},\"session_id\":\"f006cddb-2184-479e-939b-55dccd3023e3\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"739f3