{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QFZGpVgq7bnAHbvbZiyXKQ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Selection goldens (Epic 03 Story 2, G1–G4)\n2\t\n3\tCommitted expected arrangements for the band-selection walk (tech design\n4\t§Deterministic Algorithms), consumed by `test/view-select-golden.test.ts`.\n5\tEach golden pins the exact arrangement a compact must produce on the Story-0\n6\tfixture (or its straggler variant) under explicit params: subject ids per\n7\tband, form used, compact point, covered_from, and gaps.\n8\t\n9\t**Goldens are immutable once committed.** An implementation that disagrees\n10\twith a golden is wrong until the *design rule* is shown wrong — that takes the\n11\tdeviation process, not a golden edit. The expected values were hand-derived\n12\tfrom the design's rules (rules 1–6, the pinned ≤/newest-first/newest-member\n13\ttie-breakers) against the fixture's deterministic token costs.\n14\t\n15\tRegenerated once under impl-lead ruling\n16\t`02-smart-compact-story-run-001-ruling-013`: the first commit's goldens\n17\tencoded extra-rule selection behavior (smooth-obligate inclusion,\n18\tpartial-chunk retreat, suppressed brief loner); these goldens encode the\n19\tliteral rules.\n20\t\n21\t| File | Case | Rule under test |\n22\t|------|------|-----------------|\n23\t| `g1-proportions.json` | G1 | shares → bands across the full gradient |\n24\t| `g2-edge-inclusion.json` | G2a | entry exactly filling the remainder is included (≤) |\n25\t| `g2-edge-exclusion.json` | G2b | one token under the exact fill → excluded, band stops |\n26\t| `g3-oversized-loner.json` | G3 | oversized entry on an otherwise-empty band represents alone |\n27\t| `g4-turnless-straggler.json` | G4 | rule 6: straggler rides the following turn's band entry; trailing straggler is tail |\n28\t| `boundary-g1-trajectory.json` | Boundary G1 (Story 4) | advance trajectory: over-max trigger, oldest-first flips to target, whole-message floor join, oversized-newest protected alone, never-backward across batches |\n29\t\n30\t## Regeneration (only with a granted deviation)\n31\t\n32\tThe actual arrangement for any params can be printed by running the golden\n33\tsuite with `GOLDEN_DUMP=1`:\n34\t\n35\t```\n36\tGOLDEN_DUMP=1 npx vitest run test/view-select-golden.test.ts\n37\t```\n38\t\n39\tEach case logs its actual `{compactPoint, coveredFrom, arrangement, gaps}`\n40\tJSON; verify the new values against the design rules by hand before replacing\n41\ta file, and record the deviation that made the old golden wrong.\n42\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01JVfJF1EzgZaekjRcpXxggG","session_id":"8f35b3b6-f7a4-4d02-a9f9-b9315f787309","uuid":"d6031d5c-81ab-4086-8fb1-2d5bb4a66baf","timestamp":"2026-06-11T18:23:50.975Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Audit test-plan conformance"}
