e 20):\n```typescript\nimport * as threadView from \"../domains/thread-view/index.js\";\n```\n\nLines 146, 157, 159, 184, 200: All calls are `threadView.<operation>(ref, opts)`, not SDK construction. No `createSdk`, no provider wiring.\n\n**Config fallback** (lines 6-9):\n```\n// No provider is required by any view operation; calling\n// the surface directly (the cli/work.ts report/requeue pattern) keeps that\n// structural: there is no provider to configure on this path at all, and\n// view config falls back to the built-in defaults inside the surface.\n```\n\nThread-view surface defaults to `DEFAULT_VIEW_CONFIG` when no SDK seam is active (thread-view/index.ts lines 71-74).\n\n**Confirmation:** All five commands match grammar. Direct domain calls, no SDK/config wiring. Built-in defaults apply.\n\n---\n\n### Audit 8: Provider Calls, Inference, or Polling in thread-view/**\n\n**Finding: ZERO PROVIDER CALLS, ZERO INFERENCE, ZERO POLLING**\n\n**Search results:**\n- No `provider[` indexing, no `config.provider`, no provider invocations anywhere in `/src/domains/thread-view/`.\n- No `setTimeout`, `sleep`, `drainSettled`, or polling loops.\n- Only `await` calls are to:\n  - `resolveThreadRef()` (resolving file path, not async work).\n  - `messagesDomain.report()` and `turnsDomain.report()` (reading forms state, not inference).\n  - `runSweep()` (requeuing through work-queue owners, not provider).\n\n**Anti-pattern check**: `/src/domains/thread-view/internal/sweep.ts` line explicitly states:\n```\n// No derivation, no provider calls, and no waiting: a requeue returns when\n// queued by the work queue's atomic enqueue, never blocking on the work\n// itself or drainSettled/polling in this module is a contract violation (anti-shim;\n```\n\n**Confirmation:** Thread-view is pure reads and deterministic assembly. No provider, no inference, no blocking. All async calls are structural (file IO, DB reads, intra-domain work registration).\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\n✓ **Audit 1:** No u