ernal/sweep.ts:39-42), matching the tech design's classification-table resolution.\"\n  ],\n  \"architectureFindings\": [\n    \"Module placement matches the tech design exactly: thread-view surface plus the seven named internals (select, render, snapshot, boundary, sweep, profiles, materialize) plus the Story 0 seam, cli/view.ts, shared/view.ts. Migration v6 (src/shared/storage.ts:91-120) matches the design schema verbatim: singleton CHECKs, band CHECK constraint, FK cascade, view_boundary seeded to position 0.\",\n    \"The sanctioned domain cycle (intake-stream → thread-view → messages/turns ← intake-stream) is explicitly annotated in scripts/check-boundaries.mjs, which pins the allowed edge set instead of asserting acyclicity — exactly what the tech design required, not a silent pass.\",\n    \"Flow 4 wiring is as pinned: the advance registers FIRST on ctx.onCommit (src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:150-158), throw-isolated so a failing advance cannot eat the queue poke or reach intake's caller; it runs in both host modes; budgets resolve through the per-instance seam (InstanceSeam.view) with below-SDK fallback to defaults; never-backward is enforced in the UPDATE's WHERE clause as well as the decision (src/domains/thread-view/internal/boundary.ts:150-152); the advance's zone sum and status's zone sum share one query (boundary.ts:29-42), making AC-4.9's 'visible in status' structural.\",\n    \"Must-not-own lines hold throughout: the sweep touches only owners' report/requeue surfaces; status's derivation counts go through reports, never direct derived_form reads; materialize renders pull output only; the boundary reads stored token estimates only. Story 1's verifier-driven thread-touch suppression (shared/context.ts:117-130) makes pull/status reads-only structural in both host modes.\",\n    \"Minor deviation (behavior-neutral): the tech design's module matrix lists cli/view.ts as depending on 'sdk' and Flow 4 says 'the CLI builds a real SDK (cli/work.ts pattern)'; in code, cli/view.ts and the CLI intake command call domain surfaces directly (src/cli/view.ts:20, src/cli/index.ts:270), taking the design's own sanctioned below-SDK default-config path. Observable behavior is identical — no CLI view-config channel exists in this epic — and the process-suite architecture-risk test proves CLI intake advances the boundary end-to-end. Doc-vs-mechanism drift only.\",\n    \"Observation: compact stamps created_at from new Date() at the surface (src/domains/thread-view/index.ts:403) rather than the SDK's injected clock. Consistent with the design ('created_at: clock at compact') and harmless to determinism — view_id derives from maxEventOrder and materialize's generated fields derive from the stored value — and the same shape as Story 0's accepted-risk ruling on the migration seed timestamp.\",\n    \"Observation: openThreadDatabase migrates schema on open (inherited Epic 01/02 convention, src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts:191), so the first pull/status on a pre-v6 thread file performs the one-time v6 migration write before reading. AC-1.1's 'no writes' otherwise holds; this is the established storage convention, not an Epic 03 regression.\"\n  ],\n  \"epicCoverageAssessment\": [\n    \"38/38 ACs and 27/27 TCs are implemented and mapped to passing tests; verified per-TC with file:line across view-fixture, view-pull, view-compact, view-select-golden, view-sweep, view-boundary, view-render-targets, and cli-process-view. Critical TCs confirmed individually: TC-2.4 crash injection, TC-2.7 corruption refusal with derived-damage control leg, TC-3.2 no-double-requeue, TC-4.3 monster-turn floor, TC-4.6 advance-failure injection with poke survival, TC-5.5 PI format conformance.\",\n    \"All eight architecture-risk tests from the test plan exist: zero-provider across all five ops, selection goldens G1–G4 and the boundary trajectory as committed exact-value JSON in test/goldens/ compared via toEqual, advance/poke seam isolation in both directions, restart-serves-snapshot via real-file reopen, coverage-edge accounting, CLI parity for all five commands, and CLI-intake-advances-boundary at the process boundary.\",\n    \"Fixture fidelity holds: derived-form states (ready, failed-transient, failed-permanent, blocked, pending) are manufactured through real intake + drain against the scripted deterministic provider with no hand-written derived_form or work_item rows; the PI session fixture derives from a real PI session with committed provenance (PI coding agent 0.79.1, session format version 3, test/fixtures/pi-session-structure.provenance.md).\",\n    \"One residual semantic edge, human-sanctioned, recorded as non-blocking finding E03-R1-001: under the literal selection rules a chunk straddling the smooth-band budget cut (or trailing closed-unchunked turns falling off the smooth share) can leave those turns unrepresented between the smooth and detailed bands without a gap entry, while covered_from spans them. Ruling 013 explicitly rejected the implementor's compensating interpretations and required the literal rules; the omission is transient (the next compact after chunking catches up heals it) and the record retains everything.\"\n  ],\n  \"productionPathFindings\": [\n    \"No fake adapters, shims, or placeholders on any production path: no TODO/FIXME/not-implemented markers in src/; all Red-phase structured-result stubs are replaced by real implementations.\",\n    \"The deterministic provider (src/providers/deterministic.ts) is a test double living in production source by design, selectable only by explicit name through the registry — no default, no silent fallback (registry.ts: provider_not_configured on absence). No Epic 03 code path references providers at all, and the process suite strips LHC_PROVIDER to prove it structurally.\",\n    \"The Story 0 injection seam (src/domains/thread-view/internal/seam.ts) fires no-ops in production unless a hook is installed via the test/fixtures-only deep import — identical to Epic 02's intake-seam pattern; setViewInjectionHook is not exported from the public index, and the SDK's threadView surface carries exactly the five operations with no public boundary-advance.\",\n    \"thread-view contains no provider calls, no inference, and no polling or waiting (no setTimeout/sleep/drainSettled); sweep requeues return at queue-row write; pull/status/materialize run under thread-touch suppression so they can never schedule background drains.\",\n    \"materialize writes only the caller-supplied output file; every generated field derives from view/record metadata — header cwd from the thread file's directory rather than the writing process's cwd, no Date.now() anywhere on the path — making byte-identical repeats structural (AC-5.2).\"\n  ],\n  \"blockingFindings\": [],\n  \"nonBlockingFindings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E03-R1-001\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"title\": \"Literal selection rules can leave straddling turns unrepresented between smooth and detailed bands\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Chunk candidacy requires the chunk's newest live member to be strictly older than the oldest included smooth turn (src/domains/thread-view/internal/select.ts:471-485) while the smooth fill stops at its budget (select.ts:430-460). Turns in the smooth remainder that belong to a straddling chunk — or closed-but-unchunked turns that fall off the smooth share — get no band entry and no gap record, while covered_from (min over included entries' startOrder) can span them, so the omission is invisible in the receipt. Ruling 013 (artifacts/02-smart-compact/story-lead/001-ruling-response-001.json) explicitly rejected the compensating 'smooth-obligate'/'partial-chunk retreat' interpretations and required the literal rules, so this is human-sanctioned behavior; it is transient (the next compact after chunking catches up re-covers the span) and the record retains everything (AC-2.9), but it sits in tension with the epic's 'never silently omits a span' language and should be on record for the next design round.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\n        \"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/select.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"AC-2.4\", \"AC-2.5\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"human-ruling\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E03-R1-002\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"CLI wires view commands and intake to domain surfaces directly rather than building an SDK as the tech design sketch states\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Tech design Flow 4 says 'The CLI builds a real SDK (cli/work.ts pattern)' and the module matrix lists cli/view.ts depending on 'sdk', but cli/view.ts imports the thread-view domain directly (src/cli/view.ts:20) and CLI intake calls intakeStream.messageEvents directly (src/cli/index.ts:270), relying on the design's own sanctioned below-SDK default-config fallback (thread-view/index.ts:71-75). Behavior is identical — no CLI view-config channel exists this epic, the operations are provider-free, and the process-suite leg proves CLI intake advances the boundary — so this is documentation-vs-mechanism drift, resolvable by a one-line tech-design correction or by wiring the CLI through createSdk later.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\n        \"packages/lhc/src/cli/view.ts\",\n        \"packages/lhc/src/cli/index.ts\",\n        \"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md\"\n      ],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"AC-4.9\", \"AC-5.5\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"quick-fix\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E03-R1-003\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"Compact stamps created_at from the real clock rather than the SDK's injected clock\",\n      \"evidence\": \"src/domains/thread-view/index.ts:403 uses new Date().toISOString() for the view's created_at while the SDK config carries an injectable clock used elsewhere (boundary advance uses ctx.clock). Determinism is unaffected — view_id derives from maxEventOrder and materialize's generated fields derive from the stored created_at — and the team dispositioned the same shape as accepted-risk for the migration seed (Story 0 ruling). Threading the instance clock through compact would close the small consistency gap.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\n        \"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/index.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"AC-2.6\", \"AC-5.2\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"quick-fix\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E03-R1-004\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"First pull/status on a pre-v6 thread file performs the one-time schema migration write\",\n      \"evidence\": \"openThreadDatabase brings a thread file to the current schema version on every open (src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts:188-204), so a pull or status against a file recorded under Epic 02's v5 performs the v6 migration before reading — a write on what AC-1.1 calls a no-writes path. This is the inherited Epic 01/02 migration-on-open convention, necessary for the view_boundary singleton to exist, idempotent, and one-time; recorded so the convention's interaction with the reads-only contract is an explicit acceptance rather than an unnoticed one.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\n        \"packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"AC-1.1\", \"AC-2.8\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"human-ruling\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"unresolvedItems\": [\n    \"Tech design open question Q1 (band messages split per-band vs one block) remains open by design; settle during PI extension integration (Epic 05/PRD-2).\",\n    \"Deferred items stand as recorded in the tech design: non-PI render formats; sweep cross-invocation requeue cap (revisit if repeated transient-failure loops appear in use); aging banded history out of the thread file (covered_from is the seam).\"\n  ],\n  \"gateResult\": \"pass\"\n}\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"8f35b3b6-f7a4-4d02-a9f9-b9315f787309","total_cost_usd":8.3236414,"usage":{"input_tokens":5700,"cache_creation_input_tokens":157547,"cache_read_input_tokens":2926898,"output_tokens":34919,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":157547,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5229,"cache_read_input_tokens":167927,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5442,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5442},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":1674,"outputTokens":19364,"cacheReadInputTokens":2277219,"cacheCreationInputTokens":93310,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.44285339999999995,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":5700,"outputTokens":34919,"cacheReadInputTokens":2926898,"cacheCreationInputTokens":157547,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":7.880787999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"94c207a8-936e-4df9-99ca-37dabc02f1c8"}
